\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Kansas  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Message; Democracy is working its will on the issue, as the Supreme Court said.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par 16:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The press corps is making a big deal of the defeat of the Kansas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum on Tuesday, and for once they're right. The 20-or-so point rout of the effort to strip \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections from the state constitution is a message to Republicans and the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement that a total ban isn't popular even in a right-leaning state.\par \par \uc2 The defeated amendment wouldn't have imposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. It would have overruled a 2019 ruling by the state Supreme Court that found a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Kansas constitution\u8212\'20\'14a case of judicial law-writing in our view. But voters were clearly wary of how far the Kansas Legislature would go if allowed to impose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. Nearby Oklahoma and Missouri now have near-total bans, and Kansans have been paying attention.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  forces can't find much of a silver-lining in the vote. Their timing in the wake of the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 's decision overturning Roe v. Wade was obviously poor as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists were motivated. Voter turnout was unusually heavy for a primary election date. The referendum did far worse than supporters expected even in conservative counties in the state.\par \par \uc2 One message is that voters are wary of extremes on either side of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue. A majority of the public supports a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least up to several weeks of pregnancy. This is disappointing to those who believe life begins at conception, but it means the pro-life side has persuading to do if it wants to win the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate.\par \par \uc2 That's the burden of democracy, which is what the Supreme Court allowed to return on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overturning Roe. Urging Congress to pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, as some on the right want, looks like a certain loser\u8212\'20\'14in addition to likely being unconstitutional. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an issue for the states to decide.\par \par \uc2 Democrats and the press are touting the Kansas vote as a sign that progressive voters are motivated to turn out this year and might save their control of Congress despite inflation, rising crime and other national ills. That's far from certain, but Republicans would be wise to take the warning seriously.\par \par \uc2 The Kansas result will inspire Democrats across the country to make the midterms a referendum on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They may overreach with their own attempts to reinstate Roe nationally. But Republicans will need a response on the issue that reassures voters like those in Kansas who have a more nuanced view of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  than either side has been offering since Roe took the issue out of the hands of voters in 1973.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court didn't settle the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  question. It rightly returned it to the voters, and the Kansas referendum is merely the start of a long national debate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-kansas-abortion-message-referendum-constitution-supreme-court-11659536655"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Kansas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Message}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220803ei83003xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
