\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Michigan Court Ruling Allows Potential Prosecutions for  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; The decision comes weeks after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overruled Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 605 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 August 2022\par 21:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A Michigan appeals court opened the door Monday for county prosecutors to enforce the state's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-governor-abortion-rights-groups-challenge-dormant-state-abortion-ban-11649345756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dormant 1931 ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , a decision that could curb the procedure in the state for the first time since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended the U.S. constitutional right  }}}\uc2  to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ruling, which turned on issues of legal procedure instead of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, reversed a trial court ruling that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-judge-suspends-enforcement-of-pre-roe-abortion-ban-11652819032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily blocked enforcement  }}}\uc2  of the ban by local prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 The appeals court said the judge who issued a preliminary injunction against enforcement didn't have jurisdiction over local county attorneys and couldn't order them not to use the 1931 law, which bans abortions at any state of pregnancy unless the life of the mother is at risk.\par \par \uc2 David Kallman, an attorney for prosecutors Jerard Jarzynka of Jackson County and Christopher Becker of Kent County, who challenged the injunction, said his clients will begin enforcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban immediately. Mr. Kallman, senior legal counsel for the Great Lakes Justice Center, added that the prosecutors' offices don't currently have any pending cases related to providers breaking the 1931 law.\par \par \uc2 "If I were a doctor or a hospital or a medical clinic providing abortions today, I would stop immediately unless it's to save the life of a mother. Otherwise they're risking felony charges," he said.\par \par \uc2 The ruling comes weeks after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  's June 24 decision that overruled Roe v. Wade and eliminated constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood of Michigan said it plans to continue providing abortions in the state for now, arguing Monday's ruling doesn't take effect for at least 21 days, during the group's window to appeal to the state's Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Paula Thornton Greear, president and chief executive of Planned Parenthood of Michigan, said the organization is still reviewing the court's order and its legal options. "We're committed to protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Michigan," she said.\par \par \uc2 Michigan is one of eight states that had laws banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that predated Roe. Those laws have been subject to legal challenges in a number of those states, including Arizona and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Michigan Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-governor-abortion-rights-groups-challenge-dormant-state-abortion-ban-11649345756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed separate challenges  }}}\uc2 to the state's 1931 law, seeking to get the Michigan Supreme Court to recognize a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state's constitution. Ms. Whitmer filed a new motion Monday that seeks to temporarily block enforcement of the law, saying Michigan \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers "presently are forced to choose whether to continue offering healthcare services to women in this state or potentially face criminal prosecution, creating irreparable harm for women who need healthcare now."\par \par \uc2 Michigan voters also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigans-abortion-tensions-reflect-uncertain-future-in-battleground-states-11651834802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will likely vote in November  }}}\uc2  on whether to add explicit protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the state's constitution, which would likely make the 1931 law invalid. \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2  , the organization behind the effort, launched a ballot initiative in January ahead of the Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 The organization said it submitted more than 750,000 signatures, far more than required, to the state's Bureau of Elections office to place a proposed constitutional amendment on the ballot. The signatures will need to be validated and the proposal must be approved by the Board of State Canvassers before Sept. 9, according to the Michigan Department of State.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Calfas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-court-ruling-allows-potential-prosecutions-for-abortion-11659384864"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan Court Ruling Allows Potential Prosecutions for \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220801ei81004h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
