\par\par \uc2 Commentary (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Planned Parenthood's Politicized Diagnosis; The group's website used to tell the truth about treatment for ectopic pregnancies.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin Morrow Hawley \par \uc2 820 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 August 2022\par 16:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade in June, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates have been insisting that pro-life laws threaten women's health. Yet Planned Parenthood's own website has already debunked many of these arguments, explaining that treatments for medical conditions such as ectopic pregnancies and miscarriages aren't abortions.\par \par \uc2 Then Planned Parenthood changed its website in mid-July, promoting a false narrative that proves many in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry care more about advancing a political agenda than about women's health.\par \par \uc2 In July \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates argued at a congressional hearing, in which I testified on the other side, that laws protecting the unborn threaten women's health by preventing physicians from offering common pregnancy treatments. Rep. Ayanna Pressley (D., Mass.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pressley.house.gov/media/press-releases/pressley-hearing-misinformation-about-abortion-puts-lives-further-risk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2  that the treatment for an ectopic pregnancy was the same thing as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Witnesses said that women would be unable to access lifesaving medical treatment in cases of emergency.\par \par \uc2 Yet Planned Parenthood's own website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://web.archive.org/web/20220714210739/https:/www.plannedparenthood.org/learn/pregnancy/ectopic-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 used to say}}}\uc2 , "Treating an ectopic pregnancy isn't the same thing as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." After \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates insisted that post-Roe pro-life laws might interfere with treatments for ectopic pregnancy, Planned Parenthood altered its medical definition to fit the narrative. Today, its website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthood.org/learn/pregnancy/ectopic-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2 : "The medical procedures for terminating a pregnancy in the uterus are usually different from medical procedures for terminating an ectopic pregnancy."\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood was right the first time. Legally, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the intentional termination of a human life. The treatment for an ectopic pregnancy isn't an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because its purpose isn't to end a human life. Similarly, every state provides that lifesaving treatment for a pregnant woman isn't an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . When these tragic circumstances occur, a physician does everything possible to ensure the survival of both the mother and the baby.\par \par \uc2 The argument that physicians might refuse lifesaving medical care due to fear of prosecution is a red herring. Physicians who provide emergency medical care to a pregnant woman, or who treat an ectopic pregnancy or miscarriage, don't violate any state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. Many states, such as Mississippi, leave the question of lifesaving necessity up to the physician's good-faith judgment. Further, while only a fraction of OB-GYNs perform abortions, procedures to treat ectopic pregnancy or miscarriage, while tragic, are routine. Doctors can distinguish between tragic circumstances and intentionally ending a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood's reversal is consistent with other efforts to suppress inconvenient truths by adapting medical terminology to advance political purposes. The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 , an organization of medical specialists who bring unborn children into the world, has long denied that those children have a right to life. \uc2 ACOG\uc2 's position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is extreme. It is against any legislative restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In March 2022, \uc2 ACOG\uc2  released its Guide to Language and \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the guide, \uc2 ACOG\uc2  recommends avoiding the word "baby" or the phrase "unborn child." \uc2 ACOG\uc2  also insists on supporting partial-birth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rejecting the word "dismemberment" in favor of "dilation and evacuation procedures" (those terms mean the same thing\u8212\'20\'14the tearing apart of a baby during an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedure). The organization even refuses to use the word "woman" in its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. Finally, given the recent passage of state laws protecting unborn children after a detectable heartbeat, \uc2 ACOG\uc2  modified its guide to advise OB-GYNs against referring to a "heartbeat." \uc2 ACOG\uc2  recommends that doctors say "fetal cardiac activity."\par \par \uc2 Practicing obstetricians are unlikely to take \uc2 ACOG\uc2 's language guide seriously. Imagine a physician telling the excited parents, "Look, here's your embryo's fetal cardiac activity!" That would be terrible bedside manner, but it is also terrible science. Basic biology confirms that human life begins at conception. Embryologists agree that at fertilization a human being emerges as a genetically distinct member of the species Homo sapiens, needing only a proper environment to flourish. \uc2 ACOG\uc2 's wordsmithing is an attempt to avoid humanizing unborn children.\par \par \uc2 Pregnant women know that the presence of a heartbeat is significant. It is an assurance that the most vulnerable part of pregnancy has passed. Once a child's heartbeat is detected, the risk of miscarriage drops dramatically, to less than 2% after eight weeks.\par \par \uc2 ACOG\uc2 's guidance is another linguistic about-face. In 2017 it opposed a House bill that, in \uc2 ACOG\uc2 's words, banned "\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the detection of the fetal heartbeat, which occurs as early as six weeks gestation." The new language is all about politics.\par \par \uc2 That Planned Parenthood and \uc2 ACOG\uc2  are willing to modify medical terms shows they are more committed to their politics than to providing women with accurate medical information or good healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Morrow Hawley is a senior counsel for \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  and an associate professor of law at Regent University.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/planned-parenthoods-politicized-diagnosis-abortion-miscarriage-false-narrative-agenda-unborn-pregnancy-treatments-11659362911"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood's Politicized Diagnosis}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220801ei81002mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
