\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Judicial Elections Draw Attention Amid Battles Over  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 , Voting Rules; Top courts in battleground states are in play on November ballots\b0\par\par\uc2 By Deanna Paul \par \uc2 1,006 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 July 2022\par 15:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judicial elections are poised to be hotly contested in several battleground states in November, as politically charged issues including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and voting regulations bring new attention to top courts across the U.S.\par \par \uc2 These down-ballot races often don't involve household names but could prove pivotal in states such as Michigan, North Carolina and Ohio, whose state supreme courts are closely divided on ideological or political lines. In total, more than 80 state supreme court seats are on the ballot, along with far more races for lower courts. Judicial candidates are before voters in more than 30 states.\par \par \uc2 Some races have taken on a new importance since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 's ruling in June that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-judges-are-in-spotlight-after-supreme-court-overrules-roe-v-wade-11656444559"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended constitutional protection for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . The decision has redirected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  litigation to state courts, which now could determine the fate of restrictions or protections for the procedure. State judges in recent years also have been the arbiters on an array of other high-stakes issues, including Covid-19 regulations and challenges to election results.\par \par \uc2 "Most people have never thought about these courts before," said Douglas Keith, counsel at the Brennan Center for Justice at NYU Law School. "This is an awakening. These courts have the final word on a lot of key questions."\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, for instance, Democrats currently enjoy a 4-3 majority on the state Supreme Court, after gains in the 2020 election. Two justices, one Democrat and one Republican, are running for re-election in November.\par \par \uc2 The races in Michigan come after the state's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-governor-abortion-rights-groups-challenge-dormant-state-abortion-ban-11649345756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic governor and \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -rights groups brought cases }}}\uc2  urging the state's high court to declare a restrictive 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law unconstitutional. The Michigan court also has been called upon to referee election issues in a state that has been crucial to both parties' political success on a national level.\par \par \uc2 Voting cases loom over several races.\par \par \uc2 The North Carolina Supreme Court in February {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/north-carolinas-supreme-court-blocks-gop-redistricting-maps-11644023181"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 invalidated the state's congressional map }}}\uc2 , drawn by the Republican-led legislature, as an unlawful partisan gerrymander, on a 4-3 vote with Democratic justices in the majority. Two of the seats held by Democrats are on the ballot in November. The GOP made inroads on the court in 2020 when its candidate won a razor-thin contest against a Democrat who was serving as chief justice.\par \par \uc2 Ohio's Supreme Court also has issued a string of 4-3 rulings this year that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ohio-supreme-court-strikes-down-new-congressional-map-as-favoring-gop-11642195869"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected GOP-drawn maps there }}}\uc2 , with the court's retiring Republican chief justice and three Democrats in the majority. The chief justice's seat, and two others held by Republicans, are in front of voters this year. The contests also mark the first time the races are partisan contests in which the candidates' political affiliations will appear on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 Both parties have taken notice of these contests at the national level.\par \par \uc2 The Republican State Leadership Committee, a national organization focused on electing Republicans to state-level offices, has pledged record investments in this year's state supreme court races, targeting high-impact states with coming battles over redistricting.\par \par \uc2 "Defending democracy and keeping the redistricting process in the hands of the people in 2030 will require historic investments in state Supreme Court races in 2022," said RSLC President Dee Duncan earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The group spent more than $5 million on judicial races in five states during the 2019-2020 election cycle.\par \par \uc2 The National Democratic Redistricting Committee, whose board chairman is former Attorney General \uc2 Eric Holder\uc2 , lists supreme-court races in Michigan and Ohio among the contests the group is targeting.\par \par \uc2 "Democracy is on the ballot," said Garrett Arwa, NDRC interim executive director. "Part of that democracy is fighting Republican efforts to make courts less independent and more partisan. It's important to have state courts as neutral arbiters."\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you view the role of your state's supreme court? Has that changed over recent years? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Most states allow their voters to have a say on judges. That stands in contrast to the process for filling the federal judiciary, where judges are nominated by the president and confirmed by the Senate. The nature of state contests, however, varies widely. Some states make their judicial races nonpartisan, while others hold partisan elections where a judicial candidate's political affiliation is on the ballot. Still other states hold retention elections where judges, who are initially appointed to their positions, appear before voters who decide whether to keep them on the bench. The length of terms for supreme-court justices varies by state, but it is often between six and 10 years.\par \par \uc2 States have long grappled with the best method for selecting judges. Supporters of judicial elections say the contests promote accountability, while critics say political contests, particularly ones fueled by campaign donations, can undermine the belief that courts are impartial.\par \par \uc2 Judicial elections were a 19th century response to concerns that the political appointment of judges promoted cronyism and corruption at the expense of transparency, said Jed Shugerman, a professor at Fordham Law School and author of "The People's Courts," a book about judicial elections. But such races, he said, in some cases have become vehicles for large spending by interest groups.\par \par \uc2 The biggest judicial races in recent years have attracted millions of dollars in campaign spending. In the 2019-2020 election cycle, state supreme court races generated $97 million in spending, more money than in any previous cycle, according to the Brennan Center. Races in Illinois alone totaled nearly $19 million, the group found.\par \par \uc2 The state again could be home to some of this year's most expensive judicial contests. A pair of races there this November could determine control of the state's high court, which currently has a Democratic majority.\par \par \uc2 Write to Deanna Paul at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:deanna.paul@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deanna.paul@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/judicial-elections-draw-attention-amid-battles-over-abortion-voting-rules-11659194852"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judicial Elections Draw Attention Amid Battles Over \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 , Voting Rules  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220730ei7u001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
