\par \par \uc2 Voters in the Kansas primary election, where early voting is under way, will decide whether to amend the state's constitution to say it doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . PHOTO: Joe Barrett/The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 OLATHE, Kan.\u8212\'20\'14A statewide referendum on the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Kansas is shaping up as the first major political test on the issue since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 On Aug. 2, Kansas voters will decide whether to amend the state's constitution to explicitly say that it doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The referendum, planned for months, comes after the high court's June 24 decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization ended the federal constitutional right to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 A normally sleepy August primary is now the subject of an intense get-out-the-vote effort, with groups on both sides spending millions sending out glossy mailers and organizing volunteers to knock on doors. Television ads paid for by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents show crying babies and urge Kansans to protect their state from becoming a haven for out-of-state women seeking to end their pregnancies. Highways are lined with electronic billboards sponsored by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters featuring an image of Rosie the Riveter and urging voters to trust women.\par \par \uc2 "It's like if you were having a bonfire in your backyard and then poured a bunch of lighter fluid on it," said Fred Sherman, election commissioner for Johnson County, the state's largest by population, just south of Kansas City. His office is predicting a 67% turnout locally, compared with around 20% to 30% in typical primaries from recent years.\par \par \uc2 The Kansas referendum is being closely watched by national groups on both sides ahead of other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -related ballot referendums }}}\uc2  in the fall. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
