\par \par \uc2 Signs being assembled at the Shawnee, Kan., headquarters of the Value Them Both Coalition, which opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and supports the constitutional amendment eliminating state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections. PHOTO: Joe Barrett/The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 This year alone, some half-dozen states, including Michigan, California and Kentucky, all are likely to have measures on the ballot in November that propose either to weaken or enhance protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Four states\u8212\'20\'14Alabama, Louisiana, Tennessee and West Virginia\u8212\'20\'14all adopted amendments before the Dobbs decision saying their state constitutions don't protect the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . No state has yet adopted a constitutional amendment that enshrines protections for the procedure. California, Vermont and Michigan could be the first to do so, with voters in those states expected to consider such proposals in November.\par \par \uc2 The Kansas race is shaping up to be a tight one. In a state in which registered Republicans outnumber Democrats, a poll released July 19 by Co/efficient, a data-analytics firm based in Kansas City, Mo., found that 47% of likely primary-election voters planned to vote for the amendment, while 43% said they planned to vote against it.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think state constitutions might offer an effective way to protect the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Bob Beatty, a political-science professor at Washburn University in Topeka, said it would be noteworthy if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters even come close to defeating the amendment in a conservative-leaning state like Kansas. "Nationally, people would look at it and say, 'Wow, if it's sort of close in Kansas, the overturning of Roe v. Wade has certainly had an impact,'" he said.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led legislature voted last year to put the amendment on the August primary ballot. In Kansas, Republicans turn out for primary elections at roughly twice the rate of Democrats. The state also has a sizable number of unaffiliated voters who could influence the outcome.\par \par \uc2 The proposed amendment came in response to a 2019 decision by the Kansas Supreme Court that said the state's constitution protects the right of personal autonomy, including the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The amendment wouldn't outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it would clear the way for the legislature to pass more restrictions. Kansas Gov. \uc2 Laura Kelly\uc2 , a Democrat, as well as the state Supreme Court's ruling, have stymied Republicans from enacting tougher \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions like many of Kansas' neighbors, including Oklahoma, Texas and Missouri. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
