\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 California Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  Signs Bill Allowing Citizens to Sue Gun Makers; New law modeled after Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law uses private lawsuits to enforce California gun laws\b0\par\par\uc2 By Christine Mai-Duc \par \uc2 1,075 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 July 2022\par 20:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 California Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  signed a bill into law Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/californias-gavin-newsom-proposes-letting-citizens-sue-gun-makers-11639281730"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowing private citizens to sue the gun industry  }}}\uc2  to enforce the state's ban on certain weapons.\par \par \uc2 The legislation is modeled after a recent law in Texas that allows individuals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to sue \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinics  }}}\uc2  or anyone who "aids and abets" another person in obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Newsom, a Democrat, signed the bill at Santa Monica College, where a 2013 shooting rampage left five people dead in addition to the 23-year-old gunman. The assailant in that shooting used a homemade, unserialized assault rifle he assembled using parts.\par \par \uc2 "You cannot sell, you cannot manufacture, you cannot transfer these illegal weapons of war and mass destruction in the state of California. And if you do, there are 40 million people that can collect $10,000 from you and attorney fees for engaging in that illegal activity," Mr. Newsom told reporters shortly before signing the bill.\par \par \uc2 He also repeated a critique of the national Democratic Party, which he has said needs to "wake up" and be more vocal about the weakening of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and gun control laws. "The Supreme Court has put this responsibility squarely on the doorstep of governors now and legislative leaders\u8230\'20\'26We have to meet this moment and we can't do it with the passivity that we've seen in the past," Mr. Newsom said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Newsom has sought to position himself as a leader in the fight between red states and blue states over issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gun control and the government response to the pandemic. The bill signing ceremony Friday coincided with the launch of an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom/status/1550492948269129728"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ad push by Mr. Newsom's re-election campaign  }}}\uc2  in Texas newspapers. The full-page ads, placed in newspapers across the state Friday, use excerpts from a speech by Texas Gov. Greg Abbott to contrast his views with those of Mr. Newsom on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gun violence.\par \par \uc2 On the Fourth of July, Mr. Newsom's campaign launched TV ads in Florida that featured him criticizing state leaders there and encouraging Floridians to "join us in California, where we still believe in freedom." The unorthodox campaign strategy has caused many to speculate that Mr. Newsom is seeking to raise his national profile in preparation for a potential future presidential run, with Mr. Abbott and Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  as prospective opponents. Mr. Newsom again said Friday that he has "subzero" interest in running for the nation's highest office and joked that he can say it in five languages now.\par \par \uc2 The measure he signed Friday is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/california-gun-measures-let-citizens-sue-to-enforce-regulations-11657640654"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the second of two new laws  }}}\uc2  Mr. Newsom has backed that will allow individuals to sue those who make, distribute, sell or transport assault-style rifles, unserialized, homemade ghost guns and some .50-caliber rifles that are banned in California. The new law also allows suits against manufacturers and distributors of guns that are sold to anyone under the age of 21, the minimum legal age to purchase a firearm in the state.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law that California used as a model, known as the Texas Heartbeat Act, took effect last year and empowers private citizens to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and others to help enforce the law, which bans abortions past six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Texas officials had argued that the use of a private right of action to enforce its ban didn't constitute government action and therefore didn't violate the precedent set by the Supreme Court's Roe v. Wade decision. The Supreme Court accepted that reasoning and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rules-abortion-clinics-can-challenge-texas-abortion-law-11639149404"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed the Texas law to stand  }}}\uc2  in December before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  last month, eliminating the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During the Texas case, the Firearms Policy Coalition, a pro-gun group, warned in legal briefs that a similar approach could be taken by policy makers looking to further restrict weapons. Mr. Newsom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/californias-gavin-newsom-proposes-letting-citizens-sue-gun-makers-11639281730"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 floated the idea  }}}\uc2  of copying the Texas law structure late last year.\par \par \uc2 "I don't like the Texas decision. I'm not happy with it," said California state Sen. \uc2 Bob Hertzberg\uc2  , who worked with Mr. Newsom's administration to introduce the bill. "But if Texas is going to use this legal framework to essentially outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then we in California can use it to save lives and take assault weapons off the street."\par \par \uc2 Under the new California law, which will take effect Jan. 1, plaintiffs who sue gun makers and sellers to enforce state gun laws can recover a minimum of $10,000 per weapon found in violation plus attorney's fees.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think individuals should be able to sue gun manufacturers in states where their products are banned? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 It is the latest of several attempts by state lawmakers to counter a 2005 federal law that gives gun manufacturers immunity from most civil suits pertaining to negligence and product liability. After years of gun-policy gridlock, they argue, it is time to hit weapons manufacturers in their pocketbooks.\par \par \uc2 Last year, New York passed a law that allows individuals to sue the gun industry for creating a "public nuisance" and endangering public safety. A federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/judge-rejects-challenge-to-new-york-law-allowing-lawsuits-against-gun-industry-11653517712"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed a challenge to that law  }}}\uc2  earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Hertzberg, a Democrat, said he and others are hopeful the law will have a chilling effect on gun distributors and sellers and added that policy makers are looking for novel approaches to curbing gun violence.\par \par \uc2 "We have people dying and kids getting killed in schools. Is it not worth trying?" he said.\par \par \uc2 Gun-rights activists have vowed to challenge this and other gun laws Mr. Newsom recently signed, including a measure that restricts firearms marketing to minors and another that allows local prosecutors and the state attorney general to sue gun companies when they violate state laws and their products cause harm.\par \par \uc2 "He is trying to essentially put a system together where it's death by a thousand cuts\u8230\'20\'26to bleed the gun industry and gun owners to death financially," said Chuck Michel, president of the California Rifle and Pistol Association. Mr. Michel said a legal challenge to the newest law could come within weeks.\par \par \uc2 Write to Christine Mai-Duc at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:christine.maiduc@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 christine.maiduc@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/california-gov-gavin-newsom-to-sign-bill-allowing-citizens-to-sue-gun-makers-11658498491"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California Gov. Gavin Newsom Signs Bill Allowing Citizens to Sue Gun Makers  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220722ei7m00335\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
