\par\par \uc2 Commentary (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Biden's  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Politics Will Undermine America's World Standing\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jakub Grygiel and Rebeccah Heinrichs \par \uc2 840 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 July 2022\par 19:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 It isn't surprising that Biden administration officials strongly disagree with the Supreme Court's decision that overturned Roe v. Wade. But it's shocking that they've denounced it for foreign audiences. By trying to recast the U.S. as the world's pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  power, officials will weaken the legitimacy of U.S. foreign policy and undermine America's standing in the world.\par \par \uc2 America's ambassador to the United Nations, \uc2 Linda Thomas-Greenfield\uc2 , issued a statement calling Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization "a cruel, dark and dangerous decision" and asserting: "I have traveled the globe advocating for women's rights. Now, this decision renders my own country an outlier among developed nations in the world." Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  insisted that "the State Department will remain fully committed to helping provide access to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services and advancing \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the world."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has played a role in foreign policy since 1973, the year the court decided Roe and Congress passed the Helms Amendment, which prohibits federal funds for abortions abroad. President Reagan instituted the "Mexico City Policy," which required nongovernmental organizations to agree, as a condition of federal funding, that they wouldn't promote \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a method of family planning in other countries. Every subsequent Democratic president has reversed the policy, and every Republican has reinstated it.\par \par \uc2 This seesaw policy is a consequence of partisan polarization in the wake of Roe. But most polling shows that upward of 60% of Americans support restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that were legally impossible under Roe, especially during the second trimester of pregnancy. Dobbs gives these voters a say in the matter by returning it to the states.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is using national-security institutions as agents of an extreme pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  view. That will erode Americans's trust in their own government\u8212\'20\'14and, in turn, its standing in the world. It will make it harder to rally broad American support on other matters vital to national survival. Officials who urge Americans to support expensive aid or weapons packages to allies, or actions to deter Chinese and Russian abusers of human rights, shouldn't be surprised when Americans who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  respond with cool indifference.\par \par \uc2 A foreign policy pushing for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  abroad is also a strategic blunder with long-term consequences. Many countries in Africa, Asia and Latin America have strict limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and even most of the free world is closer to Dobbs than to Roe.\par \par \uc2 Some Western politicians, such as French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , and the \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  have joined Mr. Biden in denouncing Dobbs. But their statements reflect more the global solidarity of pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politicians than diplomatic prudence or even their own nations' laws and practices.\par \par \uc2 The laws of most European countries would have been deemed unconstitutional under Roe. According to international \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy organizations, only Iceland, Sweden, the Netherlands and the U.K. have widely available \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on request throughout gestation. France and Germany require health justifications or other tragic but rare events such as rape or incest for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  beyond the first trimester. Many members of the \uc2 North Atlantic Treaty Organization\uc2  prohibit elective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  beyond 10 or 12 weeks of gestation. Thus Dobbs permits U.S. states to align their laws more closely with those of American allies.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, the Biden administration's full-throated support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a gift to the West's opponents. It turns a blind eye to the practices of China and North Korea, whose enthusiasm for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is consistent with their inhumane treatment of their people. In China alone there were almost nine million abortions in 2020. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is freely available in state-run hospitals, and the Communist Party has used compulsory \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a population-control measure. By supporting an extreme view on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , U.S. officials align themselves with Chinese Communist Party officials who have gleefully criticized the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dobbs isn't a stain on America's standing in the world. To the contrary, it upholds what the Biden foreign-policy agenda purports to employ as an organizing principle for the free world: democratic self-governance. To defend the decision against the criticism of Canadian Prime Minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  or the Chinese Communist Party is to defend national sovereignty and democracy. America's top diplomats, regardless of their views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , should applaud the high court for respecting the rule of law, democratic decision making and the merits of debating complex matters that touch on the most important questions of justice and human dignity.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps Dobbs offers lessons about the merits of stronger federalism at home and robust geopolitical pluralism in the free world. Learning those lessons would strengthen the hands of our diplomats during these tumultuous times.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Grygiel is a professor of politics at the \uc2 Catholic University of America\uc2 . Ms. Heinrichs is a senior fellow at the \uc2 Hudson Institute\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bidens-abortion-politics-will-undermine-americas-world-standing-roe-v-wade-dobbs-jackson-foreign-policy-11658511777"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden's \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Politics Will Undermine America's World Standing}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220722ei7m00669\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
