\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Georgia Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban Goes Into Effect; Federal appeals court overturns lower court ruling on 2019 'heartbeat' law, citing Supreme Court's Dobbs decision\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 797 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 July 2022\par 23:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Georgia's ban on most abortions after around six weeks of pregnancy took effect after a federal appeals court cleared the way for the 2019 law to be enforced.\par \par \uc2 The Atlanta-based 11th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals said Wednesday the state's law could take effect now that the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated the federal constitutional right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . The decision also overturned a lower-court ruling that blocked the law's definition of personhood, allowing embryos and fetuses to be defined as "persons" under Georgia law.\par \par \uc2 Georgia joins a growing number of states banning or heavily restricting abortions, creating a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patchwork of access across the nation  }}}\uc2 . Many of the laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-decision-sparks-immediate-action-from-states-11656096002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have come into effect  }}}\uc2  after the Supreme Court last month overturned Roe v. Wade, returning the question of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/uncertainty-over-abortion-access-grows-after-supreme-court-ruling-11656357143"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 's legality to states  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In its opinion Wednesday, the 11th Circuit said the high court's decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization "makes clear that no right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exists under the Constitution, so Georgia may prohibit them."\par \par \uc2 The court issued a stay on the lower court's injunction of the law, allowing for it to be enforced immediately. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups, who called the move "highly unorthodox," said they would continue to push for broader \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state.\par \par \uc2 "This cruel \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban would deny our patients the right to make decisions about their own pregnancies, bodies, and futures," Kwajelyn J. Jackson, executive director of Feminist Women's Health Center, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Georgia Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  said the appeals court's decision "affirms our promise to protect life at all stages." The Republican is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/primary-election-results-latest-news/card/brian-kemp-defeats-trump-backed-david-perdue-in-georgia-gop-primary-for-governor-YwbVlXVUUeVqNDDcrRMx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking re-election  }}}\uc2  in November, when he will face Democrat \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  . Ms. Abrams, known for her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/stacey-abrams-to-run-for-georgia-governor-11638393922"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advocacy against alleged voter suppression  }}}\uc2 , has called the 2019 Georgia law draconian.\par \par \uc2 "When I'm elected as the next Governor of Georgia, I will lead the fight to repeal this law and put the power back in the hands of women," she said in a statement Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kemp {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-law-11557266086"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had signed the law  }}}\uc2  as a number of conservative-led states passed similar six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, referred to as "heartbeat bills" by supporters. At the time, the legislation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/some-in-hollywood-threaten-to-leave-georgia-over-abortion-law-11558631360"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced opposition  }}}\uc2  from actors, filmmakers and screenwriters who are part of the state's growing film and television industry.\par \par \uc2 The law bans most abortions after "a detectable human heartbeat," with exceptions for medical emergencies, instances of rape and incest that have been reported to law enforcement and if a fetus is determined to not be viable because of medical issues. It also says Georgia will "recognize unborn children as natural persons"\u8212\'20\'14a part of the law that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups argued was unconstitutionally vague.\par \par \uc2 The ban was previously blocked in court. Shortly after the Supreme Court's decision last month, Georgia Attorney General \uc2 Chris Carr\uc2  filed a notice with the federal appeals court asking it to allow the law to take effect.\par \par \uc2 State Sen. Jen Jordan, who is running against Mr. Carr for state attorney general, said Wednesday's decision resulted directly from his actions.\par \par \uc2 "Carr has played politics with women's lives, and he will pay the price this November," the Democrat said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 A representative for Mr. Carr's office said it is the attorney general's constitutional duty to defend state laws.\par \par \uc2 Zemmie Fleck, executive director of Georgia Right to Life, said her organization had a mixed reaction to the appeals court's move Wednesday, because her group aims to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 "Even though we are very thankful that we've moved it down to six weeks, we will continue to work to actually protect those lives between zero and five or six weeks as well," Ms. Fleck said.\par \par \uc2 Georgia was one of several states, including Kentucky, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, South Carolina and Ohio, to pass "heartbeat" laws in recent years. Most of the bans were blocked in courts before the Supreme Court's Dobbs decision, with two exceptions: Texas and Oklahoma.\par \par \uc2 A Texas law, known as SB8, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans most abortions after six weeks  }}}\uc2  of pregnancy. It took effect in September. The law was able to withstand legal challenges due to a novel enforcement strategy that allows private citizens to bring a civil lawsuit against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. Oklahoma lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahomas-new-abortion-ban-leaves-clinics-reeling-11653610467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed similar laws  }}}\uc2  this year.\par \par \uc2 Since the Supreme Court's ruling last month, previously blocked six-week bans have taken effect in Ohio, South Carolina and Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14Cameron McWhirter contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-six-week-abortion-ban-goes-into-effect-11658352186"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia Six-Week \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban Goes Into Effect  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220720ei7k0070t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
