\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  Says Government Could Sue States Over  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access; Justice Department will seek the dismissal of Texas suit challenging federal rules requiring hospitals to perform emergency abortions when needed to stabilize a patient\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sadie Gurman \par \uc2 658 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 July 2022\par 22:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8211\'20\'13Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  threatened to sue states that have outlawed or restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  last month\u8212\'20\'14and said the Justice Department would ask a judge to toss out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-sues-biden-administration-over-abortion-medical-emergency-guidelines-11657836049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Texas lawsuit seeking to block }}}\uc2  federal rules {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/hospitals-must-provide-abortions-in-emergency-situations-biden-administration-says-11657569637"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requiring doctors to perform abortions in emergency situations }}}\par \par \uc2 "The Justice Department is going to use every tool we have to ensure reproductive freedom," Mr. Garland said on Wednesday, adding that its lawyers would be looking at options including initiating litigation or joining private lawsuits against state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 He didn't say what legal footing those efforts would have after last month's ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated the constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Texas sued the federal government last week after the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  said a federal law protecting access to emergency treatment means hospitals must provide an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if a doctor deems it necessary to stabilize a patient, even if the procedure isn't legal under state law.\par \par \uc2 "This could not be more straightforward," Mr. Garland said. "Where that stabilizing treatment is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , [hospitals] must provide the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  released updated guidance to reduce confusion among hospitals and doctors about when an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal after the Supreme Court's ruling led to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a patchwork of state \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws }}}\uc2 , some with narrow exceptions to protect a pregnant woman's life.\par \par \uc2 Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  said the federal rules fly in the face of the high court's ruling in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/19-1392_6j37.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization }}}\uc2 . That decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-nearly-century-old-abortion-ban-in-effect-for-now-states-high-court-says-11656780694?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 triggered a near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban }}}\uc2  in Texas from the moment of fertilization, tightening access beyond the state's recent law, in place since September, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prohibiting the procedure after about six weeks of pregnancy }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "They are trying to have their appointed bureaucrats mandate that hospitals and emergency- medicine physicians perform abortions," Mr. Paxton said in announcing the suit last week. A representative for Mr. Paxton didn't immediately respond to a request for comment Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department's plan to request the suit's dismissal is a first move as it contemplates what legal experts say are the Biden administration's limited options to push for the availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Supreme Court's ruling.\par \par \uc2 The department said last week it has formed a task force comprising lawyers from across the Justice Department and led by Associate Attorney General Vanita Gupta. Among other aims, the group will evaluate state laws that hinder women's ability to seek abortions in other states where the procedure remains legal or that ban federally approved medication that terminates a pregnancy. The team will also oppose state efforts to penalize federal employees who provide what the Justice Department called "\b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services" authorized by federal law.\par \par \uc2 President Biden this month signed an executive order directing agencies to take steps to protect access to abortions and the privacy of patients seeking them. Some Democrats, including some administration officials, had expressed frustration with Mr. Biden for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/critics-inside-and-outside-white-house-push-biden-for-more-forceful-abortion-response-11656447283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not mounting a more forceful response }}}\uc2 in the days immediately following the ruling.\par \par \uc2 With regard to the lawsuit brought by Texas, Mr. Garland said federal law pre-empts state laws for hospital patients who are experiencing a medical emergency that threatens a pregnant woman's health and life. The Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act requires hospitals to provide treatment to save a patient's life, as well as to prevent organ dysfunction or serious impairment of bodily function.\par \par \uc2 Federal officials have said they would enforce that law, which imposes penalties of up to about $120,000 for each violation.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sadie Gurman at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:sadie.gurman@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sadie.gurman@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/attorney-general-merrick-garland-says-government-could-sue-states-over-abortion-access-11658354465"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Attorney General Merrick Garland Says Government Could Sue States Over \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Access }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220720ei7k0073l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
