\par \par \uc2 Pills are used to conduct more than half of abortions in the U.S., according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have sought to highlight risks of the drugs. PHOTO: Natalie Behring for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 "We're more than prepared to accommodate this increase in demand and have been preparing for this reality for months," said Kiki Freedman, chief executive officer at Hey Jane, which has nearly doubled its clinical team since September. The group, which operates in seven states, said traffic to its website was 10 times higher and payments from new patients had doubled in the week after the Supreme Court decision compared with a month earlier.\par \par \uc2 The divergent operations of U.S. and foreign-based \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill providers are part of a complex, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shifting landscape for access to the procedure }}}\uc2  across the country. The Biden administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-urges-pharmacists-to-fill-prescriptions-for-drugs-that-can-be-used-in-abortions-11657730714"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought to protect access to pills }}}\uc2 used to conduct medication abortions that are approved by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 . Some lawmakers and antiabortion advocates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-sues-biden-administration-over-abortion-medical-emergency-guidelines-11657836049?mod=hp_listb_pos2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 want to crack down }}}\uc2  on their use.\par \par \uc2 Pills are used to conduct more than half of abortions in the U.S., according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks related statistics. The procedure usually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/video/series/daniela-hernandez/medical-abortions-the-science-behind-how-abortion-pills-work/4F6E5767-B022-4B33-9276-A66E76EB5197"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 involves two medicines, mifepristone and misoprostol }}}\uc2 . The \uc2 FDA\uc2  has approved the two-drug regimen for up to 10 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Among some 2,800 people who used telehealth for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , about 96% reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lanam/article/PIIS2667-193X(22)00017-5/fulltext"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the pills were effective }}}\uc2  and 1% reported experiencing a serious adverse event, according to a 2022 study in The Lancet Regional Health-Americas. No deaths were reported among the people surveyed.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have sought to highlight risks of the drugs and said they plan to submit peer-reviewed research to the \uc2 FDA\uc2  showing that women who take the pills are more likely to visit emergency rooms afterward than those who get surgical abortions.\par \par \uc2 Some 20 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups in Mexico send \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medications to U.S. addresses at no cost, said Maria Antonieta Alcalde, director for Mexico and Central America at Ipas, a nonprofit that advocates for women's sexual rights. Some women also cross the border to buy \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills at Mexican pharmacies. Mexico is attractive to U.S. women because pills are cheaper there and the process doesn't leave a paper trail, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists said.\par \par \uc2 Austria-based Aid Access is also mailing pills to women in states that restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The nonprofit said it has U.S.-based clinicians in 22 states where the practice is allowed, and founder and physician Rebecca Gomperts, who is based in Austria, handles requests from people in states that ban or limit medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  via telehealth.\par \par \uc2 Pill requests to Aid Access from people in Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamanetworkopen/fullarticle/2789428"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly tripled to about 30 }}}\uc2  a day over the following three months after the state in September banned most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, according to research by Abigail Aiken, an associate professor of public affairs at the \uc2 University of Texas at Austin\uc2 , published in JAMA Network Open.\par \par \uc2 "That really gives us a window into what we'll see now," Dr. Aiken said. "The group providing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not complying with Texas law, but they're not in the country."\par \par \uc2 Aid Access has seen a significant increase in requests for pills for immediate and future use, said Christie Pitney, a nurse-midwife and U.S.-based Aid Access clinician.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-providers-in-illinois-colorado-and-florida-prepare-for-patient-influx-if-roe-is-overturned-11655560800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pill providers in the U.S. are expanding }}}\uc2  where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to remain protected. Choix said it began operating in New Mexico this month in addition to California, Colorado and Illinois, and it expects patients to travel there from surrounding states expected to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Choix said it plans to operate in every state where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal by the end of 2023.\par \par \uc2 Just The Pill, which provides \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in four states, said it is receiving about 25 appointment requests a day compared with 16 a day before the decision. Just The Pill also has deployed a mobile clinic to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services including abortions in Colorado and is fundraising for a second in Illinois. The clinics will operate along state borders to make them accessible to patients from nearby states, said medical director Julie Amaon.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What role will telehealth play in a post-Roe America? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Helping women travel for abortions from states where the procedure is restricted to states where it is allowed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-providers-and-advocacy-groups-face-new-legal-barriers-to-marketing-their-services-11657188001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could carry legal risks }}}\uc2 , some health-policy experts said. States including Connecticut have enacted legislation protecting patients who travel from other states and their providers. But some have laws that could allow prosecution or lawsuits targeting people or groups that help residents get abortions.\par \par \uc2 "In states that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and have tried to tamp down on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it could be hard to enforce that, but I think it's going to be risky," said Katie Keith, director of the Health Policy and the Law Initiative at Georgetown University's O'Neill Institute.\par \par \uc2 Write to Brianna Abbott at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brianna.abbott@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brianna.abbott@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Juan Montes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:juan.montes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 juan.montes@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-orders-increase-even-in-restrictive-states-11658136602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Pill Orders Increase, Even in Restrictive States  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220718ei7i000un\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
