\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 House Passes Bills Protecting  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access in First Votes After Supreme Court Ruling; Legislation not expected to advance in Senate as House Democrats try to draw contrast with Republicans ahead of midterms\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins \par \uc2 1,179 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2022\par 19:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The House passed two bills Friday aimed at ensuring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and protecting the ability of women seeking abortions to cross state lines, marking the first moves since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended the federal right to the procedure }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bills are unlikely to move in the evenly divided Senate, where Democrats would need at least 10 Republican votes to advance any legislation.\par \par \uc2 The votes follow the high court's ruling last month that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 . Now, because of a patchwork of state laws, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access will vary widely }}}\uc2  depending on where someone lives. Democrats are concerned some states could bar women from going elsewhere for the procedure and are aiming to draw a sharp distinction with Republicans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  heading into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-eager-to-talk-about-abortion-in-campaign-ads-as-gop-shies-away-from-issue-11657886401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the midterm elections }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Should access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  be legislated at the national or state level? Why? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The Democrat-led House voted 219 to 210, with one Democrat, Rep. \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  of Texas, joining all Republicans in opposition, on a bill to stop states from enacting restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability. Doctors generally consider viability, when a fetus could live outside the womb, to fall around 21 to 24 weeks into a pregnancy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-to-vote-on-abortion-rights-measure-to-counter-texas-restrictions-11632493817"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A version of the bill }}}\uc2 , the Women's Health Protection Act, passed the House last year but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/senate-to-vote-on-abortion-access-law-as-supreme-court-weighs-roes-fate-11652274305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to advance in the Senate in May }}}\uc2 , after losing one Democrat and drawing no Republican support.\par \par \uc2 The other bill, the Ensuring Access to \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Act, attempts to provide legal protection for women who cross state lines to obtain the procedure and anyone who helps them, including doctors. That bill passed 223 to 205, with three Republicans\u8212\'20\'14Reps. \uc2 Brian Fitzpatrick\uc2  of Pennsylvania, \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  of Illinois and \uc2 Fred Upton\uc2  of Michigan\u8212\'20\'14joining all Democrats in voting in favor.\par \par \uc2 "This bill respects our right to make our own decisions about our bodies," Rep. Judy Chu (D., Calif.), the sponsor of the Women's Health Protection Act, said on the House floor ahead of the votes.\par \par \uc2 Rep. Jim Banks (R., Ind.), who leads the conservative Republican Study Committee in the House, said Thursday he would oppose both bills, calling them part of what he calls the Democrats' extreme stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "This is all part of a broader package they're putting on the floor, and it just goes to show how far they've gone in that direction," Mr. Banks said.\par \par \uc2 Next week, the House plans to vote on a bill to ensure access to contraception, which could put further pressure on Republicans. Democrats have warned that the reasoning behind the Supreme Court decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could ultimately lead to contraception restrictions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://freedomfortexas.com/uploads/blog/3b118c262155759454e423f6600e2196709787a8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Some lawmakers in Texas have announced plans }}}\uc2  to introduce legislation that would, if passed, provide civil or criminal penalties for those who fund abortions or travel to obtain them. Lawmakers in Missouri have also been trying to stop their residents from having the procedure out of state. Both Texas and Missouri have on their books near-total bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department has taken the position that states can't penalize individuals for crossing state lines to obtain abortions, and efforts to enforce such measures could face trouble in the courts. At least four Supreme Court justices have indicated they would view criminalization of interstate travel for abortions as unconstitutional, including Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , who voted with the five-member majority to overrule Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 May "a state bar a resident of that state from traveling to another state to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? In my view, the answer is no based on the constitutional right to interstate travel," Justice Kavanaugh wrote in a concurring opinion last month.\par \par \uc2 Both bills face steep obstacles in the 50-50 Senate, where 60 votes are required for passage. Senate Democrats haven't announced plans to bring either bill up for passage.\par \par \uc2 A Democratic attempt to pass a bill to protect the ability to cross state lines to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to get unanimous consent in the Senate on Thursday, after Sen. \uc2 James Lankford\uc2  (R., Okla.) objected.\par \par \uc2 "This seems to be just trying to inflame, to raise the 'what if's,'" he said on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 "They want to hold women captive in their own states," said Sen. \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  (D., Wash.), one of the co-sponsors of the right to travel legislation in the Senate, and the chair of the Senate Committee on Health, Education, Labor and Pensions.\par \par \uc2 For now, Senate Democrats have decided that the best strategy is to focus on trying to pass \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation by unanimous consent rather than bring bills up for full floor votes, two Senate Democratic aides said. Democrats knew the travel protection bill would be blocked by a Republican, but the legislation would also fail if it was brought up to a vote.\par \par \uc2 The reason to stick with the unanimous consent strategy is it would allow the party to lump all Republicans together as "extreme" rather than give a small number the opportunity to take a more moderate approach, the people said.\par \par \uc2 House Democrats lamented the inability of Congress to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections signed into law, despite having majorities in the House, Senate and a Democratic president.\par \par \uc2 House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) said Friday that voters should use the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions as fuel in November to vote in more Democratic senators willing to eliminate the 60-vote threshold on most legislation known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-filibuster-senate-explained-11656606298"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the legislative filibuster }}}\uc2 . Currently, two Democratic senators have blocked the party from eliminating the rule.\par \par \uc2 "With two more Democratic senators we will be able to eliminate the filibuster when it comes to a woman's right to choose and to make reproductive freedom the law of the land," Mrs. Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are seen as underdogs in holding on to their narrow majority in the House and the evenly divided Senate is viewed as a tossup from political strategists.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-15-week-abortion-ban-outweighs-opposition-wsj-poll-finds-11648821601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A recent Wall Street Journal poll }}}\uc2  found that 55% of voters surveyed said they wanted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 If Congress were to pass nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections similar to those found in Roe v. Wade, such legislation could face a challenging court battle. In providing for federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, lawmakers would likely point to their authority to regulate interstate commerce, on the grounds that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions affect the availability and cost of the procedure across the country, affect women traveling across state lines to obtain abortions and affect companies that ship pills across state lines, among other issues.\par \par \uc2 But the Supreme Court in recent times has taken a narrower view of the commerce power than in previous eras, making the survival of any legislation uncertain.\par \par \uc2 Jess Bravin contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins+1@wsj.com."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins+1@wsj.com. }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-set-to-vote-on-bills-protecting-abortion-access-11657896570"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Passes Bills Protecting \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Access in First Votes After Supreme Court Ruling }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220715ei7f003bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
