\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Democrats Eager to Talk About  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  in Campaign Ads as GOP Shies Away From Issue; Republicans and allies focus on highest inflation in four decades, not unpopular Supreme Court ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 By John McCormick \par \uc2 1,145 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2022\par 12:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats are increasingly talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their midterm campaign advertising following the Supreme Court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversal of the landmark 1973 Roe v. Wade ruling }}}\uc2 , while Republicans are mentioning it rarely following the late-June decision.\par \par \uc2 A Wall Street Journal analysis of broadcast and national cable data from the ad-tracking firm AdImpact shows more than a third of all spots aired by Democrats and their allies in congressional and gubernatorial campaigns from July 1-12 have mentioned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-gets-a-starring-role-in-gop-congressional-campaign-ads-11648373402"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are focusing their ads on inflation }}}\uc2 , which voters have consistently cited as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-is-taking-biggest-toll-on-nonwhite-voters-wsj-poll-shows-11647255601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their top concern }}}\uc2  heading into November's elections. Less than 3% of all spots run by GOP candidates and their allies during that period included the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, the analysis showed.\par \par \uc2 "Midterm elections are fundamentally base elections, where both parties are focused on getting their base out," said Brian Walsh, a GOP strategist and onetime spokesman for the party's Senate campaign arm. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an issue that emboldens the Democratic base, whereas Republicans are laser focused on economic issues."\par \par \uc2 Several polls conducted since the ruling was handed down have found a majority of Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2022/07/06/majority-of-public-disapproves-of-supreme-courts-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disapprove of the Supreme Court's decision }}}\uc2 . With midterm voting traditionally much lower than in presidential election years, Democrats hope the issue helps motivate voters, especially women, to cast ballots.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic ads are sometimes highly personal in nature. A top candidate competing for the party's \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  nomination in Wisconsin started airing one this week in which his mother, a retired schoolteacher, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V4jXujGMQmg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 talks about an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  she had }}}\uc2  before he was born.\par \par \uc2 "Every woman should have the right to make her own decision," Lt. Gov. Mandela Barnes says in the ad, which is running in the Madison and Milwaukee markets.\par \par \uc2 The Journal's analysis relied on searches for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related words in transcripts and labeling done by AdImpact that seeks to categorize spots by issue. For both parties, the words \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Roe and reproductive were used, while pro-choice was used for Democratic ads and pro-life and unborn were used for Republican ones.\par \par \uc2 The higher level of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related mentions in Democratic ads follows an earlier surge on the topic in the party's advertising after the May 2 leak of a draft of the high court's opinion that foreshadowed the eventual reversal of a decision that made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 In an effort to establish a baseline for both parties, the analysis included airings going back to roughly a month before the leak. The timing of competitive primaries, which tend to trigger more advertising, was also a variable.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin's Democratic U.S. Senate nomination race is the contest that has seen the most \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ads since May 3, the day after the draft leaked. Through July 12, almost 7,800 airings there have made mention of the issue.\par \par \uc2 Almost half of those spots were sponsored by \uc2 Alex Lasry\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/alex-lasry-a-wealthy-democrat-is-targeted-by-both-parties-in-wisconsin-senate-race-11614528000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 son of a billionaire hedge-fund manager }}}\uc2  who co-owns the \uc2 Milwaukee Bucks\uc2  basketball team. Roughly nine out of 10 of his campaign's airings since the leak have mentioned the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Lasry, one of eight candidates on the Aug. 9 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.douglascountywi.org/DocumentCenter/View/13164/Town-of-Amnicon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin Democratic primary ballot }}}\uc2 , is also the overall top advertiser in his primary race. He and the other Democrats are competing for the right to take on Republican Sen. Ron Johnson, who supports the court's decision and is seeking a third term in a state that had the third-narrowest outcome in the 2020 presidential election, when it backed President Biden, a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Johnson's broadcast campaign ads since May 3 haven't mentioned the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but entities opposed to his re-election have criticized him on the topic.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood, a group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, ran roughly $1 million of ads critical of his support for the court's ruling for almost two weeks in late June and early July. The Senate Majority PAC, a super political-action committee aligned with Democrats, has spent more than $264,000 in Wisconsin so far on an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -themed attack on Mr. Johnson that is now airing.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Johnson's campaign declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 The Wisconsin Senate race is attracting lots of outside attention in part because it is the only seat with a Republican seeking reelection among the five Senate races {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/ratings/senate-race-ratings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rated as a "toss up" }}}\uc2  by the nonpartisan Cook Political Report.\par \par \uc2 As the only woman in the Wisconsin primary field, State Treasurer Sarah Godlewski has sought to separate herself from her Democratic opponents on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Godlewski, who is endorsed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights group Emily's List, was the first candidate in the race to air an ad on the topic following the leak. She happened to be in Washington at the time and quickly got herself filmed outside the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UKQ-27VbVIE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the spot }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ken Goldstein, a polling and political analyst who has done academic research on political advertising, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue is likely only to help Democrats "at the margins" in a year with high inflation and other headwinds for the party.\par \par \uc2 "The fundamentals are getting pretty baked into the Republicans' favor," he said. "It's an extra point or a field goal, but that could matter in close races that are within one or two points."\par \par \uc2 The top advertiser in broadcast and cable ads for mentions of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  topic from May 3 through July 12 was the \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2 . Many of its ads were ahead of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/citadels-griffin-loses-50-million-bet-in-billionaire-bout-for-illinois-governorship-11656466455"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the June 28 Illinois primary }}}\uc2 , where the \uc2 DGA\uc2  sought to boost Democratic incumbent Gov. \uc2 J.B. Pritzker\uc2 's prospects in the general election by promoting the most conservative GOP candidate.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What impact will the overturning of Roe v. Wade have on the midterm elections? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The top single Republican-aligned advertiser mentioning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  during that same period was American Dream Federal Action, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/forms/C00809020/1604588/sa/ALL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a super PAC heavily funded by Ryan Salame }}}\uc2 , the co-CEO of cryptocurrency exchange FTX Digital Markets.\par \par \uc2 The super PAC says on its website that it is also promoting candidates who "want to protect America's long term economic and national security." It has run ads boosting GOP candidates in primaries and is currently airing one in the Phoenix area in support of Eli Crane, a former Navy SEAL congressional candidate who has called on his state Legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EliCrane_CEO/status/1442632687404019712?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to decertify the 2020 presidential election }}}\uc2 . The spot calls him a "pro-life, faith-driven conservative."\par \par \uc2 Chad Day contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to John McCormick at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:mccormick.john@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mccormick.john@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-eager-to-talk-about-abortion-in-campaign-ads-as-gop-shies-away-from-issue-11657886401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats Eager to Talk About \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  in Campaign Ads as GOP Shies Away From Issue  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220715ei7f001e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
