\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Texas Sues Biden Administration Over  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Medical-Emergency Guidelines; Texas attorney general says recently released guidance from the Biden administration forces hospitals to commit crimes and risk their licensure\b0\par\par\uc2 By Elizabeth Findell and Melanie Evans \par \uc2 810 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2022\par 22:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 AUSTIN, Texas\u8212\'20\'14The state of Texas sued the Biden administration Thursday, seeking to block federal rules that say doctors are obligated to perform abortions in emergency situations where a pregnant woman is at imminent risk.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  said Monday that a federal law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/hospitals-must-provide-abortions-in-emergency-situations-biden-administration-says-11657569637"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protecting access to emergency treatment  }}}\uc2  means hospitals must provide an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if a doctor deems it necessary to stabilize a patient, even if the procedure isn't legal under state law.\par \par \uc2 Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  said the federal rules fly in the face of the recent \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  ruling to overturn Roe v. Wade, which triggered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-nearly-century-old-abortion-ban-in-effect-for-now-states-high-court-says-11656780694"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban in Texas  }}}\uc2 . The Texas law bans all abortions from the moment of fertilization.\par \par \uc2 "They are trying to have their appointed bureaucrats mandate that hospitals and emergency medicine physicians perform abortions," Mr. Paxton said of the administration. "I will ensure that President Biden will be forced to comply with the Supreme Court's important decision concerning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  called the lawsuit a reflection of an "extreme and radical" Republican official. "It is unthinkable that this public official would sue to block women from receiving lifesaving care in emergency rooms, a right protected under U.S. law," she said.\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  this week released updated guidance to reduce confusion among hospitals and doctors about when an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal after the Supreme Court's ruling created {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a patchwork of state \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws  }}}\uc2 , some with narrow exceptions to protect a pregnant woman's life.\par \par \uc2 Federal law pre-empts state laws for hospital patients who are experiencing a medical emergency that threatens a pregnant woman's health and life, the guidance said. The Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act requires hospitals to provide treatment to save a patient's life, but also to prevent organ dysfunction or serious impairment of bodily function.\par \par \uc2 Hospitals and doctors must act "regardless of the restrictions in the state where you practice," \uc2 HHS\uc2  Secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  said as the guidance was announced.\par \par \uc2 Federal officials said they would enforce the federal law, which comes with its own penalties of up to about $120,000 for each violation.\par \par \uc2 In Texas, doctors can face criminal charges under a law that predates Roe v. Wade for providing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except to save the life of a pregnant woman. Another Texas law typically bars abortions after six weeks except "if a physician believes a medical emergency exists." Violators would face civil penalties of at least $10,000.\par \par \uc2 A trigger law the Texas Legislature passed last year, set to go into effect this month, provides that all abortions in the state are banned from the moment of fertilization. The bill provides an exception if continuing the pregnancy places a woman at risk of death or "serious risk of a substantial impairment of a major bodily function."\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the federal law "forces hospitals and doctors to commit crimes and risk their licensure under Texas law," the lawsuit says.\par \par \uc2 The suit argues that the federal law has never authorized the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  to require healthcare providers to perform abortions or other care and the guidance issued on it oversteps the federal government's authority. It asks the court to issue temporary and permanent injunctions, blocking the law.\par \par \uc2 "They missed the point," \uc2 Sara Rosenbaum\uc2  , a health policy and law professor at George Washington University's Milken Institute School of Public Health, said of the Texas lawsuit. EMTALA wasn't enacted to regulate the practice of medicine, but to create a federal requirement for hospitals to provide access to emergency care, she said.\par \par \uc2 Chance Weldon, director of litigation for the right-wing \uc2 Texas Public Policy Foundation\uc2  , said the language between the federal guidelines and the state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceptions is similar, but said it is still unclear how both will be interpreted on the ground.\par \par \uc2 "Hospitals are caught between a rock and hard place," he said, of trying to determine whether a medical condition meets or defies the criteria of both laws. "There's a lack of clarity about where the overlap is, and the guidance is clear that the federal government would trump here, so that's the injury."\par \par \uc2 Hospitals, doctors and lawyers said they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-struggle-with-state-abortion-restrictions-at-odds-with-federal-law-11657445400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are reviewing laws and sorting through questions  }}}\uc2  about when an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal, in some cases for patients who have an immediate medical need.\par \par \uc2 Former Congressman \uc2 Beto O'Rourke\uc2  , a Democrat who is running against Republican Texas Gov. Greg Abbott, called the lawsuit an attack on Texas women. "This governor's extremism is killing Texas women," Mr. O'Rourke said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-sues-biden-administration-over-abortion-medical-emergency-guidelines-11657836049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas Sues Biden Administration Over \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Medical-Emergency Guidelines  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220714ei7e008y9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
