\par\par \uc2 Health News\par \uc2 Health\par \b \uc2 Some Doctors Rethink Careers After States Restrict Abortions; Doctors who perform abortions are considering their options after the Supreme Court's ruling leaves them unable to continue their work\b0\par\par\uc2 By Julie Wernau and Kris Maher | Photographs by Natalie Behring for The Wall Street Journal \par \uc2 984 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2022\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Giovannina Anthony is among doctors who have rethought their careers since the Supreme Court removed constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An obstetrician-gynecologist, Dr. Anthony has conducted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medical abortions }}}\uc2  at her clinic in Jackson, Wyo., for 17 years. She was the only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in the state before telemedicine-based startup justthepill.com.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's overturning of Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  on June 24 has put her work in doubt. If Gov. Mark Gordon, a Republican, agrees that the decision now triggers a state law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except in cases of rape, incest or danger to the mother's life, it will be take effect within five days. Mr. Gordon is awaiting an analysis of the Supreme Court decision by Wyoming's attorney general, a spokesman for the governor said.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Anthony, 55, said she considered retiring early after the Supreme Court's decision. Instead, she decided to push to keep conducting abortions in Wyoming. If the trigger law takes effect, she and other doctors said they plan to file for a court injunction against it.\par \par \uc2 "I initially felt like I had no fight left in me. Now I'm feeling a little more in fight mode," she said. "I feel like I can make a difference. And for me, that's a reason to stay."\par \par \uc2 The overturning of Roe v. Wade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has changed the work of some doctors performing abortions }}}\uc2  and other healthcare workers involved in the procedures. In response, some of the doctors and workers are traveling to other states to practice temporarily or moving to states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal from states where it is now restricted. Others said they plan to stay in states curbing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to provide access in cases when it remains legal.\par \par \uc2 Catherine Romanos, a family doctor in Ohio, said she plans to make regular drives to Michigan to conduct abortions beginning this month. She is applying for a medical license in Michigan and Illinois, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal. In Ohio, a law that recently took effect banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a fetal heartbeat is detected. Dr. Romanos said she is turning away patients whose pregnancies have advanced past that stage and in some cases advising them to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in other states.\par \par \uc2 "Everything is in flux," she said.\par \par \uc2 After the Supreme Court ruling, abortions are largely unavailable in about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a dozen states because of new bans or legal uncertainty }}}\uc2 . Another roughly half-dozen states could ban or restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon. Demand for abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-providers-in-illinois-colorado-and-florida-prepare-for-patient-influx-if-roe-is-overturned-11655560800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has risen in states where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  remains legal }}}\uc2 , doctors and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates said.\par \par \uc2 Some states that allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are recruiting healthcare workers from states restricting the procedure. The Boulder Valley Women's Health Center in Colorado {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-providers-in-illinois-colorado-and-florida-prepare-for-patient-influx-if-roe-is-overturned-11655560800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has hired two medical assistants }}}\uc2  from Texas in recent months, said medical director Kelly Peters. The center needs more staff to handle an increase in prospective patients, Dr. Peters said.\par \par \uc2 "We had 12 phone calls within the first hour or two after the decision came down," she said.\par \par \uc2 Choices, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Memphis, Tenn., said it is opening a second location three hours away in Carbondale, Ill., a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/illinois-abortion-clinics-are-preparing-for-a-potential-post-roe-world-11638419374"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state where providers have said they are conducting abortions for more patients }}}\uc2  traveling from states where the procedure is restricted.\par \par \uc2 Carafem, which operates clinics that perform abortions in Atlanta, Chicago, Nashville, Tenn., and Washington, D.C., said it has shifted a clinician from Tennessee to Illinois to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/illinois-abortion-clinics-are-preparing-for-a-potential-post-roe-world-11638419374"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 handle higher demand from patients traveling from states }}}\uc2  where the procedure is restricted.\par \par \uc2 Carafem said it canceled about half the appointments at its Nashville clinic after the Supreme Court ruling because those patients' pregnancies had progressed past the six-week mark at which Tennessee law now bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Carafem provided those patients with information about clinics in neighboring states where they could get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Carafem's chief operating officer Melissa Grant.\par \par \uc2 "What we're doing is really watching to see what the need will be because this is just starting," Ms. Grant said.\par \par \uc2 Some clinics said they plan to remain in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be further restricted. Julie Burkhart worked for two years to open what would be the only clinic providing surgical abortions in Wyoming. Wellspring Health Access was close to opening in the city of Casper near the state's center in May when someone broke through a window and set fire to a container of gas in the exam and procedure area. Ms. Burkhart said she plans to rebuild the clinic, even if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned except for rare cases in Wyoming. She said she is also thinking of operating a mobile clinic to conduct abortions.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What ripple effects do you see coming from the decision to overturn Roe v. Wade? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "Any place in America where we can save access to reproductive healthcare, we need to at least try," she said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Burkhart, president of Wellspring Health Access, is also part of a group that recently acquired the Hope Clinic, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in southern Illinois. While she rebuilds the Wyoming clinic in the hopes that the trigger law isn't enacted or is blocked, she has also been working to get the Illinois clinic more resources to handle a surge in demand since the Supreme Court decision.\par \par \uc2 "There are so many phone calls coming in that we haven't been able to get to everyone, which is very disheartening," said Ms. Burkhart. "We had been hiring more people. But now we need more folks."\par \par \uc2 Write to Julie Wernau at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Julie.Wernau@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julie.Wernau@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Kris Maher at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:kris.maher@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kris.maher@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/some-doctors-rethink-careers-after-states-restrict-abortions-11657791001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Some Doctors Rethink Careers After States Restrict Abortions  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220714ei7e000uo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
