\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Correcting the Record on a Rape Case; A man has confessed to a crime that got the President's attention.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 386 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2022\par 13:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 It appears President Biden was accurate when he related a story about a 10-year-old Ohio girl who was raped and traveled to Indiana for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We wondered Tuesday about the case, after no one had confirmed its accuracy or any public report of the crime, though the story had made the media rounds for nearly two weeks.\par \par \uc2 The Columbus Dispatch reported Wednesday afternoon that Columbus police arrested 27-year-old Gerson Fuentes, who has confessed to the sexual assault. Mr. Fuentes has been charged with rape in the first degree and is being held on $2 million bond. The Dispatch story said police learned of the girl's pregnancy through a referral by Franklin County Children Services that was made by her mother on June 22.\par \par \uc2 The Dispatch is part of the USA Today network of papers that includes the Indianapolis Star, which reported on July 1 that the 10-year-old had traveled to Indiana. The Star's story was based on a single source and provided no other confirmation.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden focused on the story last Friday as he announced a new executive order promoting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services. The White House also provided no backup details. Ohio Attorney General \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2  said publicly this week that he had heard "not a whisper" about such a case from local law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 It's unusual that no one in law enforcement stepped forward to confirm that the rape referral had been made, especially after the story had gone viral for days on the internet. But we appreciate our obligation to correct the record on the case, which is a terrible one. The best news is that an alleged rapist has been taken off the street.\par \par \uc2 These columns have long supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, albeit far more limited than those allowed under Roe v. Wade. The country needs to find a rough consensus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  now that it has returned to the states and the political process. One way to help is to make sure that stories about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , from either side of the debate, can be readily confirmed. Passions are already heated enough.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/a-politicized-rape-case-ends-in-arrest-indiana-ohio-ten-year-old-girl-caitlin-bernard-joe-biden-11657749610"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Correcting the Record on a Rape Case}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220713ei7d007pt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
