\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 An  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Story Too Good to Confirm; Biden told a tale of a 10-year old rape victim that no one can identify.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 572 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 July 2022\par 23:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Editor's note: The Columbus Dispatch reported Wednesday, a day after this editorial was published, that a Columbus, Ohio, man has been charged with the rape of a 10-year-old Ohio girl who traveled to Indiana for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Dispatch reports that Columbus police were made aware of the pregnancy through a referral to local child services by the girl's mother on June 22. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/a-politicized-rape-case-ends-in-arrest-indiana-ohio-ten-year-old-girl-caitlin-bernard-joe-biden-11657749610"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An editorial}}}\uc2  correcting the record on the case was published Wednesday evening.\par \par \uc2 All kinds of fanciful tales travel far on social media these days, but you don't expect them to get a hearing at the White House. That's nonetheless what seems to have happened Friday as President Biden signed an executive order on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Health and Human Services Secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  nearby, Mr. Biden repeated a tale making the rounds on social media in the wake of the Supreme Court's decision to overrule Roe v. Wade. He said a 10-year-old girl he didn't identify by name was forced to travel from Ohio to Indiana to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because Ohio now prohibits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a fetal heartbeat is discovered. The girl had been raped, he said, and Ohio law now includes no \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceptions in cases of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden grew agitated as he spoke: "Ten years old. Raped, six weeks pregnant. Already traumatized. Was forced to travel to another state. Imagine being that little girl. Just\u8212\'20\'14I'm serious\u8212\'20\'14just imagine being that little girl."\par \par \uc2 Imagine, indeed. The tale is a potent post-Roe tale of woe for those who want to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a voting issue this fall. One problem: There's no evidence the girl exists. PJ Media's Megan Fox was first to point this out, and so far no one has been able to identify the girl or where she lives.\par \par \uc2 The claim originated in a July 1 Indianapolis Star piece headlined, "Patients head to Indiana for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services as other states restrict care." Caitlin Bernard, an obstetrician-gynecologist, told the paper's medical reporter that after the Ohio ban went into effect she'd fielded a call about the girl from a "child abuse doctor" in the Buckeye State. The 10-year-old soon "was on her way to Indiana to Bernard's care." Presumably Dr. Bernard performed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Medical professionals have a duty to report child rape to law enforcement, but Dr. Bernard won't say where the alleged crime occurred or identify the Ohio doctor who referred the case. Ohio Attorney General \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2  told Fox News on Monday that his office had heard "not a whisper" of such a crime from prosecutors, police and sheriffs in his state. You may not be surprised to learn that Dr. Bernard has a long history of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activism in the media.\par \par \uc2 What we seem to have here is a presidential seal of approval on an unlikely story from a biased source that neatly fits the progressive narrative but can't be confirmed. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate is intense and passions run high. But the American people deserve better from their President than an unproven story designed to aggravate those passions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/an-abortion-story-too-good-to-confirm-joe-biden-ten-year-old-girl-indiana-ohio-caitlin-bernard-11657648618"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Story Too Good to Confirm}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220712ei7c0080x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
