\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 ICE Says Immigrant Women in Custody Still Entitled to  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Services; Memo says women can be transferred to another state if local laws prevent procedure\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michelle Hackman \par \uc2 508 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 July 2022\par 15:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Top immigration officials are planning to instruct detention centers around the country that women in custody are entitled to abortions and should be transferred to receive one if they are being detained in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a state where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is now illegal  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The directive is contained in an undated memorandum, seen by The Wall Street Journal, which cites the recent Supreme Court decision that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended the federal right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . The memo is from U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement Acting Director Tae Johnson and is addressed to Corey Price, head of the agency's enforcement division.\par \par \uc2 "This memorandum serves as a reminder of existing ICE policies and standards requiring that pregnant individuals detained in ICE immigration custody have access to full \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care," the memo states. "This is also a reminder that, pursuant to existing ICE policy, it may be necessary to transfer a detained pregnant individual within an area of responsibility (AOR) or to another AOR, when appropriate and practicable, in order to ensure such access."\par \par \uc2 ICE facilitates abortions for immigrants in its custody in cases of rape or incest, or when the life of the mother is threatened, according to ICE's health regulations.\par \par \uc2 An official familiar with the memo said it would likely be sent later this week, and would represent the first law enforcement agency to reinforce \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in federal custody. ICE detains immigrants in the country unlawfully on civil immigration violations, many of them in the course of their asylum applications.\par \par \uc2 The memo is designed in part to pre-empt potential conflicts with Republican-led states where ICE runs many of its jail facilities and where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have started to take effect, the official said.\par \par \uc2 Many ICE detention centers use space inside local and county jails, and ICE relies on local contractors to run those detention centers and transfer detained immigrants. Should local jails or contractors become subject to restrictive state laws, the person said, the ICE directive would take precedent.\par \par \uc2 It isn't clear how many detained immigrants the new policy would affect. Under President Biden, ICE separately issued a policy last summer that instructs officers to avoid arresting or detaining pregnant women.\par \par \uc2 It adds to the suite of policies the Biden administration is rolling out to demonstrate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-sign-order-stepping-up-efforts-to-protect-access-to-reproductive-care-11657278000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its support for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights  }}}\uc2 . On Monday, for example, the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  told hospitals in new guidance that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/hospitals-must-provide-abortions-in-emergency-situations-biden-administration-says-11657569637"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they are required to perform abortions  }}}\uc2  and provide related services in emergency situations.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has previously been a fraught issue in federal immigration custody. In 2018, under the Trump administration, officials pressured pregnant teenagers living in federal immigration shelters for unaccompanied immigrant children not to have abortions, a policy that sparked a highly publicized legal battle.\par \par \uc2 Write to Michelle Hackman at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:michelle.hackman+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 michelle.hackman+1@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ice-says-immigrant-women-in-custody-still-entitled-to-abortion-services-11657639375"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ICE Says Immigrant Women in Custody Still Entitled to \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Services  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220712ei7c003pd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
