\par\par \uc2 Health News\par \uc2 Health\par \b \uc2 Hospitals Must Provide Abortions in Emergency Situations, Biden Administration Says; Guidance aims to help doctors and hospitals reconcile state laws restricting abortions with federal law that can require the procedure\b0\par\par\uc2 By Melanie Evans \par \uc2 686 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 July 2022\par 01:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Federal health officials said doctors and hospitals must provide an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under federal law when a pregnant woman in emergency medical condition needs the procedure to be stabilized.\par \par \uc2 The Health and Human Services Department said Monday a federal law protecting access to emergency treatment mandates performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if a doctor deems it necessary in a medical emergency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-struggle-with-state-abortion-restrictions-at-odds-with-federal-law-11657445400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even if the procedure isn't legal }}}\uc2  under state law.\par \par \uc2 Under such circumstances, a doctor "must provide that treatment," and the federal Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act pre-empts state law restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the department said in new guidance to hospitals and doctors.\par \par \uc2 The department issued the guidance for performing abortions under the EMTALA law in a bid to clarify for doctors and hospitals struggling to reconcile {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state laws restricting \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  with EMTALA, which can require the procedure to stabilize certain patients.\par \par \uc2 Since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , several doctors and hospitals said they are struggling to reconcile state laws that restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to saving a woman's life with EMTALA's mandate to stabilize emergency patients, including performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect a woman's bodily functions or organs.\par \par \uc2 The announcement is the latest by the Biden administration in response to the Supreme Court's decision leaving it up to states to decide if and when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal.\par \par \uc2 "Protecting both patients and providers is a top priority, particularly in this moment," \uc2 HHS\uc2  Secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  said. "We will continue to leverage all available resources at \uc2 HHS\uc2  to make sure women can access the lifesaving care they need."\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for the Mississippi attorney general's office said the state's law makes an exception for life-threatening emergencies and dismissed the new guidance as a bid by the Biden administration to appease his base.\par \par \uc2 Idaho's attorney general declined to comment, while other state attorneys general didn't immediately provide comment.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration faces pressures from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  supporters to take action bolstering the procedure following the Supreme Court's decision.\par \par \uc2 Yet like an effort {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-administration-releases-new-hipaa-guidelines-in-light-of-abortion-ruling-11656540873"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking to protect the privacy }}}\uc2  of medical information, for instance, the newest action was short on specifics and suggested the limitations of how far the administration could go under existing laws. The new guidelines start by saying they restate current recommendations.\par \par \uc2 New guidance is more detailed than what \uc2 HHS\uc2  previously released on the issue last September, but is still ambiguous, said \uc2 Sara Rosenbaum\uc2 , a health policy and law professor at George Washington University's Milken Institute School of Public Health.\par \par \uc2 "It doesn't clarify all that it needs to around what exists as an emergency and what is stabilizing treatment," she said.\par \par \uc2 Laura Wooster\uc2 , an \uc2 American College of Emergency Physicians\uc2  official, said "a significant amount of uncertainty remains," but the professional association welcomed the new guidance.\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  officials said the guidelines make clear that EMTALA pre-empts state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans without exceptions to protect pregnant women's life and health. They pointed to examples in the guidelines indicating when a woman requires emergency stabilization, such as ectopic pregnancy, complications of pregnancy loss and preeclampsia with severe features.\par \par \uc2 EMTALA, enacted in 1986, protects access to emergency treatment in hospitals even if a patient can't afford it. Under the law, doctors and hospitals have sometimes performed emergency medical abortions to stabilize pregnant women in critical condition.\par \par \uc2 Doctors and hospital lawyers said they face great uncertainty trying to decide whether they can perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legally in light of what some doctors and hospital lawyers say is a mismatch between federal and restrictive state laws. Some said they may need to delay treatment, even though that could increase the risks for patients.\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  officials said the new guidance seeks to assure physicians they don't need to wait for patients to be near death before treatment.\par \par \uc2 Write to Melanie Evans at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Melanie.Evans@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Melanie.Evans@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/hospitals-must-provide-abortions-in-emergency-situations-biden-administration-says-11657569637"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hospitals Must Provide Abortions in Emergency Situations, Biden Administration Says }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220711ei7b004mp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
