\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Pennsylvania Lawmakers Pave Way for Antiabortion Measure on Ballot; Bill passed by both chambers could allow voters to consider a constitutional amendment saying there is no right to an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 701 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 July 2022\par 03:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania legislators passed a bill Friday that helps pave the way for a referendum on whether to exclude protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the state's constitution, setting up a potentially yearslong fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the politically divided state.\par \par \uc2 Both chambers of the state's Republican-led legislature voted to pass a bill that could allow voters to consider a constitutional amendment saying there is no right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or a right to taxpayer funding for the procedure. The bill passed the state's Senate by a vote of 28 to 22, and the House by a vote of 107 to 92.\par \par \uc2 The constitutional amendment must be approved by a majority vote in both chambers in two consecutive years. It could be on the ballot as early as 2023.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania is one of a handful of states weighing measures to amend their state constitutions following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's decision  }}}\uc2  to eliminate the federal constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In some of these states, including Michigan, Kansas and Kentucky, Republican legislatures and Democratic governors are at odds over whether to restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Friday's move allows Pennsylvania's legislature to circumvent the state's Democratic governor, who isn't involved in the process to amend the Pennsylvania constitution. Gov. \uc2 Tom Wolf\uc2  has said he would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access while in office.\par \par \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  , the Democratic candidate for governor in Pennsylvania in November, opposes the amendment and has sought to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a central issue in his campaign.\par \par \uc2 Republican legislators on Friday said the amendment is a defensive move in response to a lawsuit challenging a state ban on public funding for most abortions. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and advocates have argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are protected by a provision of the state constitution guaranteeing equality on the basis of sex. The Pennsylvania Supreme Court is expected to hear the case in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Voters in Kansas will weigh an amendment in early August that would decree that there is no right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provided in the state's constitution, undoing a decision from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-supreme-court-blocks-abortion-ban-11556298338"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state's highest court  }}}\uc2  in 2019 that had found such a right. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have relied on clinics in Kansas to help manage an influx of patients from nearby states such as Texas and Oklahoma as bans and restrictions took effect over the past year.\par \par \uc2 Several states already have adopted amendments similar to the one being proposed in Pennsylvania. Alabama, Louisiana, Tennessee and West Virginia approved similar constitutional amendments in the years before the Supreme Court's decision.\par \par \uc2 Some Democratic-led states are moving in the opposite direction. Voters in Vermont and California will consider constitutional amendments in November {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/vermont-is-one-step-closer-to-adding-abortion-rights-to-its-constitution-11644348231"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that would enshrine \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights  }}}\uc2  in their state constitutions.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have until Monday to collect more than 425,000 signatures needed to add a proposed constitutional amendment protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the November ballot.\par \par \uc2 In more-conservative states, such groups might face an uphill climb. Arizonans for Reproductive Freedom, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights group, said Thursday that it had failed to collect enough signatures to add a similar proposed amendment on the ballot in November. The group will aim to bring a similar measure to the state ballot in 2024, said Shasta McManus, campaign treasurer for the organization.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere Friday, a Louisiana judge allowed enforcement of a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state, saying her court lacked jurisdiction to hear a lawsuit challenging it. The Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one of the groups representing clinics in the state, said that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services in the state had stopped in light of the court's ruling and that it would ask a court in Baton Rouge to block the law.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana Attorney General \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2  said he would continue to defend the ban.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pennsylvania-lawmakers-pave-way-for-anti-abortion-measure-on-ballot-11657334915"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania Lawmakers Pave Way for Antiabortion Measure on Ballot  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220709ei790005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
