\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Lawsuits to Test Whether State Constitutions Protect  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights; After demise of Roe v. Wade,  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  providers and advocacy groups argue state laws should be read to protect access to the procedure\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 1,039 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 July 2022\par 14:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 's decision last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ending the federal constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  has prompted advocates for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to look anew at state constitutions, setting up legal battles over whether the protections found in Roe v. Wade exist at the state level.\par \par \uc2 Providers and legal advocacy groups so far have filed about a dozen lawsuits in state court that seek to head off {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broad \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions. }}}\uc2  The suits cite an array of provisions in state constitutions, including ones that offer privacy guarantees and protections against discrimination based on sex.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents argue that these vaguely worded provisions don't address or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recognize legal protections for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 . }}}\uc2  They say state courts would be improperly inventing new rights if they decide otherwise, much as they argue the Supreme Court did with the U.S. Constitution in its recently overturned 1973 Roe v. Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 In some cases, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates argue that state constitutions have stronger grounds for protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  than what had previously been recognized at the federal level.\par \par \uc2 "Certainly I don't think that state courts and state constitutions are going to be a full substitute for federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, but I think they are an underappreciated source of rights," said Alicia Bannon, who studies courts at New York University's Brennan Center for Justice.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups are pressing their cases in some deeply conservative states. In Oklahoma, for example, state courts over the years have repeatedly blocked \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions without squarely ruling on the question of whether the state's constitution protects a right to choose the procedure. That could change in a new batch of cases in which plaintiffs say multiple different {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-governor-signs-abortion-ban-11653529937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma bans on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  violate rights guaranteed by the state's constitution to personal autonomy, bodily integrity and health.\par \par \uc2 In North Dakota this week, the only remaining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in the state challenged a ban on most abortions set to take effect later this month, arguing it violates provisions in the state's constitution that protect life, safety and happiness.\par \par \uc2 Other litigation is proceeding in more politically mixed states, such as Pennsylvania, Michigan and North Carolina, which all have pending cases that could create state constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Courts could play a decisive roll in all three states, which have Democratic governors and Republican-led legislatures and have in recent years been unable to enact significant laws either protecting or restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Courts in a number of states, including Montana and Kansas, already have interpreted their state constitutions to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents warn that a new generation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases could create protracted battles on the state level similar to the decadeslong political, legal and cultural war that followed the Supreme Court decision creating a federal constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Every state court has the potential to have a mini-Roe and to read into their state constitution words that are not there," Carrie Severino, president of the Judicial Crisis Network, a conservative legal group, told attendees at the Western Conservative Summit in Colorado shortly before the Supreme Court decision was issued.\par \par \uc2 In a recent court filing defending an Ohio law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy, state Attorney General \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2  warned the Ohio Supreme Court that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and advocates "ask this court to travel Roe's path."\par \par \uc2 "If this court creates a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the state judiciary will face a flood of cases challenging every minute detail of the many laws regulating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Mr. Yost, a Republican, wrote. "Every judicial election will focus on this issue; voters will be urged to choose judges based on the candidates' willingness to expand or contract constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Any victories won by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters could be far less lasting than the Roe decision, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-v-wade-overturned-supreme-court-11656110804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took nearly 50 years for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  opponents to undo. }}}\par \par \uc2 Many state Supreme Court justices are elected or must be reconfirmed at regular intervals, so the composition of state courts shifts more quickly than the federal judiciary. State constitutions are also much easier to amend than the federal constitution. A handful of states this year alone are poised to hold referendums on amendments to either explicitly protect or preclude protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 State court observers said they expect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to inject a new level of money, attention and controversy into how state court judges are chosen, similar to the way that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped polarize the selection process for Supreme Court justices.\par \par \uc2 "The decisions recognizing a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provoke backlash, and we're seeing that across the board," said Amy Myrick, a lawyer at the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think state constitutions might offer an effective way to protect the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped reshape some state courts even before the recent ruling overturning Roe, most notably in Iowa. That state's highest court recognized a state constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2018, voting 5 to 2 to strike down a law that required a mandatory waiting period before a woman could get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The state's Republican-led legislature and GOP governor changed the nominating process for state Supreme Court justices in 2019 to give the governor more control. Last month, that court reversed itself in another case, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't among the fundamental privacy rights in the state constitution.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are hopeful that the Florida Supreme Court could follow a similar course in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-pauses-on-more-abortion-restrictions-following-supreme-court-decision-11656591626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenge to a 15-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban }}}\uc2  currently making its way up from the lower courts.\par \par \uc2 Florida's high court had blocked a number of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions over the years, citing a 1980 amendment to the state's constitution protecting a right to privacy. Since taking office, Republican Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has been able to appoint three members to the seven-member court.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Calfas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuits-to-test-whether-state-constitutions-protect-abortion-rights-11657375200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lawsuits to Test Whether State Constitutions Protect \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rights  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220709ei7900209\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
