\par\par \uc2 The Numbers\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Tracking  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. Is About to Get Murkier; Supreme Court decision overturning Roe v. Wade makes possible a rise in 'self-managed' abortions, for which data are harder to collect\b0\par\par\uc2 By Josh Zumbrun \par \uc2 1,072 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 July 2022\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminating the constitutional right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  is sure to alter the numbers on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. But we might not know by how much. Statistics on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are about to become unreliable at precisely the moment the public is most interested in them.\par \par \uc2 The majority opinion released last month in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization overturned Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision that established a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As a result new restrictions, including total bans, can go into effect in 22 states. And while that is expected to lead to fewer abortions, it might become hard to distinguish an actual decline from a decline in how many abortions are counted.\par \par \uc2 "When you think about accurately measuring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S., it was pretty difficult prior to the Dobbs decision and it's going to become far more difficult in this rapidly evolving legal landscape," said Lauren Ralph, associate professor at the \uc2 University of California, San Francisco\uc2 , an expert on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics.\par \par \uc2 The primary data source for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. is the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks statistics. Since 1973 it has conducted a regular survey, now triennial, of all known facilities providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S., asking how many abortions were performed.\par \par \uc2 Most clinics respond to the institute's survey. (Many hospitals don't, but hospitals provide relatively few abortions and state health data help fill in the gaps.)\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  also compiles statistics, but researchers, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates and antiabortion groups, generally agree Guttmacher's data are superior.\par \par \uc2 Guttmacher's statistics "probably do a pretty good job of capturing the overall incidence or overall number," says Jim Studnicki, vice president of data analytics at the Charlotte Lozier Institute, the research and education institute of Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America. By contrast he faults the data the CDC collects from states. State data are reported inconsistently, because some states don't report race and ethnicity\u8212\'20\'14or report any data. States don't even use a consistent definition of how many weeks along a pregnancy is. The CDC acknowledges these limitations to its data.\par \par \uc2 Most glaringly, the CDC receives and reports no data from California, while Guttmacher shows California has more abortions than any other state.\par \par \uc2 Guttmacher tallied over 900,000 abortions in clinical settings in 2019 and 2020, compared with the CDC's 2019 estimate of 630,000.\par \par \uc2 But note that key phrase: "in clinical settings." Even before Dobbs, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-providers-prepare-to-reach-patients-in-restrictive-states-11652439601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new type of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  was on the rise outside of clinics.\par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration's approval of the drug mifepristone in 2000 made it possible to obtain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  via medication. Medication abortions have steadily grown as a share of all abortions, but until recently occurred primarily in clinics.\par \par \uc2 Beginning in 2018, Aid Access, a nonprofit incorporated in Austria, became the first online telemedicine service to offer medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  anywhere in the U.S., including in states where the procedure is otherwise banned. (For those states, Aid Access mails medication from India.) Patients have a teleconsultation online with doctors in Europe and can have the medicine shipped directly to their home. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is then self-managed at home, rather than through a clinic, and therefore isn't counted by Guttmacher.\par \par \uc2 There is evidence that women in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is restricted or banned might seek out self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14through Aid Access, through online pharmacies based outside the U.S. or through other methods if a state's clinics close. In these states, it will be difficult to tell how much \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined, if at all, unless data collection changes.\par \par \uc2 "We know in the last couple of years that reliance on self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased," said \uc2 Rachel Jones\uc2 , principal research scientist at Guttmacher. "That's something we're going to have to explore."\par \par \uc2 Abigail Aiken, an associate professor at the University of Texas, spotted that gap in the statistics. In partnership with Rebecca Gomperts, a Dutch doctor and the founder of Aid Access, she calculated that from March 2018 to March 2020, a total of 57,506 people {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamanetworkopen/fullarticle/2780272"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requested self-managed medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  through Aid Access. (Aid Access doesn't know exactly how many people who request medication actually take it. In a follow-up poll, 12% of recipients said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lanam/article/PIIS2667-193X(22)00017-5/fulltext"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they didn't actually use the medicine }}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 Her research also shows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamanetworkopen/fullarticle/2789428"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demand for Aid Access surges }}}\uc2  when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes more restricted. In September 2021, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-ban-11621452346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when Texas banned abortions }}}\uc2  with few exceptions after the sixth week of pregnancy, the number of abortions in Texas clinics fell by 2,347\u8212\'20\'14over 50%\u8212\'20\'14but Aid Access received 1,831 requests for self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Texas, briefly receiving 12 times as many requests as the same period a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 While data from some organizations such as Aid Access might ultimately get reported, many other abortions might not.\par \par \uc2 In 2017, Guttmacher estimated that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/news-release/2017/abortion-common-experience-us-women-despite-dramatic-declines-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24% of women }}}\uc2  would have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by age 45. A sizable share might end up electing self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In 2020, Dr. Ralph of \uc2 UCSF\uc2  and co-authors, based on a survey of 7,022 women aged 18 to 49, estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamanetworkopen/fullarticle/2774320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7% would attempt to self-manage an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , not just through an organization like Aid Access, "but other methods: herbs, over-the-counter medicines, drugs, alcohol, physical methods, some of which we know have the potential for harm and are ineffective."\par \par \uc2 But research like hers will almost certainly become more difficult, she said. State restrictions have two effects: Women will be more likely to pursue abortions outside clinical settings, and women and providers might become less likely to talk about having or facilitating abortions, out of concern of running afoul of the new legal restrictions, she said.\par \par \uc2 "We want to know how often this is happening to understand the burden women are experiencing," Dr. Ralph said. "At the same time, we need to move carefully in an evolving legal landscape where there's the potential that behaviors could be criminalized."\par \par \uc2 Write to Josh Zumbrun at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Josh.Zumbrun@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Josh.Zumbrun@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/tracking-abortion-in-the-u-s-is-about-to-get-murkier-11657272600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tracking \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  in the U.S. Is About to Get Murkier  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220708ei780012y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
