\par\par \uc2 CMO Today\par \uc2 C Suite\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Providers and Advocacy Groups Face New Legal Barriers to Marketing Their Services; State laws and social-media policies complicate the regulatory landscape after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patrick Coffee \par \uc2 1,055 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 July 2022\par 19:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 Plan C operates under the fiscal sponsorship of the nonprofit National Women's Health Network Inc. An earlier version of this article incorrectly said the group is funded by that organization. Additionally, a local business that helped Plan C organize an ad campaign may have to remain anonymous due to concerns about liability. An earlier version of this article incorrectly identified the business as an advertising agency. (Corrected on July 7)\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court decision overturning Roe v. Wade has created {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a legally fraught landscape  }}}\uc2  for organizations that advertise \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services or provide information about getting them.\par \par \uc2 The new mishmash of proposed and existing state-level laws has all but guaranteed a raft of legal battles that could ensnare both ad buyers and sellers, some experts say.\par \par \uc2 The biggest concern for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related advertisers is the legal gray area between states that have banned various \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures and those that haven't. That is especially true when states with bans also have laws that could allow them to prosecute people or organizations that help residents get such services elsewhere or encourage lawsuits in such cases.\par \par \uc2 "There's going to be a lot of politically motivated litigation," said \uc2 Gary Kibel\uc2  , partner at law firm Davis+Gilbert LLP, which specializes in advertising law. "For the marketing and advertising industries, the unfortunate challenge is, if you're advertising something that's illegal where it is illegal, that's risky."\par \par \uc2 If a group based in Colorado runs an ad about legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services that is geo-targeted to reach Texas residents, for example, both the group and the ad seller could theoretically be sued for aiding and abetting abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under Texas Senate Bill 8  }}}\uc2 , said Mr. Kibel. The law bars \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy and lets private citizens bring civil lawsuits against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to enforce it.\par \par \uc2 Some organizations have already curtailed their marketing activities.\par \par \uc2 "We haven't done any paid advertising in restricted states since the \uc2 Scotus\uc2  decision came, just to be safe," said Stacey Kawakami, head of strategic communications at FemHealth USA Inc., which operates as nonprofit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and birth control services provider Carafem.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, nonprofit Power to Decide, which uses Google Search ads to promote a tool called \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finder that helps people find providers, is closely watching state laws to determine how they might affect its ability to advertise.\par \par \uc2 "Our intention is to do everything we can in our power to keep getting the word out to everyone in the country about this tool," said Jennifer Johnsen, vice president of digital and education at Power to Decide. "It's kind of a 'we'll see how it goes' moment."\par \par \uc2 For \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, the tension comes amid a dramatic rise in consumer interest.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Johnsen said \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finder's traffic has increased more than 10-fold since May 2, when Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published a leaked draft  }}}\uc2  of the Supreme Court opinion.\par \par \uc2 Average daily visits to the home page of Plan C, a group under the fiscal sponsorship of the nonprofit National Women's Health Network Inc. that provides information on accessing so-called \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, went from 500 before the Texas law's passage last year to 209,000 on the day last month that the Supreme Court released its decision, said Elisa Wells, co-founder and co-director at Plan C.\par \par \uc2 Some groups remain committed to getting their message out.\par \par \uc2 Plan C intends to follow through with a series of billboards and radio ads in one of the states that just outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Regarding potential lawsuits, Ms. Wells said, "We're willing to test that boundary rather than just stop providing information out of fear that it might happen." But the local business that helped Plan C organize the campaign may have to remain anonymous due to concerns about liability, she said.\par \par \uc2 Possible Health Inc., which operates as Hey Jane and provides direct-to-consumer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and related services, will continue spending tens of thousands of dollars each month on \uc2 Google\uc2  Search ads, said Gaby Izarra, co-founder and head of growth and marketing.\par \par \uc2 "Considering that only one in four people is aware that medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exists, a big part of our strategy in the months ahead will be to raise awareness around medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ms. Izarra.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, Hey Jane only runs ads on \uc2 Google\uc2  and currently limits its targeting to residents of the six states it operates in that allow the pills to be both prescribed and distributed remotely: California, Colorado, Illinois, New Mexico, New York and Washington.\par \par \uc2 Several groups also said digital ad platforms have been more likely to reject both paid and organic posts that include words like "\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 " and "pregnancy" in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Kawakami shared two Carafem posts that she said were recently censored by \uc2 Instagram\uc2  ; one featured text explaining how medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  works over a cat video, while the other read, "It's OK to have more than one \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." Both were restored only after Carafem filed complaints with \uc2 Instagram\uc2  parent \uc2 Meta Platforms Inc\uc2  ., she said.\par \par \uc2 Plan C Social Media Director Martha Dimitratou also shared images of several posts and ads that were rejected by \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  for promoting "the sale or use of\u8230\'20\'26unsafe substances."\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Meta\uc2  spokeswoman said some of the ads in question were rejected because they lacked prior certification to promote prescription drugs or had not obtained the preapproval required for all ads that include sociopolitical commentary. She declined to elaborate.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Kawakami said Carafem's greatest digital marketing success has come on TikTok. One video created in collaboration with Carafem, in which an anthropologist and influencer demonstrates how to obtain and use \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, got more than 2.3 million organic views.\par \par \uc2 Yet TikTok bans all paid ads promoting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, which it classifies as "unsuitable businesses."\par \par \uc2 "I think it's going to become even harder for folks to find places to advertise," said Mr. Kibel, the Davis+Gilbert lawyer.\par \par \uc2 Write to Patrick Coffee at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:patrick.coffee@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patrick.coffee@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-providers-and-advocacy-groups-face-new-legal-barriers-to-marketing-their-services-11657188001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Providers and Advocacy Groups Face New Legal Barriers to Marketing Their Services  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220707ei770018j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
