\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Democrats Criticize Biden Plan to Nominate Antiabortion Republican to Judgeship; Administration told Kentucky officials it would nominate Chad Meredith, documents show, but appears to have reversed course after Supreme Court's  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  decision\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew Restuccia \par \uc2 735 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2022\par 19:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The White House told Kentucky Gov. \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 's office that President Biden planned to nominate to the federal bench a Republican who has defended the state's efforts to restrict access to abortions, according to newly released documents.\par \par \uc2 But the administration hasn't followed through on announcing the nomination after the Supreme Court last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended constitutional protections for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 White House discussions about nominating Chad Meredith, the state's former solicitor general, to a lifetime role on the U.S. District Court for the Eastern District of Kentucky have been met with anger from Democrats and progressive activists. The plans and the internal documents were earlier reported by the Courier Journal newspaper in Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 On June 23, one day before the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, a White House staff member told an official in the office of Mr. Beshear, a Democrat, that Mr. Meredith's nomination would be announced the following day, according to emails released by the governor's office. The Wall Street Journal obtained the documents after a public records request.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 John Yarmuth\uc2  (D., Ky.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/mitch-mcconnell/2022/07/05/who-chad-meredith-bidens-anti-abortion-pick-kentucky-judge/7790119001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Courier Journal }}}\uc2  he thought the White House agreed to nominate Mr. Meredith, a move he opposed, as part of a deal with Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) to smooth passage for other nominees. Mr. Yarmuth's office didn't immediately respond to a request for comment. A spokesman for Mr. McConnell declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 The White House never followed through with the announcement, which would have come amid nationwide protests in response to the Supreme Court's decision. Many in the White House expected the high court to hand down its decision the following week, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 On June 29, five days after the Supreme Court ruling, the same White House staffer sent another email to the official in Mr. Beshear's office saying that the information in the previous email was "pre-decisional and privileged."\par \par \uc2 A White House official declined to comment, citing the administration's policy of not commenting on nominations until they are made public. During a Tuesday news conference, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  declined to say whether Mr. Biden would ever appoint a judge to the federal bench who doesn't support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden has announced more than 100 federal judicial nominees since taking office, according to the White House. Nearly 70 have been confirmed by the Senate, more than any president in recent decades at this point in his term. Several dozen federal judgeships remain vacant without a nominee.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Meredith, who is now a lawyer at \uc2 Squire Patton Boggs\uc2 , served as Kentucky's solicitor general from 2019-2021. Before that, he was chief deputy general counsel to then-Gov. \uc2 Matt Bevin\uc2 , a Republican. In that role, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-lets-stand-kentucky-abortion-ultrasound-law-11575919419"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. Meredith defended }}}\uc2  the state's law requiring doctors to perform an ultrasound examination\u8212\'20\'14even over a patient's objection\u8212\'20\'14before performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Meredith didn't respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 "If the president makes that nomination, it is indefensible," Mr. Beshear said last week during a press conference. The governor pointed to Mr. Meredith's alleged involvement, previously reported by the Courier Journal, in Mr. Bevin's decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/2019/12/11/bevin-issued-hundreds-pardons-and-commutations-final-day/4399770002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to issue a series of pardons and commutations }}}\uc2  before leaving office, including to a man who was convicted of homicide. Mr. Bevin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/2019/12/15/matt-bevin-pardon-controversy-former-kentucky-governor-defends-pardon/2655985001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has defended the pardons }}}\uc2  as justified.\par \par \uc2 "I don't know how the president can say he's for public safety if he makes this nomination," Mr. Beshear said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/critics-inside-and-outside-white-house-push-biden-for-more-forceful-abortion-response-11656447283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has faced criticism from some Democrats }}}\uc2  for his response to the Supreme Court's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling. His critics say the president should have been prepared to deliver a detailed plan with specific executive actions following the decision, which had leaked weeks before it was officially announced. The White House has called on Congress to take action to codify Roe v. Wade into law and said it would take steps to allow women to travel to other states for abortions and preserve access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrew Restuccia at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:andrew.restuccia@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 andrew.restuccia@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-criticize-biden-plan-to-nominate-antiabortion-republican-to-judgeship-11657129660"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats Criticize Biden Plan to Nominate Antiabortion Republican to Judgeship  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220706ei76005eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
