\par\par \uc2 Health News\par \uc2 Health\par \b \uc2 Little-Known  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pill Maker Faces Scrutiny; Debate over medication abortions draws in lone U.S. manufacturer of brand-name mifepristone\b0\par\par\uc2 By Liz Essley Whyte \par \uc2 1,146 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 July 2022\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning of Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  has put a spotlight on a small manufacturer of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, which are emerging as a flashpoint between advocates and opponents of the procedure.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates have for decades lobbied for more access to mifepristone, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication that Danco Laboratories LLC manufactures under the brand name Mifeprex and sells for about $50 a pill. They want the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  to remove safety restrictions on the drug, make it available without a prescription or expand its label to approve it for miscarriage, for which it is also sometimes prescribed, off label. An official use for miscarriage would help ensure women experiencing a miscarriage could get the drug. It might also make it more difficult for prosecutors to investigate doctors who dispense the pills in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states where abortions are banned  }}}\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  has said Danco would have to present data demonstrating that the medication is safe under those circumstances. Privately held Danco said it doesn't currently plan to ask the \uc2 FDA\uc2  for an expanded label or approval for use after miscarriage.\par \par \uc2 "There are always voices within this community that want to see us go further and do more than what we've done," said a Danco spokeswoman. "We try to be very pragmatic about our approach to things and do as much as we can within the box that we're in."\par \par \uc2 The pills used to conduct {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what are known as medication abortions  }}}\uc2  are becoming hotly contested in the U.S. Even before the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade last month and states began adding restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the pills {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-providers-prepare-to-reach-patients-in-restrictive-states-11652439601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accounted for more than half of abortions  }}}\uc2  in the U.S. according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  , a group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related statistics.\par \par \uc2 Enforcing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans where pills are available could be difficult, policy experts said, because they can be sent through the mail and taken at home. The Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/critics-inside-and-outside-white-house-push-biden-for-more-forceful-abortion-response-11656447283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 administration has said it would defend  }}}\uc2  people's right to take the drug.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have pressed states to restrict the use of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. Nineteen states have laws that require doctors to prescribe them in person, according to Guttmacher. Some require patients to return for a follow-up visit or have other restrictions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-abortion-lawsuits-continue-in-states-cutting-access-11656543956"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State bans on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  taking effect  }}}\uc2  following the overturning of Roe v. Wade also apply to the pills. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have sought to highlight risks of the drug and said they plan to submit to the \uc2 FDA\uc2  peer-reviewed research showing that women who take the pills are more likely to visit emergency rooms afterward than those who get surgical abortions.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone blocks progesterone, a hormone necessary for continuing a pregnancy, causing the gestational sac to detach from the walls of the uterus. A day or two after taking it, patients take misoprostol, a drug that causes contractions, pushing out the embryo or fetus and tissue associated with the pregnancy. Patients experience cramps and bleeding. Side effects can include nausea, vomiting and dizziness. In rarer cases women can hemorrhage or become infected.\par \par \uc2 A generic form of mifepristone made by GenBioPro Inc. has captured a significant share of the U.S. market since it was introduced in 2019, the company said in a court filing. Privately held GenBioPro filed a lawsuit against Mississippi in 2020, arguing that the state inappropriately restricts \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills since the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has said the drugs are safe and effective. Danco wasn't a party to the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 GenBioPro began distributing mifepristone via telehealth providers and pharmacies during the pandemic, soon after a judge in 2020 ruled the \uc2 FDA\uc2  couldn't enforce an earlier safety restriction requiring women seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to get them from a doctor or other provider in person. Danco followed several months later. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  made the change permanent late last year.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What is the future for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill manufacturers in the U.S.? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 New York City-based Danco, with fewer than 25 employees who now mostly work remotely, said it doesn't have the resources to do the clinical trials and legal work to ask the \uc2 FDA\uc2  for major changes to the allowed use of its product. "The company is very moderately profitable, and the investors only have so much," the spokeswoman said. "It's not a bottomless bucket for them."\par \par \uc2 Foundations formed by David Packard, George Soros and Warren Buffett {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB968103355754057093"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helped establish Danco  }}}\uc2  and pay for its clinical trials in the 1990s but aren't owners of the company, the spokeswoman said. Mr. Buffett supports a small {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/warren-buffetts-estate-planning-bill-and-melinda-gates-foundation-sends-charities-scrambling-11655811074"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 family foundation that backs \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights  }}}\uc2 , and officials there plan to receive a massive influx of money from Mr. Buffett's estate.\par \par \uc2 Danco's only product is Mifeprex, and the company maintains a low profile. Its office has no sign, and employees answer its main phone line with a "hello" instead of identifying the company. Danco said its pills are manufactured in Europe. It doesn't disclose investors, board members or its chief executive for fear they might be targeted by antiabortion activists, the spokeswoman said. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
