\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden Faces Fresh Domestic Challenges After Europe Summits; President must grapple with concerns over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling, a faltering economy and a narrowing window to pass legislation before midterm elections\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alex Leary in Madrid and Tarini Parti in Washington \par \uc2 1,348 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 July 2022\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 President Biden returned from Europe with a deal to expand the \uc2 NATO\uc2  alliance and plans for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-to-ramp-up-military-presence-in-europe-to-counter-russia-11656505684"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 biggest U.S. military footprint }}}\uc2  in the continent since the Cold War. But awaiting him back home was a host of domestic challenges, including intraparty frustration with his response to the Supreme Court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling overturning \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 , continuing economic worries and questions about the fate of his legislative agenda.\par \par \uc2 With some fellow Democrats calling for him to be more forceful on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Biden endorsed making {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-filibuster-senate-explained-11656606298"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an exception to filibuster rules }}}\uc2  to pass legislation codifying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  into law, as he wrapped up his trip. And on his first day back, he met virtually with Democratic governors, some of whom continued to push Mr. Biden to make more use of federal resources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to protect access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's backing of an exception to the filibuster came nearly a week after the Supreme Court's ruling, following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ruling-overturning-roe-v-wade-sets-off-celebrations-protests-11656083195"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests across the country }}}\uc2 . The president didn't publicly speak on the filibuster issue, and the administration continued to dodge questions about changing the rules, until he announced his decision at the end of the trip in response to a question at a press conference. Changing the Senate rule, however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-says-he-supports-exception-to-filibuster-to-codify-roe-v-wade-into-law-11656596123"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already faces major hurdles }}}\uc2  with two Senate Democrats opposed to making changes.\par \par \uc2 Acknowledging he didn't have the votes to change the filibuster rules, Mr. Biden said Friday voters needed to elect more Democrats to the Senate in November, warning that Republicans would seek to pass nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions if they take control of Congress. "There's a lot at stake here," he said.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the midterm elections, Mr. Biden has to contend with a charged political environment and a raft of economic problems, including high prices for food and gasoline. Heading into the July Fourth holiday weekend, the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  emphasized that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOP/status/1542236975633154049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the staples of a holiday barbecue would cost more }}}\uc2  because of inflation.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden also returned to new data showing U.S. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-consumer-spending-personal-income-may-2022-11656531317"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 household spending slowed in May }}}\uc2  as Americans faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-definition-cause-what-is-it-11644353564"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historically high inflation }}}\uc2  and elevated interest rates. The American economy is facing the threat of recession as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  pushes up interest rates in an attempt to cool {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/us-inflation-consumer-price-index-may-2022-11654810079"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four-decade high inflation }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some 85% of U.S. adults say the country is on the wrong track and 79% consider the economy to be poor, according to an Associated Press-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research poll released Wednesday. Only 39% of Americans approve of Mr. Biden's leadership, the poll showed, and 69% disapprove of his handling of the economy.\par \par \uc2 On Capitol Hill, a bipartisan push to increase U.S. semiconductor production and competitiveness with China\u8212\'20\'14a priority for Mr. Biden\u8212\'20\'14has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bipartisan-tech-investment-bill-hits-new-hurdle-11656694629"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 run into further trouble }}}\uc2  after Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) said last week that Republicans wouldn't back such a package as long as Democrats planned a separate climate and prescription-drug budget plan that would pass with only Democratic votes.\par \par \uc2 That second piece of legislation is being negotiated by Democratic leaders with Sen. Joe Manchin (D., W.Va.), and the White House is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-hunts-for-small-wins-as-democratic-frustration-builds-11654788300"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eager to accept whatever deal they strike }}}\uc2  and take a win, even if it is significantly scaled down from what Mr. Biden originally sought. But Congress will need to move quickly if either of the two packages is to pass before the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Following the summits in Europe, what should be President Biden's top focus on the domestic front? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Should Democrats lose power in one or both chambers of Congress, as many election analysts expect, his agenda will be hobbled and Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/prosecutors-advance-tax-probe-of-hunter-biden-11648465200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have foreshadowed numerous probes }}}\uc2  of his administration as well as the foreign business dealings of his son, Hunter.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden also faces challenges internationally.\par \par \uc2 This month he will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-meet-with-saudi-arabias-crown-prince-in-july-11655208002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel to the Middle East }}}\uc2  with stops in Israel, the West Bank and Saudi Arabia, where he is expected to encounter Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman. Mr. Biden has repeatedly criticized Saudi Arabia for its human-rights record and for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/saudi-crown-prince-says-khashoggi-was-killed-under-my-watch-denies-role-11569513897"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 2018 killing of journalist Jamal Khashoggi }}}\uc2 . Mr. Biden also called the kingdom a pariah when he was running for president.\par \par \uc2 Facing pressure over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gasoline-prices-reach-5-a-gallon-nationwide-for-the-first-time-11654910506"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gasoline prices }}}\uc2 , Mr. Biden has tried to avoid appearing as though he is backtracking on his stance for more oil production. He said Thursday he wouldn't directly ask the Saudis to increase production but instead will make a broader appeal to producers in the region. Some Democrats such as Rep. Adam Schiff (D., Calif.) have said the crown prince doesn't deserve the "dignity" of a presidential visit.\par \par \uc2 And while there were new sanctions against Russia during Mr. Biden's trip over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-u-s-guided-rockets-strengthen-ukraines-hand-against-russia-11656698614"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its war on Ukraine }}}\uc2 , some were unfinished, reflecting divergences among allies, including a proposal to cap Russian oil prices that was discussed at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/g-7-meeting-to-conclude-with-focus-on-china-11656408428"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Group of Seven summit }}}\uc2  in Germany. The path forward on action against Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is expected to grow even more challenging, with immediately available options for punishing Moscow largely exhausted and only more complicated alternatives remaining.\par \par \uc2 The president, however, cast his European trip, which included the \uc2 G-7\uc2  meeting in the Bavarian Alps and a \uc2 North Atlantic Treaty Organization{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-key-allies-close-ranks-against-china-11656591213"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 summit in Madrid }}}\uc2 , as a major success. The summits showcased allies' continued front against Russia and called attention to the economic and military threat of China, he said. An agreement with Turkey also paved the way for Finland and Sweden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/nato-allies-to-focus-on-threats-from-russia-and-beyond-at-summit-11656408633"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to join the alliance }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Putin "thought he could break the trans-Atlantic alliance," Mr. Biden said. "He tried to weaken us, he expected our resolve to fracture. But he's getting exactly what he did not want.\u8230\'20\'26We're more united than ever."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden bristled at a reporter's question Thursday about concerns over the direction of the country, both at home and among allies. "America is better positioned to lead the world than we ever have been," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We have the strongest economy in the world," he said, adding that "the one thing that has been destabilizing is the outrageous behavior of the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2  on overruling not only Roe v. Wade, but essentially challenging the right to privacy."\par \par \uc2 Mr. McConnell criticized Mr. Biden for his comments about the court. "Attacking a core American institution like the Supreme Court from the world stage is below the dignity of the president," he said.\par \par \uc2 U.S. funding for Ukraine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/with-billions-going-to-ukraine-officials-warn-of-potential-for-fraud-waste-11655121601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has reached into the tens of billions }}}\uc2 , with bipartisan support, but a longer war may test that commitment. Mr. Biden vowed Thursday to support Ukraine "as long as it takes."\par \par \uc2 Sen. Dick Durbin (D., Ill.), who was in Madrid for the NATO summit, said Mr. Biden deserved credit for his work in uniting the Western alliance against Mr. Putin, despite the domestic challenges he continues to face.\par \par \uc2 "What he's done is to organize the free world in a way never seen before," he said. "Will it push inflation off the agenda? No, that's going to be an item that we have to cope with directly. But I'm gonna make sure this president gets credit where it's due."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden, who campaigned on restoring U.S. alliances around the world, following the more isolationist views of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , also drew some GOP praise for his efforts in Europe.\par \par \uc2 "The administration has played a key part in what's made this summit a success," Sen. \uc2 Thom Tillis\uc2  (R., N.C.) said in Madrid. "I think that he's focusing on some priorities at home that I may disagree with, but that's not what we're talking about today."\par \par \uc2 Write to Alex Leary at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alex.leary@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alex.leary@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Tarini Parti at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Tarini.Parti@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tarini.Parti@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-faces-fresh-domestic-challenges-after-europe-summits-11656840601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden Faces Fresh Domestic Challenges After Europe Summits }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220703ei730002v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
