\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 New York Lawmakers Firm Up Gun,  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rules Following Supreme Court Decisions; Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  signed legislation on Friday aimed at keeping weapons out of sensitive areas as lawmakers began the process of adding an amendment to the state Constitution to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jimmy Vielkind \par \uc2 756 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 July 2022\par 01:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 New York lawmakers on Friday overhauled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-strikes-down-new-york-law-on-concealed-weapons-11655995248"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the state's gun laws  }}}\uc2  and started the process of amending the state Constitution to cement the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an extraordinary session called in response to recent \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  rulings.\par \par \uc2 The gun bill passed the Democratic-controlled state Senate and Assembly along party lines and Democratic Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  immediately signed it. The bill's provisions take effect Sept. 1.\par \par \uc2 The measure requires concealed-weapon applicants to undergo in-person training and have "the essential character, temperament and judgment necessary to be entrusted with a weapon and to use it only in a manner that does not endanger oneself or others." Applicants must also disclose former and current social-media accounts used during the past three years.\par \par \uc2 New York will also prohibit the possession of weapons in a list of "sensitive places," which include parks, day-care centers, government buildings and Manhattan's Times Square. Possession of a handgun in a private business would be banned unless the business expressly allowed people to carry. Active-duty military and law enforcement personnel, as well as retired police officers, are exempted from the restrictions.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/New-York-State-Rifle-Pistol-Association-v-Bruen-6-23-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Supreme Court's 6-3 decision  }}}\uc2  struck down the state's permitting scheme, which required an applicant to show "proper cause" to receive a weapons permit.\par \par \uc2 The court called into question the permitting regimes in five other states, including California and New Jersey, where lawmakers are considering similar measures. Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Andrea Stewart-Cousins\uc2  , called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-gun-permit-bill-would-require-in-person-training-and-mental-health-records-check-11656507600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the new legislation  }}}\uc2  urgent.\par \par \uc2 New York became the first state to change its gun laws to directly respond to last week's Supreme Court ruling, according to the Giffords Law Center to Prevent Gun Violence, a gun-control group.\par \par \uc2 "If the federal government is incapable of setting the baseline for our rights and protections, then we will do it ourselves," Ms. Stewart-Cousins, a Democrat from Yonkers, said on the chamber floor.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers also approved an Equality Amendment that would prohibit governmental discrimination against people based on a number of categories. That list includes pregnancy outcome, as well as ethnicity, sexual orientation and gender expression.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Hochul embraced the proposal in May after a leak of a draft opinion indicated the Supreme Court could soon overturn Roe v. Wade, which gave women a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . New York legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the landmark 1973 ruling, and updated its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in 2019. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Supreme Court overturned Roe  }}}\uc2  late last month.\par \par \uc2 The governor said on Friday that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights give women full control of their lives and bodies, and that amending the Constitution was "the boldest step we could take."\par \par \uc2 In New York, a constitutional amendment must be approved twice by the Legislature and then in a popular referendum. As such, no amendment could be on the ballot until 2023 at the earliest, and it could take effect no sooner than 2024.\par \par \uc2 California lawmakers this week scheduled a November vote on a constitutional amendment adding a "fundamental right to choose to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." The first time voters are poised to weigh in on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Supreme Court issued its decision will be in Kansas this summer, where there is a proposed amendment to the state Constitution to specify that it doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a right.\par \par \uc2 The New York State Catholic Conference, which represents the state's Roman Catholic bishops, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  language in the Equality Amendment was unfortunate and urged voters and lawmakers to oppose it.\par \par \uc2 "Our elected officials should stop promoting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a woman's best and only choice, and focus instead on true support for women, children and families," said Kristen Curran, the group's director of government relations.\par \par \uc2 Some Senate Republican lawmakers joined Democrats in voting for the Equality Amendment, but every GOP lawmaker opposed the gun bill. State Sen. Andrew Lanza, a Republican from Staten Island, said people would be less safe if responsible gun owners were heavily restricted in where they could carry. He joined legal observers in predicting a lawsuit over the measure.\par \par \uc2 "This is a disgrace\u8212\'20\'14see you in the courts," Mr. Lanza said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jimmy Vielkind at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-lawmakers-firm-up-gun-abortion-rules-following-supreme-court-decisions-11656706664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Lawmakers Firm Up Gun, \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rules Following Supreme Court Decisions  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220701ei710076d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
