\par\par \uc2 Business\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Google\uc2  to Delete  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Clinic Visits From Location History; Move follows Supreme Court decision that eliminated constitutional right to an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and addresses potential of warrants, subpoenas\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patience Haggin \par \uc2 524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 July 2022\par 03:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  said it would begin automatically deleting visits to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics from its users' location history, a move that comes amid growing calls for tech companies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-tech-data-privacy-answers-11656520992"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to ramp up privacy controls }}}\uc2  in the wake of last week's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court decision }}}\uc2  to eliminate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the constitutional right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company, a unit of \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2 ., said physical locations visited by users of \uc2 Google\uc2  products are stored in the location-history setting of their \uc2 Google\uc2  account. That setting is off by default, and location data is only stored for the people who have opted to turn it on, Jen Fitzpatrick, \uc2 Google\uc2 's senior vice president for core systems and experiences, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blog.google/technology/safety-security/protecting-peoples-privacy-on-health-topics/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in a blog post }}}\uc2  Friday.\par \par \uc2 "Some of the places people visit\u8212\'20\'14including medical facilities like counseling centers, domestic violence shelters, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, fertility centers, addiction treatment facilities, weight loss clinics, cosmetic surgery clinics, and others\u8212\'20\'14can be particularly personal," Ms. Fitzpatrick wrote. "Today, we're announcing that if our systems identify that someone has visited one of these places, we will delete these entries from Location History soon after they visit."\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 's new deletion policy will take effect in the coming weeks, Ms. Fitzpatrick wrote.\par \par \uc2 "Last week's ruling on Roe v. Wade was a monumental change for the U.S., and a personal one for so many of us," \uc2 Google\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Sundar Pichai\uc2  wrote in an email to employees in which he mentioned the new privacy steps announced by the company earlier Friday. "We'll work on new ways to strengthen and improve these protections over time."\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 's move addresses one possibility that privacy advocates have flagged in the wake of last week's Supreme Court ruling: the potential that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-wake-of-roe-v-wade-ruling-abortion-providers-confront-new-landscape-11656268445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prosecutors will use warrants or subpoenas }}}\uc2  to demand that tech companies turn over data revealing users who have visited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics. That data could be used to build legal cases against people who are charged with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 having an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in states that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have outlawed the procedure }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We remain committed to protecting our users against improper government demands for data, and we will continue to oppose demands that are overly broad or otherwise legally objectionable," Ms. Fitzpatrick wrote in the blog post. \uc2 Google\uc2  has "a long track record of pushing back on overly broad demands from law enforcement, including objecting to some demands entirely" and publishes data on the government demands it receives, she wrote.\par \par \uc2 In Friday's blog post, \uc2 Google\uc2  also announced updates to make it easier for users to delete their health data from fitness-tracking apps \uc2 Fitbit\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  Fit.\par \par \uc2 "For example, \uc2 Fitbit\uc2  users who have chosen to track their menstrual cycles in the app can currently delete menstruation logs one at a time, and we will be rolling out updates that let users delete multiple logs at once," Ms. Fitzpatrick wrote.\par \par \uc2 Miles Kruppa contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Patience Haggin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:patience.haggin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patience.haggin@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/google-to-delete-visits-to-abortion-clinics-from-users-location-history-11656710884"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Google to Delete \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Clinic Visits From Location History }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220701ei71007vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
