\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ruling Scrambles Voting Calculus for Suburban Women; Most in the key swing demographic oppose the Supreme Court decision, but will it move their votes?\b0\par\par\uc2 By Aaron Zitner in Washington, Scott Calvert in Folson, Pa., and Daniella Cheslow in Woodbridge, Va. \par \uc2 1,786 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 July 2022\par 14:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mary Schultz says the Supreme Court decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to eliminate the constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  left her shaken. "I can't believe they took us back 50 years, that my girls have less rights than I had," she said. One of her two grown daughters cried over the news, she said.\par \par \uc2 Yet, Ms. Schultz, 61, who lives in suburban Atlanta, said she is likely to vote this fall to re-elect Georgia's Republican governor, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , even though he signed a bill that would ban most abortions once fetal cardiac activity is detected, at about six weeks into a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Schultz sees \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a medical procedure best left primarily to a doctor and patient. But she gives Mr. Kemp credit for guiding the state through the Covid-19 crisis and thinks he would manage the state better than his Democratic challenger, \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The nation's suburbs have voted increasingly Democratic in recent years, in part because of women with shifting political allegiances such as Ms. Schultz, who backed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2016 and then \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  four years later. This year, though, concerns over inflation and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/wsj-poll-biden-ukraine-inflation-midterms-11646975533"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disillusionment with Mr. Biden's leadership }}}\uc2  have made these {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-ruling-poses-fresh-midterm-challenges-for-democrats-republicans-11656272277"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swing voters top targets for Republican candidates }}}\uc2 . Democrats are hoping anger over the Supreme Court's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling will override those concerns and prompt them to turn out on Election Day and stick with the Democratic Party. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
