\par \par \uc2 Diana Garber, reading with her grandson in Woodbridge, Va., says the Supreme Court went the right way with its Roe decision. PHOTO: Elizabeth Frantz for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania's race for governor offers one test of power of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate to move voters. Democratic nominee Josh Shapiro, the state's attorney general, says he would protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which state law allows through 24 weeks of pregnancy, and would veto any restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill passed by the GOP-led legislature.\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee, state Sen. \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , sponsored a bill in 2019 that would have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the detection of fetal cardiac activity, as early as six weeks into a pregnancy, and he would make no exceptions for rape or incest. He has also suggested that he might push for a more restrictive law in line with his belief that life begins at conception.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lewis and Gia Ward are both stay-at-home mothers and registered Republicans in the Philadelphia suburb of Ridley Park. Ms. Ward, 30, described herself as "pro-life," while Ms. Lewis, 42, said her views have softened since growing up as "a pro-life Catholic.'' For both, Mr. Mastriano's stances are too restrictive.\par \par \uc2 But where Ms. Lewis said she would back Mr. Mastriano and hope that her vote doesn't lead to tight \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, Ms. Ward said she wasn't sure she could vote for him. "I'm not that far of an extremist to where I think that you should totally outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There should be exceptions for rape and incest,'' she said. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
