\par \par \uc2 Gia Ward says the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views of the Republican gubernatorial candidate in Pennsylvania might be too restrictive for her. PHOTO: Scott Calvert/The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Beyond Pennsylvania, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has already become a factor in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3OXjNSaTFgM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Illinois governor race }}}\uc2  as well as high-profile Senate contests in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-hampshire-tests-abortions-role-in-midterm-elections-11654347601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Hampshire }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yZpyCBfUd54&feature=youtu.be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevada }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uFS-158EjB0&feature=youtu.be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin }}}\uc2  and some battleground House races.\par \par \uc2 Christine Matthews, a pollster who has worked for Republican candidates, cautioned that opinions on the court decision are bound to be shaped by additional developments. The laws in some states will become more restrictive as a result of the ruling, while others won't. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Potential restrictions on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  by medication }}}\uc2 , typically a two-drug procedure, could color women's views of the court ruling, as would certain restrictions on OB-GYN care.\par \par \uc2 "There is a middle ground of women who would call themselves pro-choice but are OK with some restrictions, and what they don't know is what their state is going to do,'' Ms. Matthews said. "Some are very alarmed. Some will say, `Surely my state will be reasonable about this; it isn't the end of the world.' We haven't seen that play out yet.''\par \par \uc2 Johnice Williams, 51, of Anaheim, Calif., said she was "highly disappointed'' in the court ruling but didn't think it would affect the laws in her own state. "Since Roe versus Wade does not affect California, I would rather focus on the efforts against inflation," said Ms. Williams, who is the co-founder of a behavioral-health advocacy group. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
