\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden Supports Exception to Filibuster to Codify Roe v. Wade Into Law; Supreme Court last week overturned Roe v. Wade decision, leaving question of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 's legality to states\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew Restuccia and Ken Thomas \par \uc2 1,525 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 June 2022\par 22:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14President Biden endorsed making an exception to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-filibuster-senate-explained-11656606298"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filibuster rules  }}}\uc2  to pass legislation codifying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  into law, an effort that would face obstacles because of key Democrats' opposition to the move.\par \par \uc2 "The most important thing to be clear about is we have to codify Roe v. Wade into law and the way to do that is to make sure Congress votes to do that," Mr. Biden told reporters during a press conference in Spain. "And if the filibuster gets in the way, it's like voting rights, it should be provided an exception for this\u8230\'20\'26to the filibuster."\par \par \uc2 Changing the filibuster rules of the Senate would allow legislation protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access to pass the chamber with 51 votes rather than the 60 votes usually required for bills to advance. Mr. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-casts-election-law-votes-as-turning-point-for-nation-in-speech-11641897003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had previously backed an exception  }}}\uc2  to filibuster rules to pass long-stalled election bills. It was the first time that the president publicly backed changing the filibuster rules to pass legislation codifying Roe v. Wade into law.\par \par \uc2 The filibuster could be changed with a simple majority vote, but not all Democrats in the 50-50 Senate are on board with such a move, saying it would fundamentally change the nature of the Senate and could backfire if the GOP takes control of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Such legislation could still face roadblocks to passage because Sens. Joe Manchin of West Virginia and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  of Arizona, both moderate Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/senate-democrats-brace-for-defeat-on-elections-bill-filibuster-changes-11642617597"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have said they opposed  }}}\uc2  changing or ending the Senate's filibuster rules. Spokeswomen for both senators said Thursday their positions were unchanged.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last week overturned Roe  }}}\uc2 , the 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the decision, a majority of the court said there was no provision in the Constitution that implicitly protected the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 returning the issue to the states  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/critics-inside-and-outside-white-house-push-biden-for-more-forceful-abortion-response-11656447283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been facing pressure  }}}\uc2  from members of his own party to deliver a more forceful response to the ruling and to lay out more executive actions. Some Biden administration officials said privately earlier this week that they didn't think the president's response had been aggressive enough. White House aides have cautioned that no policies from the executive branch can fill the void left by the court's decision, arguing that Congress must take action.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden said he would support changing the Senate rules not only for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but also to protect the broader right to privacy.\par \par \uc2 "It's a serious, serious problem that the court has thrust upon the United States, not just in terms of the right to choose, but in terms of the right to who you can marry\u8230\'20\'26a whole range of issues related to privacy," he said.\par \par \uc2 In his opinion concurring with the majority, Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  wrote that if the legal underpinnings of Roe v. Wade were wrong, then so were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-v-wade-overturned-supreme-court-11656110804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the underpinnings of other rights  }}}\uc2  not enumerated in the Constitution that the court recognized in recent decades. They include the right of married couples to use contraception, the right to same-sex romantic relationships and, in 2015, the right to same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) and his fellow Republicans oppose changing the filibuster rules for any legislation, and Mr. McConnell has said he wouldn't change the rule if his party takes control of the Senate again. Democrats tried most recently to suspend the filibuster to pass voting-access legislation, which failed when Mr. Manchin and Ms. Sinema joined Republicans in opposition.\par \par \uc2 Mr. McConnell has previously warned Democrats that if they do lift the filibuster, which he said would silence the voices of the millions of Americans represented by GOP senators, "We will make their voices heard in this chamber in ways that are more inconvenient for the majority and this White House than what anybody has seen in living memory."\par \par \uc2 Some moderate Democrats have cautioned that a change in filibuster rules would open the door to Republicans trying to enact nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, or pass other legislation Democrats oppose, with 51 votes if they take control of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Senate Majority Whip Dick Durbin (D., Ill.), who has supported altering the filibuster, sounded skeptical such a change would happen now.\par \par \uc2 "The notion of changing the rules, it is really at the mercy of one or two senators who can make that decision for us," he said Thursday. "That doesn't create the kind of environment\u8230\'20\'26for massive institutional change. This is not the political environment to be looking for that."\par \par \uc2 At the news conference, Mr. Biden said the ruling had been "destabilizing," criticizing "the outrageous behavior of the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2  , in overruling not only Roe v. Wade but essentially challenging the right to privacy."\par \par \uc2 "We have been a leader in the world in terms of personal rights and privacy rights and it is a mistake, in my view, for the Supreme Court to do what it did," he said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) said Democrats were exploring whether to hold another vote on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/senate-to-vote-on-abortion-access-law-as-supreme-court-weighs-roes-fate-11652274305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an existing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bill  }}}\uc2 , which stalled in the Senate after all Republicans and Mr. Manchin opposed it. Mr. Manchin and several moderate Republicans said they could support alternative legislation but rejected the bill because it would have voided some state bans that were allowed under previous high court rulings, and contained what critics saw as wording that would make it too easy to obtain a late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mrs. Pelosi also backed doing away with the filibuster, while acknowledging the Senate doesn't currently have the votes to take such a step.\par \par \uc2 She said the party was also looking into measures to protect personal data stored in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-period-tracker-apps-treat-your-data-and-what-that-means-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11655561595"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 health apps used to track menstrual cycles  }}}\uc2 . She said the House could also pursue legislation ensuring Americans have the right to travel freely\u8212\'20\'14essentially heading off any state attempts to criminalize travel for the purpose of getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She also said the House could pursue measures to codify the legality of same-sex marriage and access to contraception.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has been considering a number of steps that it could take in response to the ruling. Mr. Biden said he would meet Friday with a group of Democratic governors to discuss the ruling and options the federal government could take.\par \par \uc2 The meeting will include Govs. \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  of North Carolina, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  of New York, \uc2 Jared Polis\uc2  of Colorado and \uc2 Michelle Lujan Grisham\uc2  of New Mexico, according to a person familiar with the plan.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department has said it would take steps to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, saying women should be able to travel to another state for the procedure. It has also said it would protect access to contraception and medications used to treat miscarriages.\par \par \uc2 A group of nearly three dozen Senate Democrats recently sent a letter to Mr. Biden urging him to "fight back and lead a national response" to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling. The letter didn't propose specific measures. The Senate in May voted on a bill that would provide access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until a fetus is viable, usually around 23 to 24 weeks. It failed in a 49-51 vote.\par \par \uc2 If Congress were to pass nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections similar to those found in Roe v. Wade, such legislation could face a challenging court battle, legal observers said.\par \par \uc2 In providing for federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, lawmakers would likely point to their authority to regulate interstate commerce, on the grounds that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions affect the availability and cost of the procedure across the country, women are traveling across state lines to obtain abortions and companies ship pills across state lines, among other issues. But the Supreme Court in recent times has taken a narrower view of the commerce power than in previous eras, making the survival of new legislation uncertain.\par \par \uc2 "Sometimes the court will uphold broad laws that are based on commerce, sometimes they'll strike them down," said Linda McClain, a law professor at \uc2 Boston University\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 On the day Mr. Biden announced his change on the filibuster, protesters staging a sit-in near the Supreme Court called for leaders to be more aggressive in supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Katie Donnelly, a pediatrician who joined the protest, said her biggest concern is that in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal, "we could lose the lives of pregnant women." She added, "I would really like to see our elected officials do something bold in this moment."\par \par \uc2 Nadine Seiler, another protester, voiced frustration toward Democrats. "We do our work by voting for them and they do nothing for us when they get in there," Ms. Seiler said.\par \par \uc2 Natalie Andrews, Teresa Mettela and Laura Kusisto contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrew Restuccia at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:andrew.restuccia@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 andrew.restuccia@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Ken Thomas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:ken.thomas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ken.thomas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Ken Thomas at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-says-he-supports-exception-to-filibuster-to-codify-roe-v-wade-into-law-11656596123"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden Supports Exception to Filibuster to Codify Roe v. Wade Into Law  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220630ei6u002xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
