\par \par \uc2 Healthcare providers will need to be prepared and train staff on how to respond if they receive a demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  information. PHOTO: Taylor Glascock for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Some of those laws ban procuring the means of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in addition to performing one, according to Laurie Sobel , an associate director at Kaiser. At least two states, Kentucky and Louisiana, also criminalize abetting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she said. None of the laws specifically spell out any requirements for healthcare providers to release patient information, Ms. Sobel said, but she said such data could be sought as part of criminal investigations under the laws.\par \par \uc2 Some doctors in states with antiabortion statutes say they are worried. Emily Briggs, a family physician in New Braunfels, Texas, whose practice includes obstetrics, said she and colleagues are discussing how they can protect healthcare information and their trusting connection with their patients.\par \par \uc2 "My nightmare is my patients' private information not remaining private," she said. "When we lose that privacy, we have the potential to lose that trust."\par \par \uc2 HIPAA doesn't require healthcare entities to disclose information to law-enforcement and courts, said Iliana Peters, an attorney with law firm Polsinelli PC. It allows such disclosures if state law requires them. Patients don't necessarily get notice that their data have been released under those circumstances.\par \par \uc2 The new guidance emphasizes the limits on when healthcare providers are allowed to share information, she said, and it clarifies existing rules.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How should employers and doctors approach reproductive care in a post-Roe era? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "There has to be a legal requirement for the disclosure," she said, and typically a document such as a court order or court-approved subpoena or warrant, rather than simply a request from a local prosecutor or police department. Ms. Peters and other attorneys said they were advising healthcare providers to be prepared and train staff in how to respond if they get a demand for information disclosure.\par \par \uc2 Partly because of the gray areas in the intersection of the newly effective state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws and privacy rules, even with the new federal guidelines, the response of healthcare companies will make a difference, experts said.\par \par \uc2 "It's going to depend on whether the institution wants to take that to court, or wants to be compliant," said Mark Rothstein, a professor at the \uc2 University of Louisville\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 One question is whether HIPAA would allow an employee of a doctor's office, hospital or other healthcare entity to disclose the potential violation of an antiabortion statute to a law-enforcement entity, even without a legally sanctioned demand, such as a subpoena, said Mr. Nahra, the \uc2 WilmerHale\uc2  attorney.\par \par \uc2 The new guidelines say such disclosures, to be allowed under HIPAA, would have to come in very specific circumstances, such as a state law specifically requiring them.\par \par \uc2 "There's enough wiggle room in these rules that if someone wants to disclose, they could probably find a way to do that," Mr. Nahra said. But, he said, the new guidance is designed to make healthcare providers think twice about doing so.\par \par \uc2 Write to Anna Wilde Mathews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:anna.mathews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anna.mathews@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-administration-releases-new-hipaa-guidelines-in-light-of-abortion-ruling-11656540873"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ruling Prompts Privacy Guidelines From Biden Administration  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220629ei6t006va\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
