\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 New  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Lawsuits Continue in States Cutting Access; Providers bring legal claims in Ohio and West Virginia, while a judge weighs ban in Kentucky\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 625 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2022\par 23:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 State court battles over the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access continued to expand Wednesday, as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in Ohio and West Virginia filed legal challenges to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state laws curtailing access to the procedure }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups and local providers asked the state Supreme Court to block a law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after around six weeks of pregnancy that went into effect on Friday, shortly after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the U.S. Supreme Court overruled Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  and ended a half-century of protections for a woman's right to choose an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The groups argue that the six-week ban violates state constitutional protections for privacy and equal protection.\par \par \uc2 One of the providers, Planned Parenthood Southwest Ohio Region, said it has had to cancel over 600 patient appointments since the law took effect. Several patients have threatened to commit suicide and one said she would attempt to terminate her pregnancy by drinking bleach, according to the legal complaint.\par \par \uc2 Ohio Attorney General \uc2 Dave Yost\uc2 , a Republican, criticized the plaintiffs for trying to take their case directly to the state's highest court and said their legal claims are without support. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not in the Ohio Constitution," Mr. Yost said.\par \par \uc2 While the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has removed protections under the U.S. Constitution }}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , states have their own constitutions and state laws to interpret on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Since Friday's high court ruling, abortions are now largely unavailable in about a dozen states, either because of new bans or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/uncertainty-over-abortion-access-grows-after-supreme-court-ruling-11656357143"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal uncertainty }}}\uc2 . Another half dozen or more states could ban or restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming days and weeks.\par \par \uc2 In West Virginia, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and advocates filed a lawsuit in state court challenging a law dating back to the 1800s that has created uncertainty over whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in the state, causing providers to stop offering the procedure. The law has been dormant since Roe was decided in 1973 but has never been explicitly repealed.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs argue the law conflicts with more modern regulations governing legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in West Virginia, adding that state law precludes enforcing criminal laws that have been dormant for an extended period.\par \par \uc2 "The Criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ban is a relic of a bygone era\u8212\'20\'14one fundamentally out of step not only with the way pregnant people in West Virginia approach their pregnancies today, but also with the West Virginia Code itself," the plaintiffs said in the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for West Virginia Attorney General Patrick Morrisey, a Republican, said the office would review the lawsuit. Mr. Morrisey will send a legal opinion to the state's legislature Thursday about how it can proceed following the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 's decision, his office said.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere Wednesday, a state judge in Kentucky heard arguments from local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers who are seeking a temporary block of a state law that would ban many or most abortions. A decision is expected in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 Judges in Louisiana, Texas and Utah already have blocked state officials from enforcing new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  prohibitions, at least temporarily, until additional legal proceedings can take place.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana Attorney General \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2  sent a letter to the state's medical society on Wednesday saying he doesn't believe the judge's order immunizes medical providers from criminal liability if they perform abortions. "Subject to certain exceptions, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a criminal offense in the State of Louisiana, and it has been since last Friday," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-abortion-lawsuits-continue-in-states-cutting-access-11656543956"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Lawsuits Continue in States Cutting Access 