\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Uncertainty Over  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access Grows After Supreme Court Ruling; Louisiana  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban is halted for now by a state judge, while other mostly Republican-led states move forward with prohibitions\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto, Jennifer Calfas and Deanna Paul \par \uc2 1,494 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2022\par 01:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Regions across the U.S. faced an uncertain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  landscape on Monday, as some states moved to enforce new restrictions, others remained in limbo, and fresh legal battles began to take shape after the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrew constitutional protections for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access has continued to evolve almost by the hour since the court on Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruled Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2 , the 1973 decision that for almost half a century {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protected a woman's right  }}}\uc2  to choose an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Abortions are now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largely unavailable in about a dozen states  }}}\uc2 , either because of new bans or legal uncertainty, while another half dozen or more states could ban or restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming days and weeks.\par \par \uc2 After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/key-excerpts-from-supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-overturning-roe-v-wade-11656092052"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the high court's ruling  }}}\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights litigants have been turning quickly to state courts, filing at least six lawsuits that could help determine whether and how quickly conservative-leaning states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can move to curtail access  }}}\uc2  to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Several early post-Roe legal developments came Monday, with state judges in Louisiana and Utah issuing restraining orders that temporarily blocked \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in those states, while a federal judge cleared the way for South Carolina to enforce a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Judge Robin Giarrusso in New Orleans issued the Louisiana order in response to a lawsuit filed by Hope Medical Group for Women, a reproductive healthcare provider in Shreveport, and Medical Students for Choice. The groups said the state has three different laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-prepare-to-quickly-implement-abortion-trigger-laws-11655385028"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 triggering bans on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , causing significant confusion over which one is in effect, what the penalties are and what exceptions are available.\par \par \uc2 "We're in uncharted territory with respect to these laws," said Joanna Wright of Boies Schiller Flexner LLP, an attorney for the plaintiffs.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana has an explicit provision in its state constitution specifying it doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A hearing in the case is set for early July. In light of the judge's order, Hope Medical Group for Women will resume appointments Tuesday morning, said Kathaleen Pittman, the clinic's administrator.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Gov. \uc2 John Bel Edwards\uc2  , a Democrat who opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said, "This challenge to Louisiana's trigger law was completely expected. For quite some time, our law has clearly stated that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be outlawed in Louisiana if Roe v. Wade was overturned."\par \par \uc2 A Utah judge later on Monday blocked that state's 2020 law triggering a ban on all abortions except in the case of rape, incest or a medical emergency. Karrie Galloway, president and chief executive of Planned Parenthood Association of Utah, which challenged the ban, said the order would allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to resume in the state.\par \par \uc2 Judge Andrew Stone said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/22071304-utahtro062722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood's lawsuit  }}}\uc2  "raised serious constitutional issues" under state law "which are fair grounds for litigation." \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and patients would be irreparably harmed by the new law, clinic personnel would risk felony prosecution and "women in Utah will lack safe local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services," he said.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Utah Attorney General \uc2 Sean Reyes\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Since the Supreme Court ruling, bans on many or most abortions have taken effect in states including Alabama, Arkansas, Kentucky, Missouri, Ohio and South Dakota. Other states, including Oklahoma and Texas, had moved to ban most abortions even before the decision.\par \par \uc2 Where \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Is Legal and Where It Loses Protections Without Roe v. Wade\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-carolina-passes-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-legislation-11613599308"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina's six-week ban  }}}\uc2  that a judge allowed to go into effect Monday was passed last year. The law includes exceptions in cases of life-threatening medical emergencies, as well as exceptions for rape or incest before 20 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 "Our state is now carrying out a government's most sacred and fundamental duty, protecting life," said South Carolina Attorney General Alan Wilson.\par \par \uc2 Jenny Black, president and CEO of Planned Parenthood South Atlantic, said its local clinics would remain open and provide abortions in compliance with the law. "This fight is far from over," she said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and rights groups filed lawsuits in Kentucky, Mississippi and Idaho on Monday seeking to block \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans from taking effect, arguing that access to the procedure is protected by their respective state constitutions.\par \par \uc2 Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers also filed a lawsuit Monday, citing confusion over the state law on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The state has three different sets of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  prohibitions in play and the providers say that uncertainty about what laws are in effect has forced them to stop providing abortions.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-wake-of-roe-v-wade-ruling-abortion-providers-confront-new-landscape-11656268445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confusion over \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions  }}}\uc2  has prompted clinics in states such as Arizona and Wisconsin to stop appointments. Providers in Wisconsin canceled dozens of appointments Friday and Saturday, expecting the state's 1849 law banning most abortions could now be enforced.\par \par \uc2 "We really had to think about what the risks were or are for continuing to provide," said Michelle Velasquez, director of legal advocacy and services at Planned Parenthood of Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Gov. \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  , a Democrat, on Monday said he would offer clemency to doctors if they were prosecuted under the state's 1849 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, but also said it could be legally dangerous for \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  to resume abortions in the state.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Evers said he would speak to local district attorneys and to Wisconsin's attorney general about the path forward. "The details are still in progress," he said of the clemency proposal.\par \par \uc2 Some Republican state lawmakers, meanwhile, have indicated they believed the 173-year-old law is now in effect.\par \par \uc2 "Unless there is evidence indicating that those who came before us made an error, I will support Wisconsin's current law that protects the right to Life, \uc2 Liberty\uc2  , and the pursuit of Happiness for every unborn child," GOP state Sen. Chris Kapenga said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 In Mississippi, state Attorney General Lynn Fitch, a Republican, took steps Monday that allowed the state's trigger law to take effect in 10 days. Passed in 2007, that law bans most abortions except in cases of life-threatening medical emergencies or rape that has been reported to law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Mississippi was at the center of the Supreme Court's ruling last week in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/catch-up-on-wsj-s-coverage-of-the-mississippi-abortion-case-6kJe8LBmXySQIhqdy6l8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs vs. Jackson Women's Health Organization  }}}\uc2 , a case that focused on a ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy. When that litigation began, the state was seeking more latitude to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability. By the time it argued the case at the high court, the state made broader arguments and pushed for the elimination of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-opponents-consider-how-far-to-press-after-end-of-roe-v-wade-11656273349"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Antiabortion groups celebrated the move  }}}\uc2  to enforce bans in Mississippi and other states, saying they are preparing to step up and provide services to women in those places. "Lives are being saved immediately by ensuring that the people have a voice," said SBA Pro-Life America President Marjorie Dannenfelser.\par \par \uc2 Jackson Women's Health Organization, the state's only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, vowed to continue providing abortions for as long as possible.\par \par \uc2 The facility is expecting July 7 to be its last day of procedures, but will remain open, answering any calls or doing referrals and other services that are legally possible, said Diane Derzis, the clinic's owner. Meanwhile, the organization is preparing to open a new location in Las Cruces, N.M., in two weeks, Ms. Derzis said.\par \par \uc2 "This is the way it's going to be from now on," Ms. Derzis said. "None of us really know the answers yet. We're all feeling our way through this."\par \par \uc2 California's legislature passed a measure Monday that will allow voters in November to approve or reject a constitutional amendment guaranteeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state. The bill passed the Democratic-controlled state senate and assembly with more than the two-third majority needed and was supported by Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  . If approved by a majority of voters in the overwhelmingly Democratic state, it would add language to the California constitution guaranteeing individuals a "fundamental right to choose to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and their fundamental right to choose or refuse contraceptives."\par \par \uc2 In Washington, D.C., Democratic lawmakers previewed possible plans. In a letter to Democratic colleagues, House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) said she was looking at pursuing legislation that would protect women's personal data stored in \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  apps and make clear that Americans have the right to travel freely across state lines. She also said the House could again bring up a bill that aims to solidify women's access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That bill passed the House but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-bill-set-to-be-blocked-in-senate-11646087265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to advance in the Senate  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Christine Mai-Duc and Austen Hufford contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2 , Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Deanna Paul at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:deanna.paul@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deanna.paul@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Deanna Paul at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/uncertainty-over-abortion-access-grows-after-supreme-court-ruling-11656357143"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uncertainty Over \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Access Grows After Supreme Court Ruling  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220627ei6r004ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
