\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Democrats Weigh New  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Legislation After Roe v. Wade Overturned; Pelosi says lawmakers are looking at health apps, protecting women's freedom to travel\b0\par\par\uc2 By Siobhan Hughes \par \uc2 981 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2022\par 13:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Democrats were wrestling with where to focus their legislative response to the Supreme Court ruling ending federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, after Republicans stymied the party's previous attempts to enact a law guaranteeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Democrats\u8212\'20\'14who control both chambers of Congress and the White House\u8212\'20\'14have tried twice this session to pass the Women's Health Protection Act, which would establish a nationwide right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability, usually around 23 to 24 weeks. But versions of the bill drew too little support to clear the Senate, and some party lawmakers made clear they are now considering other legislation as well.\par \par \uc2 As some states moved to enforce new bans and restrictions, House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) said in a letter to colleagues Monday that the Democratic caucus was exploring whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-bill-set-to-be-blocked-in-senate-11646087265"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to hold another vote  }}}\uc2 on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill. She said the party was also looking into measures to protect personal data stored in health apps, which include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/period-tracker-apps-aim-for-anonymity-following-roe-v-wade-decision-11656202089"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 smartphone apps that some women use  }}}\uc2  to track their menstrual cycles and she said could potentially be used by prosecutors in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be criminalized.\par \par \uc2 She wrote that any legislation would make it clear that Americans have the right to travel freely throughout the country\u8212\'20\'14essentially heading off any state attempts to criminalize travel for the purpose of getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She said the House may take steps to try to codify other court rulings related to access to contraception, in-vitro fertilization and same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 Any legislation will need to overcome roadblocks in the 50-50 Senate, where 60 votes are needed to advance most bills. Some Democrats have sought to make the threshold for passing legislation a simple majority, but such a change is seen as unlikely after two Democrats, Sens. Joe Manchin of West Virginia and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  of Arizona, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/senate-democrats-brace-for-defeat-on-elections-bill-filibuster-changes-11642617597"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled it out earlier this year  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -access measures passed by the House to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access drew broad opposition from Republicans. The bill also raised the hackles of a small group of moderate Republicans and one Democrat in part because the bill would have voided some state bans that were allowed under previous high court rulings, and contained what critics saw as wording that would make it too easy to obtain a late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How should Congress respond to the Supreme Court's reversal of Roe v. Wade? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The next big public focal points are the week that the Senate returns from the July 4 recess, when committees will hold hearings. The \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  has scheduled a hearing for July 12, and the Senate Health, Education Labor and Pensions Committee plans a July 13 hearing.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  (D., Wash.), the Senate Democrats' top voice on the subject, said she has been pushing President Biden for a federal response and an action plan for weeks.\par \par \uc2 "This truly is an all-hands-on-deck moment to protect the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and I will keep pushing for the action that is needed right now," she said on social media.\par \par \uc2 She had led a group of nearly three dozen Senate Democrats in a letter to Mr. Biden, saying that "you have the power to fight back and lead a national response to this devastating decision." The letter said the administration should take "every step available" to preserve access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but didn't propose specific measures.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Mr. Biden said that the only way to secure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access was for Congress to restore the protections of Roe v. Wade as federal law. He said that if Congress lacked the votes to do so now, then voters needed to elect lawmakers who would enact \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 He said the administration would seek to protect the basic right to travel for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to use federally approved drugs to end early pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Tim Kaine (D., Va.) has been working with Sen. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  (R., Maine) on legislation that would codify the rights to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  recognized in the now-defunct 1973 Roe v. Wade decision and related rulings. But that bill hasn't been introduced in the Senate, and even if it could draw the support of the entire Democratic caucus, it would face an uphill road in winning over 10 Senate Republicans.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Sen. Elizabeth Warren (D., Mass.) told ABC's "This Week" that some strategies Mr. Biden could employ would include allow abortions to be provided on federal lands in states where new restrictions are enacted. Influential progressive Rep. \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (D., N.Y.) also backed setting up clinics on federal lands and pressed Democrats to take action on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the court, calling for the number of justices to be expanded to counter its conservative wing, among other steps.\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said on CNN on Monday that the proposal to allow abortions on federal lands wasn't being discussed in the White House, and she declined to say if she would support eliminating the filibuster, saying the votes weren't there.\par \par \uc2 Both Ms. Harris and Mr. Biden had supported carving out an exception to the Senate's 60-vote filibuster rule to advance a voting-rights bill, but neither has backed a similar step regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills, "neither side of this issue has come anywhere close to having 60 votes," Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky) told the Rotary Club of Florence on Monday. "So I think this is likely to all be litigated out, dealt with in the various states around the country through the democratic process."\par \par \uc2 Write to Siobhan Hughes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:siobhan.hughes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 siobhan.hughes@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-weigh-new-legislation-in-response-to-abortion-ruling-11656424248"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats Weigh New \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Legislation After Roe v. Wade Overturned  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220628ei6s0030d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
