\par\par \uc2 Business\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 CVS, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and Rite Aid Limit Purchases of Plan B Pills After Surge in Demand; Retailers' websites show the emergency contraceptive in short supply after Supreme Court's  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  decision\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sharon Terlep \par \uc2 567 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2022\par 16:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Some of the nation's biggest retailers are rationing over-the-counter emergency contraceptive pills as demand spikes following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Supreme Court ruling }}}\uc2  overturning a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CVS Health Corp\uc2 ., \uc2 Walmart Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 Rite Aid Corp\uc2 . were limiting purchases of the pills, which were in short supply or out of stock on major retailer websites. CVS and \uc2 Rite Aid\uc2  were limiting purchases to three, while \uc2 Walmart\uc2  was limiting orders to 10.\par \par \uc2 A CVS spokesman said that the company has implemented temporary purchase limits to ensure equitable access and that it has ample supply of the pills in stores and online. A \uc2 Walmart\uc2  spokeswoman said the company limits purchases on many items and that limits can change as demand fluctuates. \uc2 Rite Aid\uc2  said it was limiting purchases of the pills both online and in stores due to increased demand.\par \par \uc2 Walgreens Boots Alliance Inc\uc2 ., which also had a purchase limit on its website, said that the restriction was an error and that it would soon be corrected. A spokesman said the company is investigating the situation.\par \par \uc2 The pills are often referred to and sold under the Plan B brand without a prescription. Also called morning-after pills, they are designed to be taken up to three days after unprotected sex. The medication mainly works by preventing ovulation and, failing that, may stop a fertilized egg from attaching to the uterus.\par \par \uc2 Plan B pills are different from medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also known as plan C, which requires a prescription and involves the administration of different pills to terminate a pregnancy. In the U.S., medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been approved by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  for up to 10 weeks of pregnancy. Two medications\u8212\'20\'14mifepristone and misoprostol\u8212\'20\'14are typically used in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  regimen }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Several companies make versions of Plan B that range in cost from $10 to more than $50. On Monday, the cheapest option available from major retailers' websites was a pill for $35. There are three types of emergency contraceptive pills: progestin-only pills like levonorgestrel (sold under the brand name Plan B, among others), ulipristal (brand name Ella) and combined emergency contraception pills that consist of ethinyl estradiol and levonorgestrel. The latter two types require prescriptions.\par \par \uc2 Plan B One-Step, the top-selling emergency contraceptive, is owned by a pair of private-equity firms, \uc2 Kelso & Co\uc2 . and Juggernaut Capital Partners. \uc2 Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/foundation-consumer-healthcare-buys-plan-b-one-step-from-teva-1510768336"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sold the brand in 2017 }}}\uc2  to the investors as part of a move to shed its women's health business. Representatives from the firms didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 In the days following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Friday's court decision }}}\uc2 , social media filled with comments either encouraging or dissuading people to stock up on the contraceptive. Some users posted that they were buying as many as possible; others argued against stockpiling for fear it would cut off access to people with an immediate need.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood on Monday advised against stockpiling emergency contraceptives as they have limited shelf life and because hoarding supplies could limit access for women who have an immediate need.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sharon Terlep at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:sharon.terlep@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sharon.terlep@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/cvs-walmart-limit-purchases-of-plan-b-pills-after-surge-in-demand-11656358819"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CVS, Walmart and Rite Aid Limit Purchases of Plan B Pills After Surge in Demand  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220627ei6r004h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
