\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 State Judges Are in Spotlight After Supreme Court Overrules Roe v. Wade; Texas judge puts century-old  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban on hold for now, following similar court orders in Louisiana and Utah\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto, Jennifer Calfas and Deanna Paul \par \uc2 1,080 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2022\par 22:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Days after the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruled Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , the legal spotlight is shifting to state courts, where judges are on the front lines in determining the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The latest developments came Tuesday when a judge in Houston blocked enforcement of a century-old Texas law that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Judges in Utah and Louisiana on Monday also put those states' \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans on hold for now. And in Wisconsin, Attorney General \uc2 Josh Kaul\uc2 , a Democrat, filed a lawsuit Tuesday challenging a state law from 1849 banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The number of state-level legal battles is expected to continue to grow. While the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court has removed protections }}}\uc2  under the U.S. Constitution for a woman's right to choose an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , states have their own constitutions and state laws to interpret on the issue.\par \par \uc2 "Most people think the U.S. Constitution is the final word on our individual rights but it is not," said Stefanie Lindquist, a law and political-science professor at \uc2 Arizona State University\uc2 . "Pro-choice plaintiffs are now looking to state constitutions as a source of individual rights, including the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Since Friday's Supreme Court ruling, abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are now largely unavailable }}}\uc2 in about a dozen states, either because of new bans or legal uncertainty. Another half dozen or more states could ban or restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming days and weeks.\par \par \uc2 share your thoughts\par \par \uc2 What impact will the Supreme Court ruling have on your state? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The Texas court order came in response to a lawsuit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers filed Monday. The state has three different sets of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  prohibitions in play and the providers said that uncertainty about what laws are in effect has forced them to stop providing abortions.\par \par \uc2 Judge Christine Weems issued a temporary restraining order that prevents enforcement of the pre-Roe ban against the providers through July 12, when she has scheduled another court hearing. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/22072139-texastro062822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The judge found }}}\uc2  that the pre-Roe ban had been repealed and "may not be enforced consistent with the due process guaranteed by the Texas constitution."\par \par \uc2 Unlike in the federal judiciary, where judges are appointed, many states hold elections to select at least some of their judges. Ms. Weems, a Democrat, is running for re-election this year for her seat in Harris County.\par \par \uc2 Even without the ban, Texas's prohibition on nearly all abortions after six weeks of pregnancy is still in place. The law, which has stood up to legal challenges over the past year, took effect in September, It uses a novel enforcement strategy that allows members of the public to file lawsuits seeking damages against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and those who assist them.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  State-by-State\par \par \uc2 Mapping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access after the Supreme Court decision\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Is Legal and Where It Loses Protections Without Roe v. Wade }}}\par \par \uc2 After Tuesday's court order, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider Whole Woman's Health started contacting patients on waiting lists to schedule appointments for abortions in the early weeks of pregnancy, as well as staff and providers to return to the clinics.\par \par \uc2 "We will resume services in our 4 Texas clinics and help as many people as soon as possible," said \uc2 Amy Hagstrom Miller\uc2 , president and chief executive of Whole Woman's Health.\par \par \uc2 Texas Republican Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  said he would appeal the decision. "The judge's decision is wrong," he said in a tweet. "I'm immediately appealing. I'll ensure we have all the legal tools to keep TX pro-life!"\par \par \uc2 Despite the flurry of new legal activity and some initial successes, groups challenging \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions face difficult legal prospects in some states.\par \par \uc2 State courts "are a critical component of ensuring protections at the state level but the courts aren't going to be the ones to save us. That is the hard truth that everyone is facing," said \uc2 Jessica Arons\uc2 , a lawyer with \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court overruled Roe in a case from Mississippi, Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization. Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , writing for himself and four other justices, said the court in 1973 had been egregiously wrong in reading a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the Constitution.\par \par \uc2 Aside from prompting new state litigation, the ruling is upending decisions in yearslong battles in federal courts, where plaintiffs had relied on Roe and later high-court precedents to strike down state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. The latest came Tuesday when a federal appeals court allowed enforcement of a Tennessee law banning most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy. The law had been blocked in court since 2020. The state has a separate law banning all abortions that is set to take effect in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Tennessee has an amendment in its state constitution specifying that it doesn't protect a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups likely have few legal avenues remaining to challenge the state's bans.\par \par \uc2 Tennessee GOP Gov. Bill Lee said Tuesday's development marks "another significant protection for unborn children in our state."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kaul of Wisconsin argued in his lawsuit that the state's 1849 law on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  conflicts with more recent statutes that provide specific parameters for when doctors can lawfully perform the procedure. "Wisconsin \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers cannot be held to two sets of diametrically opposed laws, and the Wisconsin people deserve clarity," he said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kaul and the state's Gov. \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  are both Democrats, while both chambers of Wisconsin's legislature are controlled by Republicans. That has made it difficult for the state to pass new legislation clarifying questions around the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 Speaker \uc2 Robin Vos\uc2 , a Republican legislative leader who was among the named defendants in the lawsuit, said that Messrs. Kaul and Evers wanted to break the law instead of work with the legislature.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't health care," he said Tuesday. "For the governor and attorney general to try and use the courts to enact law is just as wrong as the original Roe v. Wade decision."\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Deanna Paul at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:deanna.paul@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deanna.paul@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-judges-are-in-spotlight-after-supreme-court-overrules-roe-v-wade-11656444559"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State Judges Are in Spotlight After Supreme Court Overrules Roe v. Wade }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220628ei6s005xx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
