\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Critics Inside and Outside White House Push Biden for More Forceful  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Response; Administration has struggled to come up with a detailed plan and messaging strategy, with progressives pushing for more action and Harris asking for more specifics\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Thomas, Tarini Parti and Andrew Restuccia \par \uc2 1,836 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2022\par 23:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Democrats, including some Biden administration officials, are growing frustrated with President Biden for not mounting a more forceful response to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's decision to overturn \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  protections }}}\uc2 , as the party works to turn the ruling into a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-move-abortion-fight-to-midterm-elections-after-supreme-court-ruling-11656098522"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallying cry ahead of the midterm elections }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The day after the Supreme Court struck down Roe v. Wade, Mr. Biden left for a five-day trip to Europe to attend two global summits. In his absence, the administration has struggled to come up with a detailed plan and messaging strategy, with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and other officials asking for more specificity, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 With roughly half of U.S. states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning, or moving to ban, many or most abortions }}}\uc2 , Democrats are pressuring the White House to take more dramatic steps to counter the decision.\par \par \uc2 Though he gave a forceful speech condemning the ruling the day it was issued, Mr. Biden hasn't publicly spoken about the issue during his foreign trip, even as several of the \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  leaders he was meeting with in the Bavarian Alps released statements criticizing the ruling.\par \par \uc2 The president vowed before leaving the country that the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/biden-calls-abortion-ruling-tragic-error--4ATIrLswM0hg5i5ctzNT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will do everything in its power to offer protections }}}\uc2  to women in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be outlawed. And he pointed to the fall elections as the chance for voters to be the final arbiter. "This is not over," he said.\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Health and Human Services Secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  said, "We want to make it clear we will protect a women's right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care services," adding, "There are women whose health could be in jeopardy if they don't know what their rights are."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Becerra, in a press conference Tuesday, said the agency will make sure its \uc2 Office for Civil Rights\uc2  safeguards patient privacy and nondiscrimination protections for patients who seek reproductive healthcare. He said the \uc2 HHS\uc2  will also work with the Justice Department and U.S. Attorney General to make sure states can't ban medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite those moves, some Democrats say more is needed. A group of Democratic lawmakers, including Sens. Elizabeth Warren of Massachusetts and Tina Smith of Minnesota, have urged Mr. Biden to declare a public health emergency to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services. The lawmakers say declaring such an emergency would make it easier for the administration to boost resources for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  and deal with a potential surge of abortions in some places.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (D., N.Y.) has called for restraining judicial review by the courts, placing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics on federal lands, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/abortion-ruling-revives-liberal-push-to-overhaul-court-ypDY5gkBIdXpqx7IFrql"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanding the court }}}\uc2  and changing the so-called filibuster rules of the Senate, which would allow legislation protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access to pass the chamber with 51 votes rather than the 60 votes usually required for bills to advance. A group of Black women in the House, led by Reps. \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\uc2  of Massachusetts and Barbara Lee of California, asked Mr. Biden to "use any and all executive authorities" to respond to the ruling. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
