\par\par \uc2 Free Expression\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Urge to Overreach Outlives Roe v. Wade; Critics of the Supreme Court take to the streets in rage, while  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  opponents push draconian restrictions.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerard Baker \par \uc2 902 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2022\par 22:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 There may be no better indication of the jurisprudential soundness of the Supreme Court's decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization than the intellectual poverty of the response from its opponents.\par \par \uc2 "F\u8212\'20\'14 you, Supreme Court!" was the thoughtful {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailymail.co.uk/tvshowbiz/article-10955725/F-Supreme-Court-Janelle-Mon-e-blunt-words-coarse-sign-language-high-court.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 response}}}\uc2  from celebrities who can be relied on at moments like these to ululate performatively. We don't expect much constitutional wisdom from pop singers and film stars. But surely we have a right to demand from those who govern us a more cogent rebuttal, some direct effort to pick apart the legal reasoning that forms the basis for a judicial opinion they so furiously denounce.\par \par \uc2 Instead the percussive reaction from the expensively educated politicians who seek to persuade us was barely more articulate than the expletive-laden shrieks from entertainment stages.\par \par \uc2 None of them actually addressed the central plank of Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/19-1392_6j37.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opinion}}}\uc2 : that in discovering a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  where none existed, Roe v. Wade (1973) and then Planned Parenthood v. Casey (1992), its reaffirming successor, represented an "abuse of judicial authority" and that it was "time to heed the Constitution and return the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the people's elected representatives."\par \par \uc2 They sought rather to hype the supposed consequences of the decision and to drown its legal reasoning in rhetorical excess, misrepresentation and\u8212\'20\'14now obligatory\u8212\'20\'14threats.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Juris Doctor, a man we know for sure is familiar with the case against Roe because he used to argue it, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2022/06/24/remarks-by-president-biden-on-the-supreme-court-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the decision had taken the country on an "extreme and dangerous path" and "the health and life of women across this nation are now at risk."\par \par \uc2 Sen. Elizabeth Warren, a former Harvard law professor, brought her customary cool, rational approach to thorny constitutional issues. She simply {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/supreme-court-set-torch-legitimacy-roe-reversal-elizabeth/story?id=85706276"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asserted}}}\uc2  that the decision somehow invalidated the court itself. The justices had "burned whatever legitimacy they may still have had." With this ruling, "they just took the last of it and set a torch to it."\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , a former attorney general of the most populous state in the union, could have seized the opportunity to shed a reputation for world-beating vacuity and given us a refutation of the majority's opinion. Instead, true to form, she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2022/06/24/remarks-by-vice-president-harris-on-the-supreme-court-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered}}}\uc2  only a tired cliche mired in its own banality: "Millions of women in America will go to bed tonight without access to the healthcare and reproductive care that they had this morning."\par \par \uc2 Demagogues gonna demagogue. We know. But if the Dobbs decision were so palpably wrong, you'd think between them these great legal minds would be able to come up with at least one argument against it that amounted to something other than an exercise in emotional blackmail.\par \par \uc2 The left's rhetorical fury is itself an unacknowledged nod in the direction of the court's own reasoning: that laws on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as morally tortuous a subject as any in modern life, should be decided not by judges making up the bioethics of trimesters, viability and personhood as they go along, but by the people. Progressives should now know what conservatives have known for a long time: that the burden is on them to convince voters to support ethically sound solutions that can balance the competing interests of women, the unborn and the soul of society itself.\par \par \uc2 The political debate that will now properly unfold need not be as bitter and divisive as some seem intent on making it. For all the hardened verities subscribed to on both sides of the argument, there is a large middle ground on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Polls consistently show that a solid majority of Americans favor legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but not to an unlimited degree. A recent Gallup {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  indicated that while 35% favor an unlimited right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and 13% would ban it completely, half of the electorate wants access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with restrictions.\par \par \uc2 More specifically, a few years ago, Gallup {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/where-americans-stand-on-abortion-in-5-charts/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  60% support for the proposition that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be "generally legal" in the first trimester of pregnancy but only 28% thought the same about the second trimester. That's much more restrictive than the framework the court imposed before Dobbs.\par \par \uc2 Opinion varies from state to state, but that's yet more reason to think that last week's judgment is consistent with the federalist reality of America.\par \par \uc2 The risk for both sides now is overreach. Even deep red states that have near total bans ready to put in place may {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/supreme-court-poised-reverse-roe-americans-support-abortion/story?id=84468131"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 find}}}\uc2  that faced with the reality of a post-Roe world, their citizens' support for outright prohibition wanes.\par \par \uc2 Propelled by the rhetorical excesses of their base, progressive politicians are already overreaching. A growing number of Democrats are expressing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-democrats-abortion-pitfall-demand-activists-trimester-first-third-polling-voters-11652190689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposition}}}\uc2  to any restrictions at all on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even in the third trimester.\par \par \uc2 For ardent opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , passionate in their defense of life in the womb and jubilant at the new framework, the post-Dobbs world may yet prove something of a disappointment. It will\u8212\'20\'14it should\u8212\'20\'14take time to persuade a country shaped by half a century of Roe. But by reasserting the constitutional order, the court has given them the opportunity\u8212\'20\'14the responsibility\u8212\'20\'14to renew a culture of life.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/overreach-roe-v-wade-dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization-joe-biden-elizabeth-warren-abortion-supreme-court-pro-life-persuasion-legal-arguments-11656349050"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Urge to Overreach Outlives Roe v. Wade}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220627ei6r005k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
