\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Churches Move Cautiously on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  and Call for Calm Post-Roe; Sunday sermons address Supreme Court ruling; 'It's not a time to spike the football,' said one priest ahead of celebrating Mass\b0\par\par\uc2 By Theo Francis, Kate King and Teresa Mettela \par \uc2 1,104 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2022\par 21:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Members of the clergy treaded carefully in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-wake-of-roe-v-wade-ruling-abortion-providers-confront-new-landscape-11656268445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discussing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  on the first Sunday after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , and they called for respectful discussions over an issue that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-guns-and-trump-a-church-group-tries-to-navigate-americas-divisions-11608298552"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 divides many congregations }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "For many in our country who've been fighting for this for so long, this felt like a huge win," said pastor Andy Stanley at North Point Community Church in Alpharetta, Ga. "But for others in our country, this felt like a gut punch. These are the cultural moments where the church has an opportunity to shine, even when we don't necessarily agree."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Stanley told parishioners he had strong personal feelings about the issue but didn't discuss what they were.\par \par \uc2 At the Shrine of the Most Blessed Sacrament in Washington, D.C., priests didn't mention the court's decision at two celebrations of Mass on Sunday morning. Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , who joined the court's majority in ruling that there is no constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is a member of the church.\par \par \uc2 At Prestonwood Baptist Church in Plano, Texas, which says it has 49,000 members across three campuses, worshipers stood and applauded the ruling.\par \par \uc2 "While we are celebrating and slapping some high-fives, if you will, we're also on our knees, thanking God," said the church's senior pastor, Jack Graham, in a video message to parishioners.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Graham, who was a member of then-President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's evangelical advisory board, thanked the former president for appointing three Supreme Court justices who voted to overturn Roe v. Wade. Dr. Graham said church members should work at the state and local level to oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Let's continue to fight for life, to fight the good fight of faith, knowing that the enemy is not people," he said. "We have a spiritual warfare in which we are engaged. But people all around us\u8212\'20\'14that's the mission field."\par \par \uc2 "It's not a time to spike the football," said the Rev. Christopher Walsh of St. Cecilia Catholic Church in Philadelphia in an interview ahead of celebrating Mass on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 He said he wanted to emphasize the need to help unexpectedly pregnant women as well as those in financial hardship.\par \par \uc2 A similar message came from one of the nation's most prominent Roman Catholic churches, St. Patrick's Cathedral in Midtown Manhattan. Father Enrique Salvo avoided direct reference to the Supreme Court's ruling and called for forgiveness toward those who make mistakes, which he said includes those who terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Some churches and clergy had called for Roe v. Wade to be upheld and spoke out Sunday morning. At one Episcopal church in the Washington area, the priest read a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.episcopalchurch.org/publicaffairs/statement-on-supreme-court-dobbs-decision-by-presiding-bishop-michael-curry/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement by Presiding Bishop Michael Curry }}}\uc2 , who criticized the decision as harmful to women.\par \par \uc2 "We pray for the poor and vulnerable who may not have other options for access" to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Bishop Curry. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
