\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 As Roe v. Wade Protests Roll On,  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Providers Race Against Deadlines; Some providers have closed since ruling eliminated constitutional right to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 , while others are on borrowed time\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas, Laura Kusisto and Ginger Adams Otis \par \uc2 878 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2022\par 16:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Protests and rallies continued Saturday evening in response to the Supreme Court's ruling that overturned Roe v. Wade and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended constitutional protections for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 , while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers halted services or rushed to move through appointments before state bans take effect.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters have converged at protests in cities across the U.S. since Friday's decision. Demonstrations took place from Los Angeles to Philadelphia on Saturday, following protests Friday from Washington Square Park in New York City to Cedar Rapids, Iowa, and Albuquerque, N.M.\par \par \uc2 In Indianapolis on Saturday, hundreds of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters gathered outside the Indiana Statehouse, chanting and waving signs.\par \par \uc2 "The 1950s called. They want their oppression back," said one sign. Meanwhile, a group of antiabortion supporters stood nearby and cheered the overturning of Roe.\par \par \uc2 A stream of demonstrators gathered Saturday at the Supreme Court in Washington, D.C., including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents who took pictures in front of the court, celebrating their victory. "Into the ash heap of history where you belong, Roe v. Wade," read one sign held up by a visitor.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's ruling, in a case from Mississippi, overturned Roe, the 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The court said there was no provision in the Constitution that implicitly protected the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision effectively returned the issue to the 50 states, which now have broad latitude to prohibit or protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they see fit.\par \par \uc2 Roughly half the states have already banned\u8212\'20\'14or are poised to soon ban\u8212\'20\'14many or most abortions. Thirteen states have so-called trigger laws, which ban nearly all abortions and were designed to take effect in the event the Supreme Court overturned Roe. The laws in several of those states took effect immediately Friday, while laws in other states are designed to take effect 30 days from the ruling.\par \par \uc2 Since the ruling, clinics in several states have closed or suspended service.\par \par \uc2 In North Dakota, the state's attorney general has 30 days to certify the Supreme Court's decision, which will allow the state's trigger law to take effect. On Friday, the state's attorney general, Drew Wrigley, said his office was "evaluating the Dobbs opinion in every detail and will give careful consideration to its impact on North Dakota's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws."\par \par \uc2 At the Red River Women's Clinic in Fargo, N.D., the state's only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, staff anticipated the usual 20 to 25 appointments to continue as scheduled this week.\par \par \uc2 "Our plan is to continue to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in North Dakota as long as we legally can," said Tammi Kromenaker, director of the Red River Women's Clinic. She said she would consult with legal counsel to ensure they comply with the law if and when the state's trigger law takes effect.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Kromenaker said she ultimately plans to open a new clinic across the river in Moorhead, Minn., where there are fewer restrictions on the procedure. The clinic has secured an office space in Moorhead.\par \par \uc2 "Our goal\u8230\'20\'26is to be able to open our doors there in as little time as possible after we're not able to provide in North Dakota anymore," Ms. Kromenaker said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, a group of Senate Democrats in a letter Saturday urged President Biden to take action. "Now is the time for bold action to protect the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," read the letter, which was signed by 34 senators. "You have the power to fight back and lead a national response to this devastating decision, so we call on you to take every step available to your Administration."\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Mr. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/biden-calls-abortion-ruling-tragic-error--4ATIrLswM0hg5i5ctzNT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he would do everything in his power }}}\uc2  to protect women in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access will be eliminated.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  also on Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/attorney-general-lays-out-justice-department-s-red-lines-after-ruling-qjmSR90s3Zzb88oidJ7j"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlined several red lines }}}\uc2  the Justice Department believed states couldn't cross in banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Those included restricting a woman's ability to travel to another state to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or banning federally approved medication that terminates a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Since the decision Friday morning, state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws have evolved almost by the hour. On Saturday in Minnesota, Gov. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  signed an executive order that aims to provide legal protections to patients who travel there from another state.\par \par \uc2 "Your reproductive freedom will remain protected in Minnesota as long as I am in office," Mr. Walz said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Friday evening, the Utah State Legislature released a statement saying its general counsel had determined that the state law triggering a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  post-Roe is now in effect. The law, passed in 2020, bans all abortions except in the case of rape, incest or a medical emergency.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Association of Utah filed a lawsuit Saturday challenging the law in state court.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Ginger Adams Otis at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Ginger.AdamsOtis@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ginger.AdamsOtis@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-roe-v-wade-protests-roll-on-abortion-providers-race-against-deadlines-11656240215"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As Roe v. Wade Protests Roll On, \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Providers Race Against Deadlines }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220626ei6q000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
