\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ruling Poses Fresh Midterm Challenges for Democrats, Republicans; GOP hopes to keep economy top of mind; Democrats want to boost turnout and avoid disillusionment among progressives\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joshua Jamerson and Andrew Restuccia \par \uc2 1,579 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2022\par 19:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Strategists in both parties acknowledge that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-move-abortion-fight-to-midterm-elections-after-supreme-court-ruling-11656098522"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is now poised to play }}}\uc2  a larger role in the midterm elections than anticipated. The pivotal question is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-wake-of-roe-v-wade-ruling-abortion-providers-confront-new-landscape-11656268445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whether the issue will be front of mind }}}\uc2  for voters, as Democrats hope, or will pale in comparison to economic concerns, as Republicans predict.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's landmark Dobbs opinion }}}\uc2 , Democrats will try to win over new voters\u8212\'20\'14and motivate core Democratic constituencies to turn out\u8212\'20\'14with an argument that Republicans and the Supreme Court have been overtaken by extremists out of step with the public in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-opponents-consider-how-far-to-press-after-end-of-roe-v-wade-11656273349"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their opposition to Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 . That 1973 decision, which established {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a constitutional right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , had widespread public support, according to public-opinion polling by The Wall Street Journal and others.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, Democrats need to ensure that some younger and more progressive Democrats don't grow disillusioned by what they see as a lack of aggressiveness by their leaders. Many lawmakers and activists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/abortion-ruling-revives-liberal-push-to-overhaul-court-ypDY5gkBIdXpqx7IFrql"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are calling for structural changes }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14such as abolishing or weakening the Senate filibuster and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/commission-on-supreme-court-reform-skeptical-about-expanding-court-11634250935"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanding the Supreme Court }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14that President Biden and some other top Democrats oppose.\par \par \uc2 Either way, Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-hunts-for-small-wins-as-democratic-frustration-builds-11654788300"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are expected to face an uphill fight }}}\uc2  in the midterms because of the economy. U.S. inflation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/us-inflation-consumer-price-index-may-2022-11654810079"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accelerated to an 8.6% annual rate }}}\uc2  in May, its fastest pace in 41 years, and average gasoline prices in the U.S. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gasoline-prices-reach-5-a-gallon-nationwide-for-the-first-time-11654910506"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 topped $5 a gallon this month }}}\uc2  for the first time. David Wasserman of the nonpartisan Cook Political Report wrote in late May that any Democrat in a House seat Mr. Biden won by single digits in 2020 "is at severe risk and even a few in seats Biden carried by 10 to 15 points could lose."\par \par \uc2 Democrats say they must keep pitching voters on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-midterms-democrats-11647629157"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their ideas for battling inflation }}}\uc2 . They also see an opportunity to win over voters in an otherwise unfavorable political environment by laying out their vision for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned/card/biden-says-midterm-wins-needed-to-protect-abortion-rights-10IqxZrHrtx5LhVe53AB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 codifying Roe into law }}}\uc2  by expanding their Senate majority and holding on to the House.\par \par \uc2 "We are now going to start seeing the stories of what women are facing in the states," said Rep. \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  (D., Wash.), the chair of the Congressional Progressive Caucus. "I really think that's going to turn up the heat on everybody."\par \par \uc2 Groups including the Democratic Senatorial Campaign Committee, which is working to expand the Democrats' 50-50 hold on the Senate with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  breaking ties, have seen an influx of fundraising, according to officials. The Democratic Legislative Campaign Committee, which focuses on statehouse battles, took in six times what it typically raises in one day by 4:30 p.m. Friday, the day the Supreme Court's decision was made public, its best fundraising day of the cycle, a spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are skeptical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have the salience in November Democrats hope it will.\par \par \uc2 "This will be one of the issues we talk about when we elect senators and House members and members of the state houses and governors. But it's not going to change the 2022 outcome," Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R., S.C.) said on Fox News Sunday, adding: "What's going to be on the ballot box is $5 gas."\par \par \uc2 A Republican strategist who works on state legislative races said that early interviews with voters since the Dobbs decision show the economy remains the top issue for independents this fall, and that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/wsj-poll-biden-ukraine-inflation-midterms-11646975533"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. Biden's low approval rating }}}\uc2  remains a headwind for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Officials in both parties agreed the onus was on Democrats to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  an issue that shakes up races. Ms. Jayapal said Mr. Biden was right to call for people to vote this November for Democrats but urged him to be aggressive in keeping the issue relevant.\par \par \uc2 Pollsters in recent months have consistently shown voters most care about the economy and inflation. One poll by \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2  in May, after the draft Dobbs decision leaked, showed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the No. 2 issue among all voters, slightly behind the economy at No. 1.\par \par \uc2 "It's not that people don't care [about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ]. It's a matter of salience," said Sarah Longwell, a Republican strategist who conducts focus groups of swing voters. Ms. Longwell, who has opposed former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's influence over the party, said that women voters who backed Mr. Trump in 2016 but picked Mr. Biden in 2020 said they cared most about the economy in focus groups after the Dobbs decision leaked.\par \par \uc2 "If you just think that the overturning of Roe is just going to overturn the dynamics of 2022, I'm not sure that that's true," she said.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are going to keep their midterm focus on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-gets-a-starring-role-in-gop-congressional-campaign-ads-11648373402"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blaming Democrats for high inflation }}}\uc2 . To the extent that the GOP has waded into \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics since the Dobbs decision, it has largely been to praise the court for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 returning the question of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  to the American people and their elected representatives.\par \par \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 , the chairwoman of the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 , said after the Dobbs opinion was handed down that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-v-wade-overturned-supreme-court-11656110804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the party would continue to run against }}}\uc2  Democrats' advocacy for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "As this debate now returns to the states and the American people, we know there is still much work ahead. Republicans will continue to advocate for life, uphold the law and stand against an extreme Democrat Party's pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda," Ms. McDaniel said.\par \par \uc2 Complicating Democrats's efforts to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a bigger issue this fall is disagreement about the best message to take to voters. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Supreme Court's ruling }}}\uc2  has brought to the forefront long-lingering generational tension within the Democratic Party, with younger progressives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/group-of-democratic-lawmakers-to-present-plan-to-expand-supreme-court-11618447336"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling for institutional changes }}}\uc2  to a system that they say is failing them and older moderates arguing for working within that system to make change.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Mr. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/biden-calls-abortion-ruling-tragic-error--4ATIrLswM0hg5i5ctzNT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called the Dobbs opinion a "tragic error" }}}\uc2  and said he would do everything in his power to protect women in states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access will be eliminated }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-at-center-of-fight-over-abortion-after-career-of-reservations-11651921202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has long been hesitant }}}\uc2  to wade too deeply into the politics of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and previously held more centrist views on the issue than many in his party. Ms. Harris has been more outspoken on the issue and her supporters hope she will take on a more prominent role advocating for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the coming weeks and months.\par \par \uc2 Activists on the left and some progressive lawmakers expressed frustration with party stalwarts for their initial response to the ruling. Advocates said Democrats should back a reimagining of the Supreme Court that would include expanding the number of justices and term limits, as well as the elimination of the filibuster in the Senate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-senate-filibuster-explained-11642618860"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Getting rid of the filibuster }}}\uc2  would mean that bills\u8212\'20\'14such as one codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\u8212\'20\'14could pass the Senate with 51 votes rather than the 60 votes now required for most legislation to advance. Adding more seats to the Supreme Court, some Democrats say, would give Mr. Biden the chance to appoint liberal justices to disrupt the current conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 Freshman Rep. Sara Jacobs (D., Calif.), who represents a deep-blue district in San Diego County and at 33 is one of the youngest members of Congress, said Democrats should make structural reforms to the court.\par \par \uc2 "As a young woman myself, I feel very, very angry and disappointed that it even got to the point where we were relying on this extreme, radical Supreme Court for our rights," she said. "Congress should have done our job and we should have codified Roe v. Wade \u8230\'20\'26 so that it was never just about the court."\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  told reporters that Mr. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/biden-doesn-t-agree-with-expanding-the-supreme-court-white-house-press-secretary-says-Ide0ATyN7uSqimTiNMOB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues to oppose expanding the high court }}}\uc2 , as many progressives have urged. "The reality is we have to get Congress to act to restore Roe, to make it law of the land," Ms. Jean-Pierre said. "And in light of this decision, they have to use their voice at the ballot box."\par \par \uc2 Brian Fallon, the executive director of Demand Justice, the progresssive group that advocates for court expansion, said Mr. Biden needed to be more critical of the court as an institution to get Democrats to come to the polls this fall.\par \par \uc2 "He's trying to walk a fine line of criticizing the court's decisions, but not seem to question the court's legitimacy or calling out the court as an institution overall. And I don't think he needs to do that. In fact, I think he's missing a political opportunity," Mr. Fallon said.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Paige White, 30, a civil-rights attorney who participated in protests outside the Supreme Court on Friday, said Democrats weren't acting boldly enough to protect women's rights and fight Republicans' agenda. "He has Black and brown women to thank for winning the election," Ms. White said of the president, "and he has done very little for us."\par \par \uc2 "I think that Democrats as a whole have to stop playing scared," she said. "Our lawmakers need to get real and get aggressive."\par \par \uc2 Alex Leary contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Joshua Jamerson at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:joshua.jamerson+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joshua.jamerson+1@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Andrew Restuccia at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:andrew.restuccia@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 andrew.restuccia@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-ruling-poses-fresh-midterm-challenges-for-democrats-republicans-11656272277"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ruling Poses Fresh Midterm Challenges for Democrats, Republicans }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220626ei6q001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
