\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Opponents Consider How Far to Press After End of Roe v. Wade; Republican-leaning states, with new power to regulate abortions, face a choice between incremental restrictions or broader bans\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 1,604 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2022\par 21:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 For the nearly half-century that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade was the law of the land }}}\uc2 , the most prominent opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  often urged an incremental approach to narrowing access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Now, having achieved {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Supreme Court victory that overruled Roe }}}\uc2  and ended the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , antiabortion advocates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-decision-sparks-immediate-action-from-states-11656096002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are considering what to do next }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some powerful voices in the movement urge a measured approach {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-ruling-poses-fresh-midterm-challenges-for-democrats-republicans-11656272277"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guided by political realities post-Roe }}}\uc2 , seeking to ban the procedure after the first trimester in more moderate states and maintaining meaningful exceptions for rape and incest. Others view this as a once-in-a-generation moment and moral imperative to push for a complete end to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially in states where conservatives hold political power. The staunchest opponents want states to treat it as murder.\par \par \uc2 This spring, anticipating that Roe might be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/churches-move-cautiously-on-abortion-and-call-for-calm-post-roe-11656268174?mod=Searchresults_pos1&page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned }}}\uc2 , a number of Republican-dominated legislatures {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a series of toughened laws }}}\uc2  and\u8212\'20\'14after the Supreme Court's decision\u8212\'20\'14pledged to enact more. This year, a half-dozen states have enacted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-wake-of-roe-v-wade-ruling-abortion-providers-confront-new-landscape-11656268445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But even in states where bans are in place or likely, there are debates about how far to go. Most bills passed in the last couple of years don't include exceptions for cases of rape and incest, for instance, which Republican politicians from \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have in the past supported.\par \par \uc2 Polls suggest most people in the U.S. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/upholding-roe-v-wade-is-supported-by-most-americans-wsj-poll-finds-11654162200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 favor legalized \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , though many also are open to some restrictions. A recent national Wall Street Journal poll found that 57% of people said a woman should be able to get a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if she wants it for any reason, and 84% said she should be able to get one if the pregnancy is the result of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 In more politically mixed states such as Florida and Virginia, some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have pushed for bans in the early weeks of pregnancy, putting them at odds with local Republican leaders who have hesitated to go that far. On the national level, Students for Life of America, a group with growing clout in conservative circles, also is lobbying for tighter bans.\par \par \uc2 "In statehouses, those we elect who have pledged to stand with us will be forced to finally act," Students for Life President Kristan Hawkins told hundreds of attendees this month at the Western Conservative Summit in Colorado. "I predict some of those who said they were with us won't be there when the final tally comes in." \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
