\par \par \uc2 Arkansas state Sen. Jim Hendren says he sees divisions within the pro-life movement. PHOTO: terra fondriest for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Arkansas Gov. Asa Hutchinson, a Republican who signed a bill last year that banned all abortions except in cases of medical emergency, said Sunday on NBC that he wished the state had a rape and incest exception.\par \par \uc2 "I would've preferred a different outcome than that. But that's not the debate today in Arkansas. It might be in the future," Mr. Hutchinson said.\par \par \uc2 In Louisiana and other states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-v-wade-overturned-supreme-court-11656110804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 longtime \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  opponents }}}\uc2  are facing a vocal minority who have said women who get abortions should face prison time. These so-called \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  abolitionists are growing more organized and recently won a minor victory when a bill by state Rep. Danny McCormick, a Republican who was seeking to classify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as homicide, was voted out of committee.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/louisiana-house-stops-abortion-bill-that-allowed-murder-charges-against-women-11652408028"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An emotional debate broke out }}}\uc2  in the state's legislature in May. "Today when Roe is on the chopping block and we have the clear opportunity to end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in our state, we are faltering," Mr. McCormick said.\par \par \uc2 Another Republican, state Rep. Alan Seabaugh, led a successful charge to sink the bill, which he said was flawed and wouldn't strengthen Louisiana's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, already among the toughest in the nation. With Roe's demise seemingly imminent, "we should be celebrating together, embracing each other as brothers in Christ," he said. "We should not be at each other's throats."\par \par \uc2 Mr. McCormick said he hopes to propose the bill or something like it again.\par \par \uc2 Mary Ziegler, a professor at \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 , and author of "Dollars for Life: The Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Movement and the Fall of the Republican Establishment," said traditional hierarchies in the antiabortion movement have broken down as the movement has achieved a monumental victory.\par \par \uc2 "The argument that you need to be cautious, you need to take your time, rings hollow for a lot of people," she said.\par \par \uc2 Prof. Ziegler said many experts had once predicted that state legislatures would pass more moderate bills if Roe were overturned, knowing the laws would be more than just political statements. "What you're seeing is actually the opposite. Now that states have the ability to potentially enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, they're doing more extreme, more sweeping things," she said.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What does overturning Roe v. Wade mean for the Republican Party? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Republican leaders in some states are debating how early in pregnancy to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In Arizona, Republicans are divided on which of two laws should govern the state: a 15-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that passed this spring, or a decades-old ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all stages of pregnancy that predated Roe.\par \par \uc2 Arizona state Sen. Nancy Barto, a Republican, sponsored the 15-week bill, but said the full ban should take precedence. The Legislature's intent was always to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as widely as the Supreme Court would allow and "to protect as many unborn as possible," she said.\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Dannenfelser, the president of Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, one of the largest antiabortion groups in the country, said she favors total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans but cautioned that if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents overshoot and ask for too much, they risk getting nothing in some states. The group has been assessing what would be realistic gains in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-roe-v-wade-ruling-sets-off-protests-as-states-plan-next-moves-11656149401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 30 or so states it considers in play }}}\uc2 based on the governor, legislature and state courts.\par \par \uc2 "The pro-life movement's ambition must be strong, but it can't overreach the will of the people of that state," Ms. Dannenfelser said. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
