\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion advocate Marjorie Dannenfelser warns that the pro-life movement shouldn't overreach. PHOTO: Stephen Voss for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 In states such as Virginia and North Carolina, that might mean pushing for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans starting in the second trimester, at 15 or 20 weeks, she said. "We could reach a consensus that is much better than nothing," she said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Hawkins, of Students for Life, has limited patience for 15-week bans, which she said do little to accomplish the goal of eliminating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some 95% of abortions occur before 15 weeks of pregnancy. For months, her organization knocked on doors for Republican Glenn Youngkin during his 2021 campaign for Virginia governor. Then, in a televised debate, Mr. Youngkin avoided saying whether he supported a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  starting in the earliest weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Susan B. Anthony\uc2  Pro-Life America endorsed Mr. Youngkin, but Students for Life stopped using door-knocking literature with his name on it. He won, and Ms. Hawkins said she wasn't invited to the inauguration.\par \par \uc2 After Friday's ruling, Mr. Youngkin said he has asked legislative leaders to introduce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation when the state General Assembly returns in January, suggesting he will be able to pass incremental new restrictions.\par \par \uc2 "We can build a bipartisan consensus on protecting the life of unborn children, especially when they begin to feel pain in the womb," he said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Hawkins said she found the governor's approach underwhelming. "Here's this amazing opportunity to lead in the moment," she said Saturday. "It wasn't much of a clarion call to the pro-life movement."\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Calfas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-opponents-consider-how-far-to-press-after-end-of-roe-v-wade-11656273349"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Opponents Consider How Far to Press After End of Roe v. Wade  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220626ei6q00231\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
