\par \par \uc2 The Planned Parenthood Loop Health Center in Chicago this month. Clinics in Illinois have seen an increase in calls from patients in surrounding states. PHOTO: Taylor Glascock for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in several states across the country halted services in the wake of the Supreme Court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision to overturn Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , while supporters and opponents began to shift their focus to pill-based abortions and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 how new restrictions would be enforced }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Clinics in a number of states, including Texas, Wisconsin and Kentucky, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stopped offering services }}}\uc2  Friday. Providers in other states, such as North Dakota and Idaho, were moving ahead with services before more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state bans took effect }}}\uc2 , typically in a matter of days or weeks.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal with few restrictions, such as Illinois, were fielding a surge of inquiries, many from women in neighboring states with more stringent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 "Already, there is confusion," said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, interim dean of the Beasley School of Law at \uc2 Temple University\uc2 . "What states are doing is changing by the day. Clinics are closing, clinics are trying to talk to patients about what their options are."\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's ruling, in a case from Mississippi, overturned Roe, the 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/key-excerpts-from-supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-overturning-roe-v-wade-11656092052"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concluded that Roe was wrongly decided }}}\uc2  and said there was no provision in the Constitution that implicitly protected the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision broadly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-decision-sparks-immediate-action-from-states-11656096002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 returned the issue to the 50 states }}}\uc2 , which now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-opponents-consider-how-far-to-press-after-end-of-roe-v-wade-11656273349"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have wide latitude }}}\uc2  to prohibit or protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they see fit. Roughly half the states have already or are poised to ban many or most abortions.\par \par \uc2 Thirteen states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-prepare-to-quickly-implement-abortion-trigger-laws-11655385028"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have trigger laws }}}\uc2 , bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  designed to take effect after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/roe-v-wade-overturned-supreme-court-11656110804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court decision overturning Roe }}}\uc2  is made, and some states have other bans or restrictions that could now be revived or enforced. These bans quickly took effect Friday in several states including Alabama, Arkansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Missouri, South Dakota and Utah. Lawmakers in Oklahoma {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-governor-signs-abortion-ban-11653529937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned most abortions last month }}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trigger laws }}}\uc2  in other states, such as Idaho, Tennessee and Texas, are designed to take effect in days or weeks or following state action.\par \par \uc2 Providers at Planned Parenthood of Wisconsin locations in Madison and Milwaukee canceled 66 appointments scheduled for Friday and Saturday after the court's ruling. Four patients were able to complete their appointments before the decision Friday morning, said Michelle Velasquez, director of legal advocacy and services at the organization.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin providers anticipated the court's decision would allow the state's pre-existing ban from 1849 to be enforceable and outlaw most abortions.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Wisconsin Gov. \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  called a special legislative session to repeal the more than 170-year-old law last week, but lawmakers adjourned without taking any action. The state's attorney general, \uc2 Josh Kaul\uc2 , has said he wouldn't enforce it. But while the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Wisconsin remains unclear, providers aren't willing to risk potential prosecution, according to Ms. Velasquez.\par \par \uc2 In North Dakota, the state's attorney general has 30 days to certify the Supreme Court's decision, which will allow North Dakota's ban to take effect. On Friday, Attorney General Drew Wrigley said in a statement that his office was "evaluating the Dobbs opinion in every detail and will give careful consideration to its impact on North Dakota's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws."\par \par \uc2 At the Red River Women's Clinic in Fargo, N.D., the state's only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, staff anticipated the usual 20 to 25 appointments to continue as scheduled this week.\par \par \uc2 "Our plan is to continue to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in North Dakota as long as we legally can," said Tammi Kromenaker, director of the Red River Women's Clinic. She said she would consult with legal counsel to ensure the clinic complies with the law if and when the state's trigger law takes effect.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/illinois-abortion-clinics-are-preparing-for-a-potential-post-roe-world-11638419374"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers in Illinois }}}\uc2 , which passed legislation in 2019 expanding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, have seen an increase in calls from patients in surrounding states since the Supreme Court's ruling, said Jennifer Welch, president and chief executive of Planned Parenthood of Illinois.\par \par \uc2 The move by clinics in Wisconsin to cancel appointments prompted more patients there to seek abortions in Illinois, according to Ms. Welch.\par \par \uc2 "We absolutely have been talking with patients from all over the country," Ms. Welch said on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the national spotlight over the weekend began to swing to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which involves {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drugs prescribed to trigger abortions }}}\uc2  and sometimes sent through the mail.\par \par \uc2 Pill-based procedures accounted for 54% of U.S. abortions in 2020, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
