\par \par \uc2 The Tulsa Women's Clinic in Oklahoma. State lawmakers banned most abortions last month. PHOTO: Michael Noble Jr. for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Many states had already moved to restrict medication abortions before outright bans went into place following Friday's ruling. Many require the doctor providing a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be physically present, prohibiting the use of telemedicine, according to Guttmacher. Others say the clinicians who administer such medications must be physicians.\par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration has approved medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. for up to 10 weeks of pregnancy. Patients can legally obtain the drugs at clinics or through U.S.-based telemedicine providers.\par \par \uc2 Health and Human Services Secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  and Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said after Friday's ruling that they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/attorney-general-lays-out-justice-department-s-red-lines-after-ruling-qjmSR90s3Zzb88oidJ7j"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would defend access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills }}}\uc2 . "States may not ban mifepristone based on disagreement with the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's expert judgment about its safety and efficacy," Mr. Garland said. A White House official reiterated plans to protect access to the pills.\par \par \uc2 The state restrictions and efforts of the Biden administration to keep pill access open are setting up a likely clash in court, said \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2 , a state policy analyst at Guttmacher. This is uncharted territory nearly 50 years after states could last ban abortions, she said.\par \par \uc2 "There are so many pieces that are new," she said.\par \par \uc2 South Dakota Gov. \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , a Republican, on Sunday defended her state's decision to prohibit telemedicine abortions, when asked whether the state was prepared to fight potential legal battles over the issue.\par \par \uc2 "What the Supreme Court said was that the Constitution does not give a woman the right to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Ms. Noem said Sunday on \uc2 CBS\uc2 's "Face the Nation." "That means that in each state they will make the decision how they handle these situations." In March, Ms. Noem signed a bill restricting medical abortions via telemedicine that goes into effect July 1.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana's Democratic Gov. \uc2 John Bel Edwards\uc2  signed a bill earlier this month banning the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication that goes into effect Aug. 1.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-ruling-poses-fresh-midterm-challenges-for-democrats-republicans-11656272277"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Other politicians }}}\uc2  took to the airwaves Sunday morning to discuss the Supreme Court's ruling.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Michigan Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  said she is backing women's \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  but faces opposition from the state's Republican legislature. Michigan is one of several states with laws on the books predating Roe, which could allow the state to curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access following the Supreme Court's decision. Last month, a Michigan judge ruled the state's 91-year-old {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-judge-suspends-enforcement-of-pre-roe-abortion-ban-11652819032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state law wouldn't be enforceable }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/churches-move-cautiously-on-abortion-and-call-for-calm-post-roe-11656268174"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  opponents on Sunday }}}\uc2  compared \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in many circumstances with other capital crimes, and thus well within the purview of states to ban.\par \par \uc2 "When you're saving life, that's an appropriate role of the state," Republican Arkansas Gov. Asa Hutchinson said on NBC's "Meet the Press."\par \par \uc2 Some Democratic politicians urged changes to the structure of the court.\par \par \uc2 "I believe we need to get some confidence back in our court and that means we need more justices on the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2 ," said Sen. Elizabeth Warren (D., Mass.) on ABC's "This Week" on Sunday morning.\par \par \uc2 "We've done it before, we need to do it again," Ms. Warren said. The White House said this weekend that Mr. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/abortion-ruling-revives-liberal-push-to-overhaul-court-ypDY5gkBIdXpqx7IFrql"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doesn't support an expansion }}}\uc2  of the high court.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's decision also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-roe-v-wade-ruling-companies-reimbursing-medical-and-travel-expenses-for-abortion-risk-blowback-11656109337"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 creates new challenges for employers }}}\uc2 and health insurers covering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, especially whether and how to pay for travel to states where the procedure remains available.\par \par \uc2 Companies including \uc2 Starbucks Corp\uc2 ., \uc2 Uber Technologies Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . have said they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/uber-lyft-others-to-support-employees-traveling-out-of-state-for-abortion-vtYQJSQ5KFZppFnOXQGF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would reimburse travel for medical services }}}\uc2  including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 Just Eat Takeaway.com N.V\uc2 .'s \uc2 Grubhub\uc2  and \uc2 Dick's Sporting Goods\uc2  said they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/levi-s-ben-jerry-s-other-brands-reaffirm-support-for-reproductive-rights-MowjzyrLOTmBtZ4ogdx8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would provide up to $4,000 }}}\uc2  to cover expenses traveling for services not available in workers' home state.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-debate-puts-corporate-initiatives-in-the-spotlight-11651687778"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Companies that choose to cover \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14and any travel necessary to get one\u8212\'20\'14have to balance alienating employees agitating for their employers to take a stand versus the risk of legal attacks or political blowback in states that have banned the procedure.\par \par \uc2 "Benefits are suddenly starting to become very political, and it's forcing employers to take a position," said \uc2 Michael Turpin\uc2 , executive vice president at USI Holdings Corp., an insurance brokerage.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-roe-v-wade-ruling-sets-off-protests-as-states-plan-next-moves-11656149401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 converged in cities across the U.S. }}}\uc2  Demonstrations took place from Los Angeles to Philadelphia on Saturday, following protests Friday from Washington Square Park in New York City to Cedar Rapids, Iowa, and Albuquerque, N.M.\par \par \uc2 Several hundred protesters gathered in front of the Supreme Court building on Sunday to denounce the court's decision.\par \par \uc2 "I am angry that we are standing here today and there are not hundreds of thousands of people protesting this decision with us," Alix Zabala, 20, told the crowd, using a bullhorn. "I am angry. I am scared. I should not be scared to be a woman in this country."\par \par \uc2 On Saturday at the Supreme Court, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents took pictures in front of the court, celebrating their victory. Read one sign held up by a visitor: "Into the ash heap of history where you belong, Roe v. Wade."\par \par \uc2 Jon Kamp, Liz Essley Whyte, and Sarah Chaney Cambon contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Deanna Paul at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:deanna.paul@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deanna.paul@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-wake-of-roe-v-wade-ruling-abortion-providers-confront-new-landscape-11656268445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Providers Confront New Landscape After Roe }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220626ei6q001rx\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
