\par \par \uc2 A number of companies have decided to cover travel expenses for employees seeking medical procedures that aren't available in their home states, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services. PHOTO: Taylor Glascock for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Julie Jones, chair of law firm \uc2 Ropes & Gray\uc2  , sent a memo to employees saying the firm would hold gatherings over the next few days to speak about the decision and give an overview of federal and state law on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The firm's lawyers are also in touch with its pro bono group to work on related cases, according to an email reviewed by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 "As a woman, I have a profound feeling of vulnerability caused by the elimination of a longstanding right of women\u8212\'20\'14a right that affects their bodies and their agency," she wrote. \uc2 Ropes & Gray\uc2  has about 1,400 lawyers across the world.\par \par \uc2 Facebook\uc2  parent \uc2 Meta Platforms Inc\uc2  . Chief Operating Officer \uc2 Sheryl Sandberg\uc2  called the Supreme Court decision "a huge setback," and said in an \uc2 Instagram\uc2  post it jeopardizes the health of millions of women and girls.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Meta\uc2  spokesman said the company plans to offer travel-expense reimbursements to access out-of-state healthcare and reproductive services, and is "in the process of assessing how best to do so given the legal complexities involved."\par \par \uc2 Without health insurance to foot the bill, obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be costly. In the U.S., the median self-pay price for a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2020 was $560, and the median cost of a first-trimester procedural \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was $575, according to a study published in April in the journal Health Affairs. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\p