\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court's  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Decision Sparks Immediate Action From States; After Roe v. Wade is overruled, Republican state officials press ahead with tight  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  restrictions\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,465 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2022\par 00:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruling Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  triggered immediate responses across the U.S., as conservative states moved forward with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions }}}\uc2 , some clinics suspended service and advocates on both sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate girded for new state-level battles.\par \par \uc2 More than 20 states were poised to ban most abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 if Roe was overturned }}}\uc2 . Some of those prohibitions took effect right away, while others may take time as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state officials sort out }}}\uc2  both practical and legal details.\par \par \uc2 Minutes after the Supreme Court announced its decision, Missouri Attorney General \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2 , a Republican, said he issued an opinion allowing implementation of a state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, previously adopted by the legislature, that was triggered once the justices overruled Roe. The state law doesn't make exceptions for pregnancies that result from rape or incest and makes performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  punishable by five to 15 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 Missouri, he said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , "has become the most Pro Life state in America."\par \par \uc2 South Dakota Republican Gov. \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  said nearly all abortions were now illegal as her state's trigger law took effect. Planned Parenthood's clinic in Sioux Falls, the state's only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, stopped providing abortions before the decision. Louisiana Attorney General \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2  likewise said his state's trigger law banning most abortions has taken effect.\par \par \uc2 In total, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-prepare-to-quickly-implement-abortion-trigger-laws-11655385028"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 states have trigger laws }}}\uc2  that were designed to ban most abortions quickly if the Supreme Court eliminated the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "In the very short term there's going to be a lot of confusion," said Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9, interim dean of the Beasley School of Law at \uc2 Temple University\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers across the country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rushed to accommodate }}}\uc2  to new laws, consulting with legal counsel on their next steps. It wasn't immediately clear how many clinics stopped providing abortions Friday.\par \par \uc2 "We're all scrambling," said Jay Thibodeau, communications director for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Care Network. "This is chaotic."\par \par \uc2 Among the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics halting the procedure was Hope Medical Group for Women in Shreveport, La., said Kathaleen Pittman, the clinic's administrator. The clinic\u8212\'20\'14one of three in Louisiana\u8212\'20\'14sits across the border from Texas and had seen an influx in patients after the Lone Star State implemented a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy last year.\par \par \uc2 "We have devastated patients already here today so we are concentrating on them and assisting them with their options," Ms. Pittman said in an email shortly after the court's decision.\par \par \uc2 In Kentucky, EMW Women's Surgical Center stopped providing abortions on the advice of its lawyers. The state has an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that is designed to take effect immediately.\par \par \uc2 "We have advised them to stop providing all care until our legal team has the time to analyze the entire opinion and how it relates to existing federal and Kentucky laws," said Samuel Crankshaw, a spokesman for ACLU of Kentucky. He said his organization plans to file a lawsuit in state court arguing the state's constitution provides protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kentucky Republican Attorney General \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2  said the Supreme Court's decision marks "a new era."\par \par \uc2 In states where the legal landscape is unclear, some clinics said they had stopped providing abortions for now. Wisconsin has a 1849 law banning nearly all abortions with an exception for the safety of the pregnant woman. Democratic Gov. Tony Evers previously said that the state's attorney general would challenge the law if Roe were overturned. But before the court's ruling, Planned Parenthood clinics in the state already had stopped scheduling abortions for after June 25, because of the existing state law.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, more liberal states took defensive action to protect women seeking abortions and providers who care for them. The governors of California, Oregon and Washington said Friday they were launching a multistate commitment to safeguard \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access that includes protecting patients who travel from states where it is illegal. The states will also discourage local law enforcement from cooperating with out-of-state investigations and arrests related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Massachusetts, Gov. \uc2 Charlie Baker\uc2 , a Republican, signed an executive order Friday similarly aimed at protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, including for women who come from out of state to seek the procedure. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
