\par \par \uc2 Coalition for Life volunteers block access to a Planned Parenthood clinic in St. Louis on Friday. PHOTO: Neeta Satam for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Illinois Gov. \uc2 J.B. Pritzker\uc2 , a Democrat, said he would call a special session of the state's legislature to add more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-providers-in-illinois-colorado-and-florida-prepare-for-patient-influx-if-roe-is-overturned-11655560800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protections for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 . The state is one of more than a dozen others that have enshrined protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent years, and clinics there anticipate an influx of patients from states with new bans.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  sought to expedite legal efforts to overturn a 1931 state law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In May, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-judge-suspends-enforcement-of-pre-roe-abortion-ban-11652819032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state judge temporarily suspended }}}\uc2  enforcement of the law. Ms. Whitmer asked the Michigan Supreme Court to immediately consider whether the state's constitution protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The urgency of the moment is clear\u8212\'20\'14the Michigan court must act now," she said.\par \par \uc2 In Washington, D.C., Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  called the ruling "a devastating blow to reproductive freedom," but emphasized that women have the right to travel between states to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Under bedrock constitutional principles, women who reside in states that have banned access to comprehensive reproductive care must remain free to seek that care in states where it is legal," Mr. Garland said. "Moreover, under fundamental First Amendment principles, individuals must remain free to inform and counsel each other about the reproductive care that is available in other states."\par \par \uc2 There are several states with minimal explicit restrictions or protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In those states \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to remain legal, although lawmakers could move to either protect or ban the procedure, according to \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2 , a state policy analyst at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a policy group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  statistics.\par \par \uc2 The decision prompted emotional reactions around the country, with antiabortion groups celebrating the achievement of a goal they have worked toward all their adult lives and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates mourning the loss of nearly 50 years of protections they viewed as sacred. By midday Friday several hundred protesters had gathered outside the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 "This is a fascist ruling. This is illegitimate," one \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights protester yelled into a megaphone. "We need massive nonviolent mass outpourings of resistance across this country."\par \par \uc2 With another megaphone, one \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent stood in front of "Goodbye Roe" signs and said, "This is a day of celebration for the pro-life generation."\par \par \uc2 With Roe's demise in hand, antiabortion activists said they would push legislators in Republican-led states without strong existing bans to call special legislative sessions to pass new laws.\par \par \uc2 "We have built an army that tomorrow will go to state capitals around the country," said Kristan Hawkins, president of Students for Life of America.\par \par \uc2 Indiana Gov. \uc2 Eric Holcomb\uc2  said in a tweet Friday that he had called the state legislature back into session for July 6.\par \par \uc2 In some Republican-led states, officials began sorting out how to revive years of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions that had been blocked by judges because of the Supreme Court's protections of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Georgia Attorney General Chris Carr, a Republican, asked a federal appeals court to reverse a decision blocking a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks of pregnancy that the state passed in 2019.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, a federal judge issued an order Friday allowing the state's six-week ban to take effect. The law had been blocked by the courts for almost three years. \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  and other groups said they planned to file a new case on behalf of local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers challenging the law in state court.\par \par \uc2 In moderate states including Florida, Virginia and North Carolina, Republican leaders might have to chart a more delicate path forward. In Virginia, Republican Gov. Glenn Youngkin said he has asked legislative leaders to introduce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation when the state General Assembly returns in January, suggesting he will be able to pass incremental new restrictions.\par \par \uc2 "We can build a bipartisan consensus on protecting the life of unborn children, especially when they begin to feel pain in the womb, and importantly supporting mothers and families who choose life," he said.\par \par \uc2 Kris Maher, Robert Barba, Cameron McWhirter and Jon Kamp contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-decision-sparks-immediate-action-from-states-11656096002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Decision Sparks Immediate Action From States  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220624ei6o005sd\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
