\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \uc2 Tech\par \b \uc2 Lawmakers Want \uc2 FTC\uc2  to Investigate \uc2 Apple\uc2  , \uc2 Google\uc2  Over Mobile Tracking; Identifiers built into iOS and Android facilitate the collection and sale of personal data, Democrats say\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patience Haggin \par \uc2 745 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par 20:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Four Democratic lawmakers called on the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  to investigate \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2  . and \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2  .'s \uc2 Google\uc2  , alleging the companies engage in unfair and deceptive practices by enabling the collection and sale of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mobilewalla-says-data-it-gathered-from-consumers-cellphones-ended-up-with-government-11637242202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mobile-phone users' personal information  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  "knowingly facilitated these harmful practices by building advertising-specific tracking IDs into their mobile operating systems," the lawmakers wrote in a letter to \uc2 FTC\uc2  chair Lina Khan sent on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Both companies have recently taken steps to limit the collection of user data through these mobile-ad identifiers\u8212\'20\'14a string of numbers and letters built into iOS and Android, the respective mobile operating systems of \uc2 Apple\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  . Users of both operating systems now have a way to opt out of having their identifier transmitted to apps. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/apples-privacy-changes-are-poised-to-boost-its-ad-products-11619485863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Apple last year introduced a new version  }}}\uc2  of its software that requires each app to ask the user for permission to access the device's identifier, and \uc2 Google\uc2  is planning to adopt new privacy restrictions to curtail tracking across {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/google-plans-to-curtail-cross-app-tracking-on-android-phones-11645016401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apps on Android smartphones  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Until recently, however, \uc2 Apple\uc2  enabled this tracking ID by default and required consumers to dig through confusing phone settings to turn it off. \uc2 Google\uc2  still enables this tracking identifier by default, and until recently did not even provide consumers with an opt-out," said the letter, which was signed by Sen. \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  (D., Ore.); Sen. Elizabeth Warren (D., Mass.); Sen. \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  (D., N.J.); and Rep. Sara Jacobs (D., Calif.). "These identifiers have fueled the unregulated data broker market by creating a single piece of information linked to a device that data brokers and their customers can use to link to other data about consumers."\par \par \uc2 These identifiers are ostensibly anonymous, they wrote, but can be easily traced back to the individuals who own the phones associated with them. "It is often possible to easily identify a particular consumer in a dataset of 'anonymous' location records by looking to see where they sleep at night," they wrote.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Google\uc2  spokesman said the company never sells user data and said its app store, \uc2 Google\uc2  Play, prohibits the sale of data by developers. "The advertising ID was created to give users more control and provide developers with a more private way to effectively monetize their apps," he said in a statement. "Any claims that advertising ID was created to facilitate data sale are simply false."\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  didn't respond to requests for comment, and the \uc2 FTC\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lina-khan-sees-turbulent-start-as-head-of-federal-trade-commission-11637073000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ms. Khan took over the FTC  }}}\uc2  about a year ago, the agency has been looking to strengthen the rules that govern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ftc-weighs-new-online-privacy-rules-11632913200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 how digital businesses collect user data  }}}\uc2 . The agency can also bring enforcement actions against companies for unfair or deceptive practices.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of \uc2 Apple\uc2  's move last year to require apps on its iOS platform to ask the user for permission to access the device's identifier, digital-ad companies have become less able to target ads with precision and prove that the ads generate sales. \uc2 Meta Platforms Inc\uc2  ., the parent of \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  , said earlier this year that it expected a roughly $10 billion hit to 2022 sales as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/apples-privacy-change-is-hitting-tech-and-e-commerce-companies-11634901357"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a result of Apple's change  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The office of Mr. Wyden on Friday said the possibility that the Supreme Court might repeal Roe v. Wade prompted lawmakers to call on the \uc2 FTC\uc2  to act, "along with growing awareness of how the advertising ecosystem causes users' information to be abused." Later Friday morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2 , eliminating the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and leaving the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 's legality to the states.\par \par \uc2 "Prosecutors in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes illegal will soon be able to obtain warrants for location information about anyone who has visited an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider," the lawmakers wrote in their letter. "Private actors will also be incentivized by state bounty laws to hunt down women who have obtained or are seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by accessing location information" through data brokers, they wrote.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 FTC\uc2  should investigate \uc2 Apple\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  's role in transforming online advertising into an intense system of surveillance that incentivizes and facilitates the unrestrained collection and constant sale of Americans' personal data," they wrote.\par \par \uc2 Write to Patience Haggin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:patience.haggin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patience.haggin@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawmakers-want-ftc-to-investigate-apple-google-over-mobile-tracking-11656077945"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lawmakers Want FTC to Investigate Apple, Google Over Mobile Tracking  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220624ei6o002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
