\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ruling Prompts Glee and Anger From U.S. Leaders; Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  called the decision a historic victory; Sens. Joe Manchin and \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  criticized justices\b0\par\par\uc2 By Siobhan Hughes and Alex Leary \par \uc2 772 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par 22:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A Supreme Court ruling that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended the constitutional right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  elicited strong responses from a range of U.S. leaders, exposing one of the deepest fault lines in American politics.\par \par \uc2 Many Republicans hailed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization-6-24-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's decision }}}\uc2  as a victory for the antiabortion movement. But Democrats reacted with outrage, with some saying the Supreme Court has put the matter squarely in the hands of Congress, increasing pressure on legislators to write \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights protections into law and on voters to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-move-abortion-fight-to-midterm-elections-after-supreme-court-ruling-11656098522"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elect Democrats in the midterms. }}}\par \par \uc2 "We must channel our mourning and outrage into action, demanding new laws in Congress and in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state legislatures across the country }}}\uc2  to preserve this fundamental human right," Sen. Jeanne Shaheen (D., N.H.) said. "And we need to raise our voices like never before at the polls this November to elect leaders who actually trust women."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) called the decision a "historic victory for the Constitution and for the most vulnerable in our society."\par \par \uc2 "Millions of Americans have spent half a century praying, marching, and working toward today's historic victories for the rule of law and for innocent life. I have been proud to stand with them throughout our long journey and I share their joy today," he said.\par \par \uc2 The intense outpouring from both Democrats and Republicans reflected how divisive America's top court and its opinions have become.\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who installed a solid conservative majority on the Supreme Court, heralded the court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning of Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  as the "biggest win for life in a generation."\par \par \uc2 "It was my great honor to do so!" Mr. Trump said of the nominees confirmed during his tenure: Justices \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett. All were on the five-justice majority that overruled Roe.\par \par \uc2 Asked on Fox News whether he feels he played a role in the longstanding policy reversal, Mr. Trump said, "God made the decision."\par \par \uc2 President Biden promised to do everything in his power to protect women in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access will be eliminated }}}\uc2  following the Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade, which he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called a tragic error. }}}\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden spoke from the White House on Friday, calling it a "sad day for the court and the country." He said the original 1973 ruling was the correct decision and has been the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law of the land for 50 years. }}}\uc2  He argued the decision was the culmination of a deliberate Republican effort to "upset the balance of our law."\par \par \uc2 Sen. Joe Manchin of West Virginia was the only Senate Democrat to vote against a bill last month providing a federal guarantee to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability. He was the only Democrat to vote for confirming Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 . He has opposed adding new seats to the Supreme Court to weaken the power of the 6-3 conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 But on Friday, he said that the Supreme Court had gone too far, and he singled out Justice Kavanaugh and Justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I trusted Justice Gorsuch and Justice Kavanaugh when they testified under oath that they also believed Roe v. Wade was settled legal precedent, and I am alarmed they chose to reject the stability the ruling has provided for two generations of Americans," Mr. Manchin said.\par \par \uc2 Republican Sen. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine, who supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, also said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/roe-v-wade-supreme-court-overturned/card/susan-collins-says-draft-ruling-would-be-inconsistent-with-justices-past-comments-MhPpRBT4TjpRxoPGqQJG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision was inconsistent }}}\uc2  with what Justices Gorsuch and Kavanaugh said in the testimony and in meetings with her. At those meetings, she said, "They both were insistent on the importance of supporting longstanding precedents that the country has relied upon."\par \par \uc2 Ms. Collins has been working with Sen. Tim Kaine (D., Va.) on federal legislation to codify the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as established under Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 Democrats last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/senate-to-vote-on-abortion-access-law-as-supreme-court-weighs-roes-fate-11652274305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to advance a bill }}}\uc2  seeking to ensure women's access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the wake of Friday's Supreme Court's decision, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  called on voters to elect more officials who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. And former first lady Michelle Obama urged those upset with the ruling to "channel your frustration and anger into action by getting involved."\par \par \uc2 Catherine Lucey and Ken Thomas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Siobhan Hughes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:siobhan.hughes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 siobhan.hughes@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Alex Leary at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alex.leary@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alex.leary@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-abortion-ruling-prompts-glee-and-anger-from-u-s-leaders-11656111306"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ruling Prompts Glee and Anger From U.S. Leaders  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220624ei6o00899\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
