\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court Overturns Roe v. Wade, Eliminates Constitutional Right to  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; The court upholds law from Mississippi that bans  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks, opens door to widespread prohibitions on the procedure\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brent Kendall and Jess Bravin \par \uc2 1,581 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par 22:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 A photograph published in a previous version of this article misidentified an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporter. The photo has been removed. (Corrected on June 24.)\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated the constitutional right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , overruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision }}}\uc2  and leaving the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 's legality to the states.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization-6-24-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court's decision }}}\uc2  upheld {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a law from Mississippi }}}\uc2  that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy, roughly two months earlier than what has been allowed under Supreme Court precedent dating back to Roe.\par \par \uc2 In doing so, the court's conservative majority said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/leaked-draft-of-supreme-court-opinion-indicates-roe-v-wade-may-be-overturned-11651554510"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Roe decision was egregiously wrong }}}\uc2  in recognizing a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an error the court perpetuated in the decades since.\par \par \uc2 "The Constitution makes no reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and no such right is implicitly protected by any constitutional provision," Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  wrote for the court.\par \par \uc2 "It is time to heed the Constitution and return the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the people's elected representatives," he wrote in his opinion in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization.\par \par \uc2 Latest Updates\par \par \uc2 Get the latest updates on the overturning of Roe at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WSJ's Live Blog }}}\par \par \uc2 Read the decision: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization-6-24-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization }}}\par \par \uc2 The ruling, one of the most consequential in modern memory, marked a rare instance in which the court reversed itself to eliminate a constitutional right that it had previously recognized.\par \par \uc2 The court voted 6-3 to side with Mississippi, but 5-4 on the broader question of whether to overrule Roe.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/key-excerpts-from-supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-overturning-roe-v-wade-11656092052?mod=livecoverage_web"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 majority's decision }}}\uc2  in Roe was grounded in its view that in 1868, when the 14th Amendment was adopted, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was widely restricted throughout the U.S. Therefore, Justice Alito wrote, the right to end an unwanted pregnancy couldn't be derived from the amendment's provisions protecting individual liberty and equality from infringement by state governments.\par \par \uc2 "A right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not deeply rooted in the Nation's history and traditions. On the contrary, an unbroken tradition of prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on pain of criminal punishment persisted from the earliest days of the common law until 1973," when Roe was decided, Justice Alito wrote.\par \par \uc2 "In interpreting what is meant by the 14th Amendment's reference to 'liberty,' we must guard against the natural human tendency to confuse what that Amendment protects with our own ardent views about the liberty that Americans should enjoy," he said.\par \par \uc2 The court rejected arguments that respect for precedent, a legal principle called stare decisis, should protect Roe from reconsideration a half-century after it was argued.\par \par \uc2 Where \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Is Legal and Where It Loses Protections Without Roe v. Wade\par \par \uc2 Justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett joined the Alito opinion. Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , in a concurring opinion, agreed that the Mississippi law should stand, but didn't support rescinding the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  altogether.\par \par \uc2 "Both the Court's opinion and the dissent display a relentless freedom from doubt on the legal issue that I cannot share," the chief justice wrote. Allowing states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability without deciding whether to overrule Roe was a more prudent and responsible course, he argued.\par \par \uc2 The court's decision to overrule Roe and a 1992 case reaffirming \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Chief Justice Roberts wrote, "is a serious jolt to the legal system\u8212\'20\'14regardless of how you view those cases. A narrower decision rejecting the misguided viability line would be markedly less unsettling, and nothing more is needed to decide this case."\par \par \uc2 The court's three liberals, signaling profound disagreement, jointly authored a dissent. They accused the majority of discarding the balance precedents struck between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a woman's interest }}}\uc2  and that of the state in protecting "potential life."\par \par \uc2 "Today, the Court discards that balance. It says that from the very moment of fertilization, a woman has no rights to speak of," Justices \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and Elena Kagan wrote. "After today, young women will come of age with fewer rights than their mothers and grandmothers had."\par \par \uc2 President Biden, speaking from the White House, said the ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/video/watch-biden-addresses-supreme-court-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/6D518197-5337-48D0-944B-C2C3BAA0582A.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marked a "sad day for the court and the country." }}}\par \par \uc2 "This decision is a culmination of a deliberate effort over decades to upset the balance of our law," Mr. Biden said. "It's a realization of an extreme ideology and a tragic error by the Supreme Court in my view."\par \par \uc2 The president said the decision's rationale put in question precedents affirming other rights related to personal privacy that stemmed from the same legal theories that led to Roe. Those rights ranged from access to contraception, which the court recognized in 1965, to same-sex marriage, afforded under a 2015 decision.\par \par \uc2 In that he had agreement from Justice Thomas, who wrote separately to urge his colleagues to overrule such precedents "at the earliest opportunity." Those cases rely in part on 14th Amendment provisions that protect individual liberty from state interference without due process. Justice Thomas wrote that the court erred by relying on the due-process clause as a source of specific rights.\par \par \uc2 While Justice Alito's opinion, along with a concurrence from Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , discounted such concerns, the dissenters saw Justice Thomas as more candid.\par \par \uc2 "According to the majority, no liberty interest is present\u8212\'20\'14 because (and only because) the law offered no protection to the woman's choice in the 19th century," they wrote. "But here is the rub. The law also did not then (and would not for ages) protect a wealth of other things," they wrote, including the right "to marry across racial lines," "to not be sterilized without consent," "to contraceptive use," to "same-sex intimacy and marriage."\par \par \uc2 "If the majority is right in its legal analysis, all those decisions were wrong," they wrote. It was no surprise that the Constitution was blind to reproduction, they wrote. "The 'people' did not ratify the 14th Amendment. Men did."\par \par \uc2 Although the case before the court involved a 15-week ban, the overruling of Roe gives states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-decision-sparks-immediate-action-from-states-11656096002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broad latitude to regulate or prohibit \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  as they see fit. Many conservative-leaning states are poised to tighten access further, while some liberal ones have established permissive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimes under state law. The decision could become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-decision-sparks-immediate-action-from-states-11656096002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a major issue in this year's elections }}}\uc2 , as state and federal lawmakers look to position themselves in a post-Roe world.\par \par \uc2 Almost half the states have laws in place or at the ready to curtail or outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while others have laws that would preserve its legality. Questions on whether and how to limit abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are expected to continue roiling state legislative debates }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision is a defining moment for a Supreme Court that is more conservative than it has been in many decades, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-trump-pick-amy-coney-barrett-could-mean-for-future-of-the-supreme-court-11601155192"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a shift in legal thinking }}}\uc2  made possible after President \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/trump-says-it-was-great-honor-to-appoint-justices-who-voted-to-overturn-roe-bG8IoHon8J4NePvvnKQc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 placed three justices on the court }}}\uc2 . Two of them succeeded justices who voted to affirm \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In anticipation of the ruling, several states have passed laws limiting or banning the procedure, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-state-abortion-laws-stand-if-roe-v-wade-is-overturned-11651614828"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 states have so-called trigger laws }}}\uc2  on their books that called for prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe were overruled. Clinics in conservative states have been preparing for possible closure, while facilities in more liberal areas have been getting ready for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/illinois-abortion-clinics-are-preparing-for-a-potential-post-roe-world-11638419374"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a potentially heavy influx of patients }}}\uc2  from other states.\par \par \uc2 The ruling follows a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-confirms-authenticity-of-leaked-draft-opinion-overruling-roe-v-wade-11651592725"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highly unusual leak last month }}}\uc2  of an early draft opinion in the case that suggested the court was preparing to overrule Roe and withdraw federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Justice Alito's majority decision was very similar to the leaked draft version, with some changes to address arguments raised in the dissenting and concurring opinions.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hunt-for-who-leaked-draft-roe-v-wade-opinion-has-no-road-map-11651748254"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been investigating the leak }}}\uc2  at a time of strained relationships among members of the court. Justice Thomas in a recent speech suggested {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/clarence-thomas-criticizes-supreme-court-leak-of-draft-opinion-on-roe-v-wade-11652508439"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trust among members of the court had been lost }}}\uc2 . And when the court heard oral arguments in the Dobbs case in December, Justice Sotomayor questioned whether the court could "survive the stench" created by perceptions "that the Constitution and its reading are just political acts."\par \par \uc2 The court's Roe decision in 1973, written by Nixon appointee Justice Harry Blackmun, reflected a line of legal thinking that the Constitution barred political majorities from imposing their moral judgments on the intimate choices of individuals. The Roe court grounded the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the 14th Amendment's guarantee that states can't deprive individuals of life and liberty without due process of law. The ruling built off a constitutionally recognized right to privacy, which came when the court struck down state restrictions on contraceptives.\par \par \uc2 The court does on occasion overrule its past decisions\u8212\'20\'14notably, for instance in the 1954 Brown v. Board of Education decision that ended racial segregation in public schools\u8212\'20\'14but justices for years have dueled over when it is appropriate to do so. Most of those debates have taken place in cases that had nothing to do with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the future of Roe has loomed over the discussions.\par \par \uc2 Jan Wolfe contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Brent Kendall at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brent.kendall@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brent.kendall@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jess.bravin+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jess.bravin+1@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court Overturns Roe v. Wade, Eliminates Constitutional Right to \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220624ei6o002jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
