\par \par \uc2 The waiting room at the Tulsa Women's Clinic in Oklahoma earlier in June. PHOTO: Michael Noble Jr. for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 "There's a pit in my stomach, and I'm just so worried about what this means for average people out there who don't expect themselves to be in a position where they may really, for their own well being, be pursuing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Dr. Monnig said in a call after the court's decision Friday.\par \par \uc2 Texas, Oklahoma and Kentucky in recent months all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-lawmakers-pass-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11652984908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have passed \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws }}}\uc2  either temporarily or permanently suspending access to most abortions, providing a preview of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-barrier-abortion-roe-v-wade-11654170644"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what life could look like }}}\uc2  in some two dozen states post-Roe.\par \par \uc2 Andrea Gallegos, an executive administrator at a clinic in Oklahoma and one in San Antonio, said her Tulsa clinic saw the number of patients triple last year after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-in-court-what-you-need-to-know-11631730720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas's law took effect }}}\uc2 . Lawmakers in Oklahoma then took Texas' law a step further, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oklahoma-lawmakers-pass-near-total-ban-on-abortion-11652984908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning abortions at any stage }}}\uc2  of pregnancy with exceptions for a medical emergency or if the pregnancy is the result of rape, sexual assault or incest that has been reported to law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 After the laws took effect in May, Ms. Gallegos has called patients days or sometimes hours before their scheduled abortions to let them know they can no longer provide them. One patient was already en route from Texas and had to turn around, while another had a panic attack, Ms. Gallegos said.\par \par \uc2 "We're going to be forcing more and more women to remain pregnant," Ms. Gallegos said. Tulsa Women's Clinic, which primarily provided abortions, still offers sonograms and now tries to help refer patients to clinics in other states. The clinic's future is now unclear. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
