\par \par \uc2 A mobile clinic in Fairview Heights, Ill. PHOTO: Neeta Satam for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Dr. Marchin said Planned Parenthood has been preparing for the surge by enhancing services for patients traveling from out-of-state and making it easier for patients to use telehealth appointments.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., Planned Parenthood, which offers telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in several states, and telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers like Just the Pill, Hey Jane and Choix, said they are expecting an influx of patients. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  via telemedicine involves a consultation with a healthcare provider, who can prescribe mifepristone and misoprostol, the two drugs that are typically used in a medication-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen. Depending on the provider, the patient can choose to pick up the medication from a clinic or it can be mailed directly to the patient.\par \par \uc2 Women in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned will need to leave their state for the telehealth consultation with a U.S. provider and to pick up their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. Some telemedicine-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers offer delivery to P.O. boxes or courier drop boxes, as well as follow-up medical support.\par \par \uc2 Patients for whom this isn't an option might rely on online vendors to source mifepristone and misoprostol without a doctor's prescription, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates say. There are dozens of such vendors online, though their provenance and reliability are mostly unknown.\par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration said the sale of unapproved \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication bypasses important safeguards designed to protect patients' health. Nisha Verma, a fellow at the \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 , said most women are able to safely and effectively manage their abortions using mifepristone and misoprostol when these medications are acquired from reliable sources, even without doctor supervision. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
