\par \par \uc2 The embryology lab at Boston IVF's fertility center in Waltham, Mass. PHOTO: Kayana Szymczak for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration said it would continue to defend the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 use of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills }}}\uc2  to carry out the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said Friday after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/attorney-general-lays-out-justice-department-s-red-lines-after-ruling-qjmSR90s3Zzb88oidJ7j"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that states couldn't ban mifepristone }}}\uc2 , a medication used to induce abortions. \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  Secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  said he would work to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-providers-prepare-to-reach-patients-in-restrictive-states-11652439601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maintain access to the medication }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I have directed every part of my Department to do any and everything we can here," he said.\par \par \uc2 The field of reproductive medicine also has come of age under the umbrella of Roe, and legal experts say overturning it could have unintended consequences for in-vitro fertilization and contraception. Fertility clinics across the country say they have contingency plans in place, including limiting services and finding potential workarounds in states that might pass \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws that could affect IVF.\par \par \uc2 Losing or discarding an embryo in an IVF setting could be criminalized by statutes that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the moment of fertilization or that grant personhood rights to embryos, said Barbara Collura, CEO and president of \uc2 Resolve: The National Infertility Association\uc2 , a patient-advocacy nonprofit.\par \par \uc2 "We always had the backstop of Roe v. Wade and now we won't have that," said Ms. Collura.\par \par \uc2 Liz Whyte contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Deanna Paul at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:deanna.paul@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deanna.paul@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fall-of-roe-v-wade-upends-abortion-landscape-for-american-women-11656081225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fall of Roe v. Wade Upends \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Landscape for American Women }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220624ei6o00335\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
