\par\par \uc2 Best of the Web Today\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Another Tough Day for the Left; Progressives had to choose this of all weeks to restart their argument over what a woman is.\b0\par\par\uc2 By James Freeman \par \uc2 1,079 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par 22:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 In their more candid moments even leftist luminaries like the late Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  admitted significant flaws in Roe v. Wade. But now that the Supreme Court has returned the contentious issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the people and their elected representatives, Roe's flaws don't make it any easier for some activists to accept that each state will now be free to set its own policies.\par \par \uc2 It's understandable to be deeply disappointed and even sad when your side loses an important case. What is unacceptable is for the attorney general of the United States to forget his duty to enforce the law and instead to express publicly his contempt for it. The Supreme Court has ruled today and \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  has issued a press release in opposition to the ruling as if he is a political candidate running a campaign against the justices. In a release from the Department of Justice Mr. Garland {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/attorney-general-merrick-b-garland-statement-supreme-court-ruling-dobbs-v-jackson-women-s#:~:text=���The ability to decide one's,to control one's own body."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 "Today, the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade and Planned Parenthood v. Casey and held that the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer protected by the Constitution.\par \par \uc2 "The Supreme Court has eliminated an established right that has been an essential component of women's liberty for half a century \u8211\'20\'13 a right that has safeguarded women's ability to participate fully and equally in society. And in renouncing this fundamental right, which it had repeatedly recognized and reaffirmed, the Court has upended the doctrine of stare decisis, a key pillar of the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 "The Justice Department strongly disagrees with the Court's decision. This decision deals a devastating blow to reproductive freedom in the United States. It will have an immediate and irreversible impact on the lives of people across the country. And it will be greatly disproportionate in its effect \u8211\'20\'13 with the greatest burdens felt by people of color and those of limited financial means.\par \par \uc2 One can make substantive arguments against the attorney general's various claims but even if one shares his politics, issuing such screeds and seeking to undermine the authority of the court should be anathema to any responsible law-enforcement officer.\par \par \uc2 It's critical that Mr. Garland regains his composure and focuses on his job. As Kyle Mann of the satirical website Babylon Bee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/The_Kyle_Mann/status/1540343550155534336?s=20&t=ZDRkR8pP4cPBEp2Ki8pOag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notes}}}\uc2  with graveyard humor, there could be a violent reaction to today's ruling from extremists:\par \par \uc2 Authorities are warning tonight's protests may escalate from "mostly peaceful" to "somewhat peaceful"\par \par \uc2 Those protesting the ruling have a particular challenge in that there is now some disagreement among themselves about what exactly they are advocating and for whom. The left has been engaged in a confusing internal debate about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/judge-jackson-and-the-biology-of-gender-11648069148"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what a woman is}}}\uc2 . This week the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights organization \uc2 NARAL Pro-Choice America\uc2  didn't necessarily help clarify things by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NARAL/status/1539322351262871552?s=20&t=GdMlObBKYHQ1EHT2nhN6MQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeting}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 If your feminism doesn't include trans women and girls, it's not feminism\par \par \uc2 If your feminism doesn't understand how anti-trans policies disproportionately impact BIPOC folks, particularly Black trans women and girls, it's not feminism\par \par \uc2 The tweet also included emojis for emphasis. Of course before assessing the impact of today's ruling on BIPOC folks it's important to know what BIPOC means. A 2020 Vox story carried the headline "Why the term 'BIPOC' is so complicated, explained by linguists," and now includes this note at the bottom of the article:\par \par \uc2 Correction: An earlier version of this article defined BIPOC as standing for "Black and Indigenous people of color." It stands for Black, Indigenous, people of color.\par \par \uc2 Now comes an email from Lisa Burkert of the public-relations firm The TASC Group relaying a statement on today's ruling from Sean Ebony Coleman, founder and executive director of LGBTQ center Destination Tomorrow:\par \par \uc2 "We need to highlight the fact that this Supreme Court decision will impact anyone with a uterus, whether or not they are female identified. Poor Black and brown LBT people in rural areas will suffer the most. \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  are human rights, and no one should be forgotten in this fight, especially trans masculine folks. The fact that this is happening during Pride month should also not be lost on us \u8211\'20\'13 at a time when we are celebrating freedom, our freedoms are being challenged and taken away. This is our call to action. All those who are not cis, white males are in danger. Those in the margins must come forward, band together and fight."\par \par \uc2 As this column {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/working-with-wokesters-11655935034"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted earlier in the week}}}\uc2 , efforts among progressive leftists to band together have lately been especially challenging. And today's issue seems to be getting more and more complex. Perhaps state legislators can figure out which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws make sense for the individuals in their particular jurisdictions. Experienced legislators tend to have the ability to understand how the wants and needs of their constituents change over time, and also have an instinct for positioning themselves for future electoral success.\par \par \uc2 Take for example, the experienced legislator who became our president in 2021. Way back in 1986 the Journal's Al Hunt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wsj.com/public/resources/documents/19860407hunt.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  about Sen. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (D., Del.):\par \par \uc2 He says he opposes efforts to limit a woman's right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but also opposes federal funds to finance abortions. Yet he did vote in the Judiciary Committee for one anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  constitutional amendment, and has fudged a few times on funding measures -- earning the enmity of both sides.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  moans a lot and then usually votes against us," says Jeannie Rosoff, a top official of the pro-choice Planned Parenthood. "It's very difficult to know whether this issue is purely personal, purely political or a combination of both with him." Meanwhile, Douglas Johnson of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  National Right to Life organization complains: "It appears to us that in recent years Sen. Biden has made a political judgment that he should be more pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 One can never precisely predict the evolution of politicians or voters' preferences. But perhaps in another 36 years Mr. Biden will be a Roe opponent again.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 James Freeman is the co-author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1982163984"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "The Cost: Trump, China and American Revival."}}}\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Follow James Freeman on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FreemanWSJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/newsletters?sub=157"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Subscribe to the Best of the Web email.}}}\par \par \uc2 To suggest items, please email best@wsj.com.\par \par \uc2 (Lisa Rossi helps compile Best of the Web.)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/another-tough-day-for-the-left-11656109057"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Another Tough Day for the Left}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220624ei6o007k9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
